		tags = { "Mammals", "Rodents" },
		aliases = { "Gliridae", "Myoxidae", "Muscardinidae" },
		summary = "A **dormouse** is a [[Rodent|rodent]] of the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] **Gliridae** (this family is also variously called **Myoxidae** or **Muscardinidae** by different taxonomists). Dormice are nocturnal animals found in Africa, Asia, and Europe. They are named for their long dormant [[Hibernation|hibernation]] period of six months or longer. There are nine genera and 28 living species of dormice, with half of living species belonging to the African genus Graphiurus.",
		infobox = {
