		tags = { "Mammals", "Carnivora" },
		summary = "A **lynx** is any of the four extant [[Species|species]] (the Canada lynx, Iberian lynx, Eurasian lynx and the bobcat) within the medium-sized wild [[Felidae|cat]] [[Genus|genus]] **Lynx**. The name originated in [[Middle English]] via Latin from the Greek word lynx, derived from the Indo-European root leuk- (light, brightness), in reference to the luminescence of its reflective eyes.",
