		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Genus of birds",
		tags = { "Birds", "Corvoidea" },
		aliases = { "Menura", "Menuridae" },
		summary = "A **lyrebird** is either of two [[Species|species]] of ground-dwelling Australian birds that compose the genus **Menura**, and the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] **Menuridae**. They are most notable for their ability to [[Mimicry|mimic]] a variety of natural and artificial sounds from their environment and for the striking beauty of the male bird's huge tail when it is fanned out in courtship display. Lyrebirds have unique plumes of neutral-coloured tailfeathers and are among Australia's best-known native birds.",
