		description = "Family of spiders",
		tags = { "Arthropods", "Arachnids" },
		aliases = { "Tarantulas", "Theraphosidae" },
		summary = '**Tarantulas** are a group of large and often hairy [[Spider|spiders]] of the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] **Theraphosidae**. More than a thousand [[Species|species]] have been identified, within almost 200 [[Genus|genera]]. The term "tarantula" is usually used to describe members of the family Theraphosidae, although many other members of the same infraorder (Mygalomorphae) are commonly referred to as "tarantulas" or "false tarantulas". Some of the more common species have become popular in the exotic pet trade. Many [[New World]] species kept as pets have setae known as urticating hairs that can cause irritation to the skin, and in extreme cases, cause damage to the [[Human eye|eyes]].',
		infobox = {
			{ "Scientific name", "Theraphosidae" },
