		tags = { "Insects and other hexapods", "Orthoptera" },
		aliases = { "Katydids", "Bush crickets" },
		summary = '[[Insect|Insects]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] **Tettigoniidae** are commonly called **katydids** (especially in North America) or **bush crickets**. They have previously been known as "long-horned [[Grasshopper|grasshoppers]]". More than 8,000 [[Species|species]] are known. Part of the suborder Ensifera, the Tettigoniidae are the only [[Neontology|extant]] family in the superfamily Tettigonioidea.',
