		description = "Family of birds",
		tags = { "Birds", "Passerida" },
		aliases = { "Thrushes", "Turdidae" },
		summary = "The **thrushes** are a [[Passerine|passerine]] [[Bird|bird]] [[Family (taxonomy)|family]], **Turdidae**, with a worldwide distribution. The family was once much larger before biologists reclassified the former subfamily Saxicolinae, which includes the chats and [[European robin|European robins]], as [[Old World flycatcher|Old World flycatchers]]. Thrushes are small to medium-sized ground living birds that feed on insects, other invertebrates, and fruit. Some unrelated species around the world have been named after thrushes due to their similarity to birds in this family.",
