	{
		title = "The Thinker",
		category = "Art",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🗿",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Sculpture by Auguste Rodin",
		tags = { "Specific works", "Sculpture" },
		summary = 'This universally recognized expression of "deep thought" has made the sculpture one of the most widely known artworks in the world. It has become the iconic symbol of thinking; images of the sculpture in profile are often used to indicate [[Philosophy|philosophy]] and other practices of contemplation or [[Introspection|introspection]].',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"There are 27 other known full-sized bronze castings of the figure, approximately 185 cm tall, though not all were made under Rodin's supervision. Various other versions, several in plaster, as well as studies and dozens of posthumous castings, exist in a range of sizes.",
