		summary = "[[William Shakespeare]] (c. 23 April 1564 – 23 April 1616) wrote [[Sonnet|sonnets]] on a variety of themes. When discussing or referring to **Shakespeare's sonnets**, it is almost always a reference to the 154 sonnets that were first published all together in a quarto in 1609. However, there are six additional sonnets that Shakespeare wrote and included in the plays [[Romeo and Juliet]], Henry V and Love's Labour's Lost. There is also a partial sonnet found in the play Edward III.",
