		fame = 3,
		emoji = "📚",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "none",
		tags = { "Literature", "Literatures by language and area" },
		summary = "**Spanish literature** is literature (Spanish poetry, [[Prose|prose]], and drama) written in the [[Spanish language]] within the territory that presently constitutes the Kingdom of [[Spain]]. Its development coincides and frequently intersects with that of other literary traditions from regions within the same territory, particularly Catalan literature, Galician intersects as well with Latin, Jewish, and Arabic literary traditions of the [[Iberian Peninsula]]. The literature of [[Spanish America]] is an important branch of Spanish literature, with its own particular characteristics dating back to the earliest years of Spain’s conquest of the Americas (see [[Latin American literature]]).",
