		tags = { "Africa", "Central Africa" },
		summary = '**Bangui** is the [[Capital city|capital]] and largest city of the [[Central African Republic]]. It was established as a French outpost in 1889 and named after its location on the northern bank of the [[Ubangi River]]; the Ubangi itself was named from the Bobangi word for the "rapids" located beside the settlement, which marked the end of navigable water north from [[Brazzaville]]. The majority of the population of the Central African Republic lives in the western parts of the country, in Bangui and the surrounding area.',
