		summary = "**Beirut** is the [[Capital city|capital]] and largest city of [[Lebanon]]. As of 2025, Greater Beirut has a population of 2.4 million, just under half of Lebanon's population, which makes it the twelfth-largest city in the [[Levant]] region and the sixteenth-largest in the [[Arab world]]. The city is situated on a peninsula at the midpoint of Lebanon's [[Mediterranean Sea|Mediterranean]] coast. Beirut has been inhabited for more than 5,000 years, making it one of the oldest cities in the world.",
