			{ "Area", "24758 km²" },
			{ "Elevation", "222 m" },
			{ "Population", "9,066,906" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Changsha",
		category = "City",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🏙️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Capital of Hunan, Central China",
		tags = { "Eastern Asia", "China" },
		summary = "**Changsha** is the capital of [[Hunan]], China. Located in the lower reaches of the Xiang River in northeastern Hunan, it is the 15th most populous city in China with a population of 10,513,100.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'The city forms a part of the Greater Changsha Metropolitan Region along with Zhuzhou and Xiangtan, also known as the Changzhutan City Cluster. Greater Changsha was named one of the 13 emerging mega-cities in China in 2012 by the [[Economist Intelligence Unit]]. It is also a National Comprehensive Transportation Hub, and one of the first National Famous Historical and Cultural Cities in China. Changshanese, a kind of Xiang Chinese, is spoken in the downtown area, while Ningxiangnese and Liuyangnese are also spoken in the counties and cities under its jurisdiction. As of the 2020 Chinese census, the [[Prefecture-level city|prefecture-level city]] of Changsha had a population of 10,047,914 inhabitants. Changsha has a history of more than 2,400 years of urban construction, and the name "Changsha" first appeared in the Yi Zhou Shu written in the pre-Qin era.',
			},
