		summary = "**Damietta** is a port city which serves as the capital city of the Damietta Governorate in [[Egypt]]. It is located at the Damietta branch, an eastern distributary of the [[Nile Delta]], 15 km from the [[Mediterranean Sea]], and about 200 km north of [[Cairo]]. The city was a Catholic bishopric and is a multiple titular see. Damietta is also a member of the [[UNESCO|UNESCO Global Network]] of Learning Cities, having joined in 2019.",
