		description = "Metropolitan city in Sindh",
		tags = { "Southern Asia", "Pakistan" },
		aliases = { "Neroonkot" },
		summary = "**Hyderabad**, also known as **Neroonkot**, is the capital and largest city of the Hyderabad Division in the [[Sindh]] province of Pakistan. It is the second-largest city in Sindh, after [[Karachi]], and the 7th largest in Pakistan.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Founded in 1768 by Mian Ghulam Shah Kalhoro of the Kalhora Dynasty, Hyderabad served as a provincial capital until the British transferred the capital to Bombay Presidency in 1840. It is about 150 km inland of [[Karachi]], the largest city of Pakistan, to which it is connected by a direct railway and M-9 motorway.",
			},
