	{
		title = "Lusaka",
		category = "City",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🏙️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Capital and largest city of Zambia",
		tags = { "Africa", "Eastern Africa" },
		summary = "**Lusaka** is the [[Capital city|capital]] and largest city of [[Zambia]]. It is one of the fastest-developing cities in [[Southern Africa|southern Africa]]. Lusaka is in the southern part of the central plateau at an elevation of about 1279 m. As of 2022, the city's population was approximately 2,204,059. Lusaka is the centre of both commerce and government in Zambia and connects to the country's four main highways heading north, south, east, and west. English is the official language of the city administration, while Bemba, Tonga and Chichewa are the commonly spoken street languages.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The earliest evidence of settlement in the area dates to the 6th century AD, with the first known settlement in the 11th century. It was then home to the Lenje and Soli peoples from the 17th or 18th century. The founding of the modern city occurred in 1905 when it lay in the [[British protectorate]] of Northern Rhodesia, which was controlled by the British South African Company (BSAC). The BSAC built a railway linking their mines in the Copperbelt to [[Cape Town]] and Lusaka was designated as a water stop on that line, named after a local Lenje chief called Lusaaka. White Afrikaner farmers then settled in the area and expanded Lusaka into a regional trading centre, taking over its administration.",
