		description = "Dense urban core together with its satellite cities",
		tags = { "Cities", "Urban studies and planning" },
		aliases = { "Metro" },
		summary = "A **metropolitan area** or **metro** is a region consisting of a densely populated [[Urban area|urban agglomeration]] and its surrounding territories; which share [[Industry (economics)|industries]], commercial areas, transport network, [[Infrastructure|infrastructure]] and housing. A metropolitan area usually comprises multiple principal cities, [[Jurisdiction|jurisdictions]] and [[Municipality|municipalities]]: [[Neighbourhood|neighborhoods]], townships, boroughs, [[City|cities]], [[Town|towns]], exurbs, [[Suburb|suburbs]], counties, districts and even [[State (polity)|states]] and [[Nation|nations]] in areas like the eurodistricts. As social, economic and political institutions have changed, metropolitan areas have become key economic and political regions.",
