		description = "Ancient city in Iran",
		tags = { "Historical cities", "Asia" },
		summary = "**Susa** was an ancient city in the lower [[Zagros Mountains]] about 250 km east of the [[Tigris]], between the Karkheh and Dez Rivers in [[Iran]]. It represents the current city of Shush, located on the site of ancient Susa. One of the most important cities of the [[Ancient Near East]], Susa served as the capital of [[Elam]] and the winter capital of the [[Achaemenid Empire]], and remained a strategic centre during the [[Parthian Empire|Parthian]] and [[Sasanian Empire|Sasanian]] periods.",
