		summary = 'The **Adivasi** (also spelled **Adibasi**) are the heterogeneous tribal groups across the [[Indian subcontinent]]. The term Adivasi, a 20th-century construct meaning "ancient inhabitants", is now widely used as a self-designation by many of the communities who are officially recognised as "Scheduled Tribes" in India and as "Ethnic minorities" in Bangladesh. They constitute approximately 8.6% of India\'s population (around 104.2 million, according to the 2011 Census) and about 1.1% of Bangladesh\'s population (roughly 2 million, 2010 estimate).',
