		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Afroeurasia", "Eurafrasia" },
		summary = '**Afro-Eurasia** (also known as **Afroeurasia**, and **Eurafrasia**) is a landmass, occasionally described as a [[Supercontinent|supercontinent]], comprising the [[Continent|continents]] of [[Africa]], [[Asia]], and [[Europe]]. The terms are compound words of the names of its constituent parts. Afro-Eurasia has also been called the "[[Old World]]", in contrast to the "[[New World]]" referring to the [[Americas]] plus sometimes [[Oceania]] and [[Antarctica]].',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Afro-Eurasia encompasses 85,135,000 km², 57% of the world's land area, and has a population of approximately 6.7 billion people, roughly 86% of the [[World population|world population]]. Together with [[Mainland Australia|mainland Australia]], they comprise the vast majority of the land in the world's [[Eastern Hemisphere]]. The Afro-Eurasian mainland is the largest and most populous contiguous landmass on [[Earth]].",
			},
