		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Arab culture** is the culture of the [[Arabs]], from the [[Atlantic Ocean]] in the west to the [[Arabian Sea]] in the east, in a region of the [[Middle East and North Africa]] known as the [[Arab world]]. The various religions the Arabs have adopted throughout their history and the various empires and kingdoms that have ruled and took lead of the civilization have contributed to the ethnogenesis and formation of modern Arab culture. [[Arabic|Language]], [[Arabic literature|literature]], gastronomy, art, architecture, [[Arabic music|music]], [[Spirituality|spirituality]], [[Islamic philosophy|philosophy]], and mysticism are all part of the cultural heritage of the Arabs.",
