		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Arabic abjad" },
		summary = "The **Arabic alphabet**, or the **Arabic abjad**, is the [[Arabic script]] as specifically codified for writing the [[Arabic]] language. It is a unicameral script written from right-to-left in a cursive style, and includes 28 letters, of which most have contextual forms. The Arabic alphabet is an [[Abjad|abjad]], meaning that the letters only record consonants; due to its optional use of diacritics to notate vowels, it is considered an impure abjad.",
