		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Basso continuo** is a harmonic musical structure, almost universal in the [[Baroque music|Baroque]] era (1600–1750), that generally consisted of a bassline and a chord progression. The phrase is often shortened to **continuo**, and the instrumentalists playing the continuo part are called the continuo group.",
