		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Capitol Records, LLC", "Capitol Records, Inc.", "Capitol" },
		summary = "**Capitol Records, LLC** (known legally as **Capitol Records, Inc.** until 2007 and simply referred to as **Capitol**) is an American record label owned by [[Universal Music Group]] (UMG) through its Capitol Music Group imprint. It was founded as the first West Coast-based record label of note in the United States in 1942 by Johnny Mercer, Buddy DeSylva, and Glenn E. Wallichs. Capitol was acquired by British music conglomerate [[EMI]] as its North American [[Subsidiary|subsidiary]] in 1955. EMI was acquired by Universal Music Group in 2012 and underwent a merger with the company a year later, making Capitol and the Capitol Music Group both distributed by UMG.",
