		summary = "**Class discrimination**, also known as **classism**, is [[Prejudice|prejudice]] or [[Discrimination|discrimination]] on the basis of [[Social class|social class]]. It includes individual attitudes, behaviors, systems of policies and practices that are set up to benefit the [[Upper class|upper class]] at the expense of the lower class. Social class refers to the grouping of individuals in a hierarchy based on wealth, income, education, occupation, and social network.",
