		emoji = "🗣️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "none",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Classical languages" },
		summary = "The Indian **classical languages** are the [[Languages of India|languages of India]] perceived as having high antiquity, and valuable, original and distinct [[Indian literature|literary heritage]]. The [[Government of India]] declared in 2004 that languages meeting strict criteria could be accorded the status of a classical language of India. It was instituted by the Ministry of Culture along with the Linguistic Experts' Committee. The committee was constituted by the Government of India to consider demands for the categorisation of languages as classical languages. In 2004, [[Tamil language|Tamil]] became the first language to be recognised as a classical language of India. As of 2024, 11 languages have been recognised as classical languages of India.",
