		summary = "**Computer engineering** (**CE**, **CoE**, **CpE**, or **CompE**) is a branch of [[Engineering|engineering]] specialized in developing [[Computer hardware|computer hardware]] and software. It integrates several fields of [[Electrical engineering|electrical engineering]], electronics engineering and [[Computer science|computer science]]. Computer engineering may be referred to as Electrical and Computer Engineering or Computer Science and Engineering at some universities.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Computer engineers require training in hardware-software integration, software design, and [[Software engineering|software engineering]]. It can encompass areas such as [[Electromagnetism|electromagnetism]], [[Artificial intelligence|artificial intelligence (AI)]], [[Robot|robotics]], [[Computer network|computer networks]], [[Computer architecture|computer architecture]] and [[Operating system|operating systems]]. Computer engineers are involved in many hardware and software aspects of [[Computing|computing]], from the design of individual microcontrollers, [[Microprocessor|microprocessors]], [[Personal computer|personal computers]], and [[Supercomputer|supercomputers]], to [[Circuit design|circuit design]]. This field of engineering not only focuses on how computer systems themselves work, but also on how to integrate them into the larger picture.",
