		tags = { "Psychology", "Interpersonal relations" },
		aliases = { "Co-operation" },
		summary = '**Cooperation** (now much less often written as **co-operation** in [[British English]] and very rarely "coöperation" in [[American English]]) takes place when a group of organisms works or acts together for a collective benefit to the group as opposed to working in [[Competition|competition]] for selfish individual benefit. In [[Biology|biology]], many [[Animal|animal]] and [[Plant|plant]] [[Species|species]] cooperate both with other members of their own species and with members of other species with whom they have (symbiotic or [[Mutualism (biology)|mutualistic]]) relationships.',
