		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Cylinder (geometry)" },
		summary = "A **cylinder** has traditionally been a three-dimensional solid, one of the most basic of curvilinear geometric [[Shape|shapes]]. In elementary geometry, it is considered a prism with a [[Circle|circle]] as its base.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'A cylinder may also be defined as an infinite curvilinear [[Surface (mathematics)|surface]] in various modern branches of geometry and [[Topology|topology]]. The shift in the basic meaning—solid versus surface (as in a solid ball versus [[Sphere|sphere]] surface)—has created some ambiguity with terminology. The two concepts may be distinguished by referring to **solid cylinders** and **cylindrical surfaces**. In the literature the unadorned term "cylinder" could refer to either of these or to an even more specialized object, the right circular cylinder.',
