		tags = { "Business and economics", "Banking and finance" },
		summary = "**Debt** is an obligation that requires one party, the debtor, to pay [[Money|money]] [[Loan|borrowed]] or otherwise withheld from another party, the creditor. Debt may be owed by a [[Sovereign state|sovereign state]] or country, [[Local government|local government]], [[Company|company]], or an individual. Commercial debt is generally subject to contractual terms regarding the amount and timing of repayments of principal and [[Interest|interest]]. [[Loan|Loans]], bonds, notes, and mortgages are all types of debt.",
