	{
		title = "Disgust",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "😊",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Basic emotion",
		tags = { "Psychology", "Emotions and traits" },
		summary = "**Disgust** is an [[Emotion|emotional]] response of rejection or revulsion to something potentially contagious or something considered offensive, distasteful or unpleasant. In The Expression of the Emotions in Man and Animals, [[Charles Darwin]] wrote that disgust is a sensation that refers to something revolting. Disgust is experienced primarily in relation to the [[Sense|sense]] of [[Taste|taste]] (either perceived or imagined), and secondarily to anything which causes a similar feeling by sense of smell, touch, or [[Visual perception|vision]]. Musically sensitive people may even be disgusted by the cacophony of inharmonious sounds.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Disgust is one of the basic emotions of Robert Plutchik's theory of emotions, and has been studied extensively by Paul Rozin. It invokes a characteristic facial expression, one of Paul Ekman's six universal facial expressions of emotion. Unlike the emotions of [[Fear|fear]], [[Anger|anger]], and [[Sadness|sadness]], disgust is associated with a decrease in heart rate (for body-envelope violations) and proto-nausea of the stomach (for bodily effluvia).",
			},
		},
		related = { "Self-esteem" },
	},
	{
		title = "Disneyland",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🌳",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Theme park in Anaheim, California, US",
		tags = { "Entertainment", "Recreation and tourism" },
		summary = "**Disneyland** is a [[Amusement park|theme park]] at the Disneyland Resort in Anaheim, California, United States. It was the first theme park opened by [[The Walt Disney Company|the Walt Disney Company]] and the only one designed and constructed under the direct supervision of [[Walt Disney]], opening on July 17, 1955.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Disney initially envisioned building a tourist attraction adjacent to his studios in Burbank to entertain fans who wished to visit; however, he soon realized that the proposed site was too small for the ideas that he had. After hiring the Stanford Research Institute to perform a feasibility study determining an appropriate site for his project, Disney bought a 160 acres site near Anaheim in 1953. The park was designed by a creative team hand-picked by Walt from internal and outside talent. They founded WED Enterprises, the precursor to today's Walt Disney Imagineering. Construction began in 1954 and the park was dedicated during a special televised press event on the [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] Television Network on July 17, 1955, a day before its public opening.",
			},
