		summary = 'The **Eastern Hemisphere** is the half of the planet Earth which is east of the [[Prime meridian|prime meridian]] (which crosses Greenwich, London, United Kingdom) and west of the antimeridian (which crosses the [[Pacific Ocean]] and relatively little land from pole to pole). It is also used to refer to [[Afro-Eurasia]] ([[Africa]] and [[Eurasia]]) and [[Australia (continent)|Australia]], in contrast with the [[Western Hemisphere]], which includes mainly [[North America|North]] and [[South America]]. The Eastern Hemisphere may also be called the "**Oriental Hemisphere**", and may in addition be used in a cultural or [[Geopolitics|geopolitical]] sense as a synonym for the European term, "[[Old World]]".',
