		fame = 3,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Empirical statistical testing of economic theories",
		tags = { "Business and economics" },
		summary = '**Econometrics** is an application of [[Statistics|statistical methods]] to economic data in order to give [[Empirical evidence|empirical]] content to economic relationships. More precisely, it is "the quantitative analysis of actual economic [[Phenomenon|phenomena]] based on the concurrent development of theory and observation, related by appropriate methods of inference." An introductory [[Economics|economics]] textbook describes econometrics as allowing economists "to sift through mountains of data to extract simple relationships." Jan Tinbergen is one of the two founding fathers of econometrics. The other, Ragnar Frisch, also coined the term in the sense in which it is used today.',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"A basic tool for econometrics is the multiple linear regression model. Econometric theory uses statistical theory and mathematical statistics to evaluate and develop econometric methods. Econometricians try to find estimators that have desirable statistical properties including unbiasedness, efficiency, and consistency. Applied econometrics uses theoretical econometrics and real-world data for assessing economic theories, developing econometric models, analysing economic history, and forecasting.",
			},
