		fame = 1,
		emoji = "📈",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Social science studying goods and services",
		tags = { "Business and economics" },
		summary = "**Economics** is a [[Social science|social science]] that studies the [[Production (economics)|production]], distribution, and [[Consumption (economics)|consumption]] of [[Goods and services|goods and services]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Economics focuses on the behaviour and interactions of economic agents and how [[Economy|economies]] work. [[Microeconomics]] analyses what is viewed as the basic elements of economies, including individual agents and [[Market (economics)|markets]], their interactions, and the outcomes of those interactions. Individual agents may include households, firms, buyers, and sellers. [[Macroeconomics]] analyses economies as systems where production, distribution, consumption, savings, and investment expenditure interact; and the factors of production affecting them, such as: labour, [[Capital (economics)|capital]], land, and enterprise, [[Inflation|inflation]], [[Economic growth|economic growth]], and public policies that impact these elements. It also seeks to analyse and describe the [[World economy|global economy]].",
