		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "The **euro sign** is the currency sign used for the [[Euro|euro]], the official currency of the [[Eurozone|eurozone]]. The design was presented to the public by the [[European Commission]] on 12 December 1996. It consists of a stylized letter E (or epsilon), crossed by two lines instead of one. Depending on convention in each nation, the symbol can either precede or follow the value, e.g., €10 or 10€, often with an intervening space.",
