		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Colonial Algeria" },
		summary = "**French Algeria**, also known as **Colonial Algeria**, was a colony and later an [[Departments of France|integral part]] of [[France]]. French rule lasted from the beginning of the French conquest in 1830 until the end of the Algerian War which resulted in Algeria gaining independence on 5 July 1962.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The French conquest of Algeria began in 1830 with the invasion of Algiers which toppled the Regency of Algiers, though Algeria was not fully conquered and pacified until 1903. Algeria was ruled as a colony from 1830 to 1848, and then as multiple departments of France after the implementation of the 1848 French Constitution, a situation that lasted until Algerian independence in 1962. After a trip to [[Algiers]] in 1860, the French emperor [[Napoleon III]] became keen on establishing a client kingdom there which he would rule in a [[Personal union|personal union]], expanding freedoms for the indigenous population and limiting colonisation.",
