				"Overview",
				"Georgians are ethno-linguistically separate from all of their neighboring nations and primarily speak [[Georgian language|Georgian]], a Kartvelian language with no known relation to any other language family in the world. Georgians arose from Colchian and Iberian [[Civilization|civilizations]] of [[Classical antiquity|classical antiquity]]; Colchis was interconnected with the [[Ancient Greece|Hellenic world]], whereas Iberia was influenced by the [[Achaemenid Empire]] until [[Alexander the Great]] conquered it. In the early 4th century, the Georgians became one of the first to embrace Christianity. The vast majority of Georgians are Orthodox Christians, with most following their national Georgian Orthodox Church; there are also some historically Catholic and Muslim communities, as well as a significant number of irreligious Georgians.",
