		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Branch of the Indo-European language family",
		tags = { "Language", "Language families" },
		summary = "The **Germanic languages** are a branch of the [[Indo-European languages|Indo-European]] [[Language family|language family]] spoken natively by a population of about 515 million people mainly in [[Europe]], [[Northern America]], [[Oceania]], and [[Southern Africa]]. The most widely spoken Germanic language, [[English language|English]], is also the world's most widely spoken language with an estimated 2 billion speakers. All Germanic languages are derived from [[Proto-Germanic language|Proto-Germanic]], spoken in Iron Age Scandinavia, [[History of Germany|Iron Age Northern Germany]] and along the [[North Sea]] and Baltic coasts.",
