		tags = { "Entertainment", "Recreation and tourism" },
		aliases = { "Hike" },
		summary = 'A **hike** is a long, vigorous [[Walking|walk]], usually on trails or footpaths in the countryside. Walking for pleasure developed in Europe during the eighteenth century. Long hikes as part of a religious [[Pilgrimage|pilgrimage]] have existed for a much longer time. "Hiking" is the preferred term in [[Canada]] and the [[United States]]; the term "[[Walking|walking]]" is used in these countries for shorter, particularly urban walks. In the United Kingdom and Ireland, the word "walking" describes all forms of walking, whether it is a walk in a [[Park|park]] or backpacking in the [[Alps]]. The word hiking is also often used in the UK, along with **rambling**, **hillwalking**, and **fell walking** (a term mostly used for hillwalking in northern England).',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The term **bushwalking** is endemic to Australia. In New Zealand a long, vigorous walk or hike is called tramping. It is a common activity with numerous hiking organizations worldwide.",
			},
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Hindi",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗣️",
