			"Location identifier",
			"International Air Transport Association airport code",
		},
		summary = "An **IATA airport code**, also known as an **IATA location identifier**, **IATA station code**, or simply a **location identifier**, is a unique three-letter geocode designating many [[Airport|airports]], cities (with one or more airports) and [[Metropolitan area|metropolitan areas]] (cities with more than one airport) around the world, defined by the International Air Transport Association (IATA). The characters prominently displayed on baggage tags attached at airport check-in desks are an example of a way these codes are used.",
