			{
				"Overview",
				"The assignment of these codes is governed by IATA Resolution 763, and it is administered by the IATA's headquarters in [[Montreal]], Canada. The codes are published semi-annually in the IATA Airline Coding Directory. Alphabetical lists of airports sorted by IATA code are available. IATA also provides codes for airport handling entities and for certain railway stations, bus stations and ferry ports. A list of railway station codes, shared in agreements between airlines and rail lines such as Amtrak, SNCF, and, is available. However, many railway administrations have their own list of codes for their stations, such as Amtrak station codes.",
			},
		},
		related = { "Terrestrial animal", "Filter feeder" },
