		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = 'An **ideology** is a set of ideals, values, or [[Belief|beliefs]] that is attributed to a person or group of people, especially those held for reasons that are not purely about belief in certain [[Knowledge|knowledge]], and in which "practical elements are as prominent as theoretical ones". It is related to, but distinct from, a [[Worldview|worldview]].',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'The term was coined by Antoine Destutt de Tracy, a French Enlightenment aristocrat and [[Philosophy|philosopher]], who conceived it in 1796 as the "science of ideas" to develop a rational system of ideas. In [[Political science|political science]], the term is used in a descriptive sense to refer to political belief systems.',
