		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Igbo languages are spoken by a total of 31 million people. The number of Igboid languages depends on how one classifies a language versus a [[Dialect|dialect]], so there could be around 35 different Igbo languages. The core Igbo cluster, or Igbo proper, is generally thought to be one language but there is limited mutual intelligibility between the different groupings (north, west, south and east). A standard literary language termed 'Igbo izugbe' was generically developed and later adopted around 1972, with its core foundation based on the Orlu (Isu dialects), Anambra (Awka dialects) and Umuahia (Ohuhu dialects), omitting the nasalization and aspiration of those varieties.",
