		tags = { "Philosophy", "Logic" },
		summary = "**Inductive reasoning** refers to a variety of methods of reasoning in which the conclusion of an argument is supported not with deductive certainty, but at best with some degree of probability. Unlike [[Deductive reasoning|deductive reasoning]] (such as mathematical induction), where the conclusion is certain, given the premises are correct, inductive reasoning produces conclusions that are at best probable, given the premises provided.",
