		tags = { "Sociology" },
		aliases = { "Industrialization" },
		summary = '**Industrialisation** ([[British English|UK]]) [[American and British English spelling differences|or]] **industrialization** ([[American English|US]]) is "the period of social and economic change that transforms a human group from an [[Agrarian society|agrarian]] and [[Feudalism|feudal society]] into an industrial society. This involves an extensive reorganisation of an [[Economy|economy]] for the purpose of [[Manufacturing|manufacturing]]." Industrialisation is associated with an increase in [[Pollution|polluting]] industries heavily dependent on [[Fossil fuel|fossil fuels]]. With the increasing focus on [[Sustainable development|sustainable development]] and green industrial policy practices, industrialisation increasingly includes technological leapfrogging, with direct investment in more advanced, cleaner technologies.',
