	{
		title = "Information",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Facts provided or learned about something or someone",
		summary = "**Information** is an [[Abstraction|abstract concept]] that refers to something which has the power [[Communication|to inform]]. At the most fundamental level, it pertains to the interpretation (perhaps formally) of that which may be [[Sense|sensed]], or their [[Abstraction|abstractions]]. Any natural process that is not completely random and any observable pattern in any [[Means of communication|medium]] can be said to convey some amount of information. Whereas digital signals and other [[Data|data]] use discrete signs to convey information, other phenomena and artifacts such as analogue signals, poems, pictures, [[Music|music]] or other [[Sound|sounds]], and currents convey information in a more continuous form.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Information is not [[Knowledge|knowledge]] itself, but the [[Meaning (philosophy)|meaning]] that may be derived from a representation through interpretation. The concept of information is relevant to and connected with various concepts, including constraint, [[Communication|communication]], [[Control system|control]], [[Data|data]], [[Shape|form]], [[Education|education]], [[Knowledge|knowledge]], meaning, understanding, mental stimuli, pattern, [[Perception|perception]], [[Proposition|proposition]], representation, and entropy. Information is often processed iteratively: Data available at one step are [[Data processing|processed]] into information to be interpreted and processed at the next step. For example, in written text each [[Symbol|symbol]] or [[Letter (alphabet)|letter]] conveys information relevant to the word it is part of, each word conveys information relevant to the phrase it is part of, each phrase conveys information relevant to the sentence it is part of, and so on until at the final step information is interpreted and becomes knowledge in a given domain.",
			},
		},
	},
	{
