		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "ICH" },
		summary = "**Intangible cultural heritage** (**ICH**)—as opposed to a place's tangible [[Cultural heritage|cultural heritage]], cultural properties such as historic sites, monuments, and [[Artifact (archaeology)|artifacts]]—comprises manifestations of intellectual wealth such as customs, [[Belief|beliefs]], [[Tradition|traditions]], [[Folklore|folklore]], [[Language|language]], and knowledge, as expressed in particular through [[Craft|craftsmanship]] and [[Performance|performance]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Responding to the perceived over-representation of Western Europe among [[World Heritage Site|World Heritage Sites]], to help valorize cultural diversity, and following on from earlier related measures in Japan (1950) and in South Korea (1962), in 2001, UNESCO made a survey among states and [[Non-governmental organization|NGOs]] to try to agree on a definition, and the Convention for the Safeguarding of the Intangible Cultural Heritage was drafted in 2003 for its protection and promotion.",
