		description = "Grapheme which represents a word or a morpheme",
		tags = { "Language", "Basics" },
		aliases = { "Logograph", "Lexigraph" },
		summary = "In a written language, a **logogram**, also **logograph** or **lexigraph**, is a written character that represents a semantic component of a language, such as a [[Word|word]] or [[Morpheme|morpheme]]. [[Chinese characters]] as used in Chinese as well as other languages are logograms, as are [[Hieroglyphs|Egyptian hieroglyphs]] and characters in cuneiform script. A [[Writing system|writing system]] that primarily uses logograms is called a logography. Non-logographic writing systems, such as [[Alphabet|alphabets]] and syllabaries, are phonemic: their individual symbols represent sounds directly and lack any inherent meaning.",
