		summary = "The **Maasai** are an Eastern Nilotic ethnic group native to northern, central and southern regions of [[Kenya]] including northern [[Tanzania]], near the [[African Great Lakes]] region. Their native language is Maa, a Nilotic language related to Dinka, Kalenjin and Nuer, a branch within the broader [[Nilo-Saharan languages|Nilo-Saharan language family]]. Except for some elders living in rural areas, most Maasai people speak the official languages of Kenya and Tanzania—[[Swahili]] and [[English language|English]].",
