		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Form of local government",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "A **mayor–council government** is a system of [[Local government|local government]] in which a [[Mayor|mayor]] who is directly elected by the voters acts as chief executive, while a separately elected city council constitutes the legislative body. It is one of the two most common forms of local government in the United States, and is the form most frequently adopted in large cities, although the other common form, council–manager government, is the [[Local government|local government]] form of more municipalities.",
