		summary = "The **Mon language**, formerly known as **Peguan** and **Talaing**, is an Austroasiatic language spoken by the [[Mon people]]. Mon, like the related [[Khmer language]], but unlike most languages in [[Mainland Southeast Asia|mainland Southeast Asia]], is not [[Tone (linguistics)|tonal]]. The Mon language is a recognised indigenous language in Myanmar as well as an indigenous language of Thailand.",
		sections = {
