		description = "Person at the head of a monarchy",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "A **monarch** is a [[Head of state|head of state]] for life or until abdication, and therefore the head of state of a [[Monarchy|monarchy]]. A monarch usually exercises the highest authority and power in the [[Sovereign state|state]]. Usually, a monarch either personally [[Inheritance|inherits]] the lawful right to exercise the state's sovereign rights (often referred to as the throne or [[The Crown|the crown]]) or is [[Elective monarchy|selected by an established process]] from a family or cohort eligible to provide the nation's monarch. Alternatively, an individual may proclaim oneself monarch, or even usurp power, as many Ancient Greek tyrants did. If a young child is crowned the monarch, then a [[Regent|regent]] is often appointed to govern until the monarch reaches the requisite adult age to rule.",
