		summary = "A **mother**, **mom**, **mum**, **mommy**, or **mummy** is the female [[Parent|parent]] of a [[Child|child]]. A woman may be considered a mother by virtue of having given birth, by raising a child who may or may not be her biological [[Offspring|offspring]], or by supplying her ovum for [[Fertilisation|fertilisation]] in the case of gestational surrogacy.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'A biological mother may have legal obligations to a child not raised by her, such as an obligation of monetary support. An adoptive mother is a female who has become the child\'s parent through the legal process of [[Adoption|adoption]]. A putative mother is a female whose biological relationship to a child is alleged but has not been established. A stepmother is a non-biological female parent married to a child\'s preexisting parent, and may form a family unit but generally does not have the legal rights and responsibilities of a parent in relation to the child. A [[Father|father]] is the male counterpart of a mother. Women who are pregnant may be referred to as expectant mothers or mothers-to-be. The process of becoming a mother has been referred to as "matrescence". The [[Adjective|adjective]] "maternal" refers to a mother and comparatively to "paternal" for a [[Father|father]].',
