		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The vehicle propulsion is provided by an [[Engine|engine or motor]], usually a gasoline/[[Diesel engine|diesel]] [[Internal combustion engine|internal combustion engine]] or an [[Electric motor|electric]] traction motor, or some combination of the two as in hybrid electric vehicles and plug-in hybrid vehicles. For legal purposes, motor vehicles are often identified within many vehicle classes, including [[Car|cars]], [[Bus|buses]], [[Motorcycle|motorcycles]], off-road vehicles, light trucks, and regular [[Truck|trucks]]. These classifications vary according to the legal codes of each country. [[International Organization for Standardization|ISO]] 3833:1977 is the standard for road vehicle types, terms, and definitions. Typically, to avoid requiring people with disabilities from having to possess an operator's license to use one, or requiring tags and insurance, powered wheelchairs are specifically excluded by law from being considered motor vehicles.",
