		summary = "The **northern celestial hemisphere**, also called the **Northern Sky**, is the [[Northern Hemisphere|northern half]] of the [[Celestial sphere|celestial sphere]]; that is, it lies north of the celestial equator. This arbitrary sphere appears to rotate westward around a polar axis due to [[Earth's rotation]].",
		sections = {
