		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Matter composed of organic compounds",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Organic material", "Natural organic matter", "NOM" },
		summary = "**Organic matter**, **organic material** or **natural organic matter** (**NOM**) is the large source of carbon-based compounds found within natural and engineered, terrestrial, and aquatic environments. Organic molecules can also be made by chemical reactions that do not involve life. Basic structures are created from [[Cellulose|cellulose]], [[Tannin|tannin]], cutin, and lignin, along with other various [[Protein|proteins]], [[Lipid|lipids]], and [[Carbohydrate|carbohydrates]]. Organic matter is very important in the movement of nutrients in the environment and plays a role in water retention on the surface of the planet.",
