		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Organology** is the science of musical instruments and their classifications. It embraces study of instruments' history, instruments used in different cultures, technical aspects of how instruments produce sound, and musical instrument classification. There is a degree of overlap between organology, ethnomusicology (being subsets of [[Musicology|musicology]]) and the branch of the science of [[Acoustics|acoustics]] devoted to musical instruments.",
