		category = "Concept",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🤔",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Philosophical study of history and its discipline",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Philosophy of history** is the [[Philosophy|philosophical]] study of [[History|history]] and its [[Academic discipline|discipline]]. The term was coined by the French philosopher [[Voltaire]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"In [[Contemporary philosophy|contemporary philosophy]] a distinction has developed between the speculative philosophy of history and the critical philosophy of history, now referred to as analytic. The split between these approaches may be approximately compared, by analogy and on the strength of regional and academic influences, to the schism in commitments between [[Analytic philosophy|analytic]] and [[Continental philosophy|continental philosophy]] wherein the analytic approach is pragmatic and the speculative approach attends more closely to a [[Metaphysics|metaphysics]] (or anti-metaphysics) of determining forces like language or the [[Phenomenology (philosophy)|phenomenology]] of perception at the level of background assumptions. At the level of practice, the analytic approach questions the meaning and purpose of the historical process whereas the speculative approach studies the foundations and implications of history and the [[Historical method|historical method]].",
			},
