		emoji = "🍬",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Sugar transport tissue in vascular plants",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Phloem** is the living tissue in [[Vascular plant|vascular plants]] that transports the soluble [[Organic compound|organic compounds]] made during [[Photosynthesis|photosynthesis]] and known as photosynthates, in particular the sugar [[Sucrose|sucrose]], to the rest of the plant. This transport process is called translocation. Different types of phloem can be distinguished. The early phloem formed in the growth apices is called protophloem. Protophloem eventually becomes obliterated once it connects to the durable phloem in mature organs, the metaphloem. Further, secondary phloem is formed during the thickening of stem structures.",
