		description = "Experience that feels good or is enjoyable",
		tags = { "Psychology", "Emotions and traits" },
		summary = "**Pleasure** is an experience that feels good, that involves the enjoyment of something. It contrasts with pain or [[Suffering|suffering]], which are forms of feeling bad. It is closely related to value, desire and action: humans and other conscious animals find pleasure enjoyable, positive or worthy of seeking. Pleasure is part of various other mental states such as ecstasy, euphoria and flow. [[Happiness]] and [[Well-being|well-being]] are closely related to pleasure but not identical with it. There is no general agreement as to whether pleasure should be understood as a sensation, a quality of experiences, an attitude to experiences or otherwise.",
