		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Honorary name given after death",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "A **posthumous name** is an honorary [[Personal name|name]] given mainly to revered dead people in East Asian culture. It is predominantly used in Asian countries such as [[China]], [[South Korea|Korea]], [[Vietnam]], [[Japan]], [[Brunei]], [[Cambodia]], [[Indonesia]], [[Laos]], [[Malaysia]], [[Myanmar]], the [[Philippines]], [[Singapore]], [[Timor-Leste]] and [[Thailand]]. Reflecting on the person's accomplishments or reputation, the title is assigned after death and essentially replaces the name used during life. Although most posthumous names are given to royalty, some posthumous names are given to honor significant people without hereditary titles, such as courtiers or military generals.",
