			{
				"Overview",
				'The boundaries of provinces can only be altered by the Spanish Parliament, giving rise to the common view that the [[Autonomous communities of Spain|17 autonomous communities]] are subdivided into 50 provinces. In reality, the system is not hierarchical but defined according to jurisdiction. The body charged with government and administration of a province is the provincial council, but their existence is controversial. As the province is defined as a "local entity" in the Constitution, the Provincial council belongs to the sphere of local government.',
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Category", "Province" },
