	{
		title = "Public administration",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Academic discipline; implementation or management of policy",
		tags = { "Politics and government", "State structure and administration" },
		aliases = { "Public policy and administration", "Public management" },
		summary = "**Public administration**, also known as **public policy and administration** or **public management**, is the implementation of [[Public policy|public policies]], which are sets of proposed or decided actions to [[Problem solving|solve problems]] and address relevant social and economic issues.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'Administrative effectiveness refers to the consistent performance of administrative duties and the timely achievement of set objectives (Akinfolarin, 2017). This implementation generally occurs through the administration of government programs in the public sector, but also through the [[Management|management]] of [[Nonprofit organization|non-profit organizations]] in the community sector, and/or [[Business|businesses]] in the private sector that provide [[Goods and services|goods and services]] to the government through public-private partnerships and government procurement. It has also been characterized as the "translation of politics into the reality that citizens experience every day." In an academic context, public administration has been described as the study of government [[Decision-making|decision-making]]; the analysis of policies and the inputs that have produced them, as well as those necessary to produce alternative policies.',
			},
		},
