	{
		title = "Publishing",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Production and distribution of media",
		tags = { "Mass media" },
		summary = "**Publishing ** is the process of making information, literature, music, software, and other content, whether in physical or digital form, available to the public for sale or free of charge. Traditionally, the term publishing refers to the creation and distribution of [[Printing|printed works]], such as [[Book|books]], zines, [[Comic book|comic books]], [[Newspaper|newspapers]], and [[Magazine|magazines]], to the public. The advent of digital information systems has led to an expansion of its scope to include digital publishing, such as e-books, digital magazines, websites, [[Social media|social media]], [[Music|music]], and video game publishing.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The commercial publishing industry ranges from large multinational conglomerates such as News Corp, Pearson, Penguin Random House, and Thomson Reuters to major retail brands and thousands of small independent publishers. It has various divisions such as trade/retail publishing of fiction and non-fiction, educational publishing, and academic and scientific publishing. Publishing is also undertaken by governments, civil society, and private companies for administrative or compliance requirements, business, research, advocacy, or public interest objectives. This can include annual reports, research reports, market research, policy briefings, and technical reports. Publishing has evolved from a small, ancient form limited by law or religion to a modern, large-scale industry disseminating all types of information.",
