		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Spiciness", "Hotness" },
		summary = '**Pungency**, commonly referred to as **spiciness**, **hotness** or **heat**, is a sensation that contributes to the flavor of certain foods such as [[Chili pepper|chili peppers]]. Highly pungent foods may be experienced as unpleasant. The term **piquancy** is sometimes applied to foods with a lower degree of pungency that are "agreeably stimulating to the palate". In addition to chili peppers, piquant ingredients include wasabi, [[Horseradish|horseradish]] and [[Mustard (condiment)|mustard]]. The primary substances responsible for pungency are capsaicin (in chilis), piperine (in peppercorns) and allyl isothiocyanate (in [[Radish|radishes]], mustard and wasabi).',
