		summary = "**Reductionism** is any of several related [[Philosophy|philosophical]] ideas regarding the associations between [[Phenomenon|phenomena]] which can be described in terms of simpler or more fundamental phenomena. It is also described as an intellectual and philosophical position that interprets a complex system as the sum of its parts, contrary to holism. Reductionism tends to focus on the small, predictable details of a system and is often associated with various philosophies like emergence, [[Materialism|materialism]], and [[Determinism|determinism]].",
