		title = "Regent",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "One who governs in place of a monarch",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "In a [[Monarchy|monarchy]], a **regent** is a person appointed to execute the office of a [[Monarch|monarch]] temporarily, essentially as a substitute ruler. Regencies may arise for a number of reasons, including the monarch being a minor, ill, absent from the country, or otherwise unavailable. A regent may also be appointed in cases where the throne is vacant, or the identity of the legitimate monarch is disputed. The rule of a regent or regents is called a **regency**.",
	},
