		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Ferroconcrete", "Ferro-concrete" },
		summary = "**Reinforced concrete**, also called **ferroconcrete** or **ferro-concrete**, is a [[Composite material|composite material]] in which [[Concrete|concrete]]'s relatively low tensile strength and [[Ductility|ductility]] are compensated for by the inclusion of reinforcement having higher tensile strength or ductility. The reinforcement is usually, though not necessarily, steel reinforcing bars (known as rebar) and is usually embedded [[Passivation (chemistry)|passively]] in the concrete before the concrete sets. However, post-tensioning is also employed as a technique to reinforce the concrete. In terms of volume used annually, it is one of the most common engineering materials.",
