		summary = "**Reproduction** (or **procreation** or **breeding**) is the [[Biological process|biological process]] by which new individual [[Organism|organisms]] – [[Offspring|offspring]] – are produced from their parent or parents.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"In asexual reproduction, an organism can reproduce without the involvement of another organism. Asexual reproduction is not limited to [[Unicellular organism|single-celled organisms]]. The [[Cloning|cloning]] of an organism is a form of asexual reproduction. By asexual reproduction, an organism creates a genetically similar or identical copy of itself. This produces offspring organisms whose genetic characteristics are derived from both parental organisms.",
