		title = "Resin",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🌱",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Organic polymer, typically from plants",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "A **resin** is a highly viscous liquid or solid that can be converted into a [[Polymer|polymer]]. Resins may be biological or synthetic in origin but are typically harvested from plants. Resins are mixtures of [[Organic compound|organic compounds]] insoluble in water, predominantly terpenes. Technically, resins should not be confused with gums, which consist predominantly of water-soluble polysaccharides, although the two terms are often interchangeable in the less formal context. Common resins include pine oleoresins, [[Amber|amber]], hashish, frankincense, myrrh, and the animal-derived resin shellac. Resins are used in varnishes, [[Adhesive|adhesives]], food additives, incenses, and [[Perfume|perfumes]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Resins repel [[Herbivore|herbivores]], insects, and pathogens, while the volatile phenolic compounds may attract benefactors such as predators of insects that attack the plant.",
			},
