		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Sigillary script" },
		summary = "**Seal script** or **sigillary script** is a style of writing [[Chinese characters]] that was common throughout the latter half of the 1st millennium BC. It evolved organically out of bronze script during the [[Zhou dynasty]] (1046–256 BC). The variant of seal script used in the state of Qin eventually became comparatively standardized, and was adopted as the formal script across all of China during the [[Qin dynasty]] (221–206 BC). It was still widely used for decorative engraving and seals during the [[Han dynasty]] (202 BC – 220 AD).",
