		tags = { "Psychology", "Emotions and traits" },
		summary = "**Shame** is an unpleasant self-conscious [[Emotion|emotion]] associated with negative self-evaluation in relation to [[Social norm|social norms]] and one’s personal [[Morality|moral]] standards. It can generate feelings of pain, exposure, distrust, powerlessness, and worthlessness, which in turn may give rise to [[Anger|anger]], denial, avoidance, reduced sensitivity to shame, and a tendency to externalize blame.",
