	{
		title = "Slovene language",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🗣️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "South Slavic language",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Slovene", "Slovenian" },
		summary = "**Slovene** ( or ) or **Slovenian** is a South Slavic language of the [[Balto-Slavic languages|Balto-Slavic]] branch of the [[Indo-European languages|Indo-European language family]]. Most of its 2.5 million speakers are the inhabitants of [[Slovenia]], the majority of them ethnic Slovenes. As Slovenia is part of the [[European Union]], Slovene is also one of its 24 [[Languages of the European Union|official and working languages]]. Its grammar is highly fusional, and it has a dual grammatical number, an archaic feature shared with some other Indo-European languages. Two accentual norms (one characterized by pitch accent) are used. Its flexible word order is often adjusted for emphasis or stylistic reasons, although basically it is an SVO language.",
		infobox = {
