		fame = 2,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "System of linked social structures",
		tags = { "Society", "Basics" },
		summary = "The term **social order** can be used in two senses: In the first sense, it refers to a particular system of [[Social structure|social structures]] and [[Institution|institutions]]. Examples are the ancient, the [[Feudalism|feudal]], and the capitalist social order. In the second sense, social order is contrasted to social chaos or disorder and refers to a stable state of society in which the existing social structure is accepted and maintained by its members. The **problem of order** or Hobbesian problem, which is central to much of [[Sociology|sociology]], [[Political science|political science]] and [[Political philosophy|political philosophy]], is the question of how and why it is that social orders exist at all.",
