		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Any interpersonal relationship between two or more conspecifics between/within groups",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "A **social relation** is the fundamental unit of analysis within the [[Social science|social sciences]], and describes any voluntary or involuntary interpersonal relationship between two or more conspecifics within and/or between groups. The group can be a language or kinship group, a social institution or organization, an economic class, a nation, or gender. Social relations are derived from human behavioral ecology, and, as an aggregate, form a coherent [[Social structure|social structure]] whose constituent parts are best understood relative to each other and to the social ecosystem as a whole.",
