	{
		title = "Spanish language",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗣️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Romance language",
		tags = { "Indo-European languages", "Italic languages" },
		aliases = { "Spanish", "Castilian" },
		summary = "**Spanish** or **Castilian** is a [[Romance languages|Romance language]] of the [[Indo-European languages|Indo-European language family]] that evolved from the [[Vulgar Latin]] spoken on the [[Iberian Peninsula]] of [[Europe]]. It originated in the [[Kingdom of Castile]], a historical kingdom in north-central [[Spain]]. Today, it is a global language with 519 million native speakers, mainly in the [[Americas]] and Spain, and about 636 million speakers total, including [[Second language|second-language speakers]]. Spanish is the official language of 21 countries, as well as one of the [[Official languages of the United Nations|six official languages]] of the [[United Nations]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Spanish is the world's second-most spoken native language after [[Mandarin Chinese]]; the world's fourth-most spoken language overall after [[English language|English]], Mandarin Chinese, and [[Hindustani language|Hindustani]] ([[Hindi]]-[[Urdu]]); and the world's most widely spoken Romance language. The country with the largest population of native speakers is [[Mexico]]. Spanish is part of the Ibero-Romance language group, which evolved from several dialects of Vulgar Latin in Iberia after the collapse of the Western Roman Empire in the 5th century. The oldest Latin texts with traces of Spanish come from mid-northern Iberia in the 9th century, and the first systematic written use of the language happened in Toledo, a prominent city of the [[Kingdom of Castile]], in the 13th century. Spanish colonialism in the [[Early modern period|early modern period]] spurred the introduction of the language to overseas locations, most notably to the Americas.",
