		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "A **structure** is an arrangement and organization of interrelated elements in a material object or [[System|system]], or the object or system so organized. Physical structures include artifacts and objects such as [[Building|buildings]] and [[Machine|machines]] and natural objects such as [[Organism|organisms]], [[Mineral|minerals]] and [[Substance (chemistry)|chemicals]]. Abstract structures include [[Data structure|data structures]] in [[Computer science|computer science]] and [[Musical form|musical form]]. Types of structure include a [[Hierarchy|hierarchy]] (a cascade of one-to-many relationships), a network featuring many-to-many links, or a lattice featuring connections between components that are neighbors in space.",
