		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Debate in social sciences",
		tags = { "Sociology" },
		aliases = { "Structure or agency" },
		summary = "In the [[Social science|social sciences]] there is a standing debate over the primacy of **structure or agency** in shaping human behaviour. [[Social structure|Structure]] is the recurrent patterned arrangements which influence or limit the choices and opportunities available. Agency is the capacity of individuals to act independently and to make their own free choices. The structure versus agency debate may be understood as an issue of [[Socialization|socialization]] against [[Autonomy|autonomy]] in determining whether an individual acts as a free agent or in a manner dictated by [[Social structure|social structure]].",
