		summary = "**Telephone numbers in Indonesia** have different systems for landlines and mobile phones: landlines use area codes, while mobile phones do not.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'For landline area codes, the digit "0" is added before the area code when dialing domestic long distance from within Indonesia, but is always omitted when calling from abroad. Instead, callers would use the Indonesian country code +62, followed by the area code, without the "0". Domestic phone numbers in large cities have 8 digits, and in other areas 7 digits. Mobile phone numbers have 9 to 11 digits for postpaid services, depending on the operator, whereas prepaid services have 10 to 12 digits, determined by the operator. Until October 1999, East Timor was included in the Indonesian telephone numbering plan, using the area codes 0390 (for Dili) and 0399 (for Baucau). To make a phone call to Indonesia from abroad, the following formats are used:',
