		summary = "In [[Turkey]], time is given by [[UTC+03:00]] year-round. This time is also called **Turkey Time** (**TRT**). This time zone coincides with the Moscow Time and [[UTC+03:00|Arabia Standard Time]] zones. TRT was adopted by the Turkish Government on 8 September 2016. It was also in use in [[Northern Cyprus]] until it reverted to [[Eastern European Time]] (EET) in October 2017.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"During some seasons (March–October), the TRT coincides with the [[Eastern European Summer Time]] (the daylight-saving version of the Eastern European Time).",
