		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Minimum horizontal distance to a point of equal elevation",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "The **topographic isolation** of a summit is the minimum horizontal distance to a point of equal [[Elevation|elevation]], representing a radius of dominance in which the peak is the highest point. It can be calculated for small [[Hill|hills]] and [[Island|islands]], major mountain peaks, and even submarine summits. [[Mount Everest]], the highest point on Earth, has an undefined isolation, since there is no higher point to reference.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Because topographic isolation can be difficult to determine, a common approximation is the distance to a peak called the **nearest higher neighbour** (NHN).",
