	{
		title = "Topography",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Study of the forms of land surfaces in earth",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Topography** is the study of forms and features of land surfaces. The topography of an area may refer to landforms and features themselves, or a description or depiction in maps.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Topography is a field of geoscience and [[Planetary science|planetary science]], and is concerned with local detail in general, including not only [[Terrain|relief]], but also [[Natural environment|natural]], artificial, and [[Culture|cultural]] features such as roads, land boundaries, and buildings. In the United States, topography often means specifically relief, even though the [[United States Geological Survey|USGS]] topographic maps record not just [[Elevation|elevation]] contours, but also roads, populated places, structures, land boundaries, and so on. Topography in a narrow sense involves the recording of relief or [[Terrain|terrain]], the three-dimensional quality of the surface, and the identification of specific [[Landform|landforms]]; this is also known as geomorphometry. In modern usage, this involves the generation of elevation data in digital form (DEM).",
