		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Extreme form of authoritarianism and a theoretical concept",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Totalitarianism** is a political system and a [[Government|form of government]] that completely controls the public sphere and the private sphere of society. It is characterized by its prohibition of opposing [[Political party|political parties]] and its extreme suppression of opposition to the state. In the field of [[Political science|political science]], totalitarianism is the extreme form of [[Authoritarianism|authoritarianism]], wherein all political power is held by a dictator. This figure controls the national politics and peoples of the nation with continual propaganda campaigns that are broadcast by state-controlled and state-aligned private [[Mass media|mass communications media]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"A totalitarian government uses [[Ideology|ideology]] to control most aspects of human life, such as the [[Political economy|political economy]] of the country, the system of [[Education|education]], the [[The arts|arts]] and [[Science|sciences]], and the private [[Morality|morality]] of its citizens. In the exercise of power, the difference between a totalitarian government and an authoritarian government is one of degree. Whereas totalitarianism features a charismatic dictator and a fixed [[Worldview|worldview]], authoritarianism only features a dictator who holds power for the sake of holding power. The authoritarian dictator is supported, either jointly or individually, by a [[Military junta|military junta]] and by the socio-economic elites who are the ruling class of the country. The word totalitarian was first used in the early 1920s to describe the Italian Fascist government.",
			},
		},
		related = { "Xbox One" },
	},
	{
