		fame = 3,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Dose dependant harmfulness of substances",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Toxicity** is the degree to which a [[Substance (chemistry)|chemical substance]] or a particular [[Mixture|mixture]] of substances can damage an [[Organism|organism]]. Toxicity can refer to the effect on a whole organism, such as an [[Animal|animal]], [[Bacteria|bacterium]], or [[Plant|plant]], as well as the effect on a substructure of the organism, such as a [[Cell (biology)|cell]] (cytotoxicity) or an organ such as the [[Liver|liver]] (hepatotoxicity).",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Toxicity is species-specific, making cross-species analysis problematic. Newer [[Paradigm|paradigms]] and metrics are evolving to bypass animal testing, while maintaining the concept of toxicity endpoints.",
			},
