		summary = "**Setswana**, also known by its [[Endonym and exonym|native name]] **Tswana**, is a Bantu language indigenous to [[Southern Africa]] and spoken by about 8.2 million people. It is closely related to the Sepedi and Sesotho languages, as well as the Sekgaladi and likely the Silozi language.",
