				"Overview",
				"Setswana is a [[Lingua franca|lingua franca]] in Botswana. It is an official language of [[Zimbabwe]] and [[South Africa]].. The Setswana language in the Botswana has variations in which it is spoken according to the ethnic groups found in Botswana (Bakgatla, Barolong, Bakwena, Batlhaping, Bahurutshe, Bafokeng, Batlokwa, Bataung, and Batswapong, Balete, Bangwato, Babirwa, among others); the written language remains the same. A number of speakers are found in South Afrca. A small number of speakers are also found in [[Zimbabwe]] (unknown number) and [[Namibia]] (about 10,000 people).",
