		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "In ancient Greek religion and [[Greek mythology|mythology]], the **twelve Olympians** are the major deities of the Greek pantheon, commonly considered to be [[Zeus]], [[Poseidon]], [[Hera]], Demeter, Aphrodite, [[Athena]], [[Artemis]], [[Apollo]], Ares, Hephaestus, [[Hermes]], and either Hestia or Dionysus. They were called Olympians because, according to tradition, they resided on [[Mount Olympus]].",
		sections = {
			{ "Overview", "Besides the twelve Olympians, there were many other cultic groupings of twelve gods." },
