		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Verse in the uncountable (mass noun) sense refers to [[Poetry|poetry]] in contrast to [[Prose|prose]]. Where the common unit of verse is based on meter or [[Rhyme|rhyme]], the common unit of prose is purely grammatical, such as a [[Sentence (linguistics)|sentence]] or paragraph. Verse in the second sense is also used pejoratively in contrast to poetry to suggest work that is too pedestrian or too incompetent to be classed as poetry.",
