		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = 'The **Western Hemisphere** is the half of the planet Earth that lies west of the Prime Meridian and east of the 180th meridian. The other half is called the [[Eastern Hemisphere]]. In the [[United States]], the term "Western Hemisphere" is often used as a metonym for the [[Americas]], even though geographically, the hemisphere also includes parts of other continents.',
