		summary = "The **Western canon** is the body of [[High culture|high-culture]] literature, philosophy, art, music and architecture from the [[Western culture|Western world]], with works classified within it considered to be—and celebrated—as classics in the context of [[Western culture|Western civilization]]. The concept has been discussed and debated in cultural criticism with regard to Western exceptionalism and which works constitute the canon, given the lack of official standardization of the category.",
