		title = "Wildlife",
		category = "Concept",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "💭",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Undomesticated organisms",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Wildlife** refers to [[Domestication|undomesticated]] animals and uncultivated plant species which can exist in their natural [[Habitat|habitat]], but has come to include all [[Organism|organisms]] that grow or live wild in an area without being [[Species|introduced]] by humans. Wildlife was also synonymous to game, birds and mammals hunted for sport. Wildlife can be found in all [[Ecosystem|ecosystems]], both wild and most developed [[Urban area|urban areas]], forming distinct groups. While the term in [[Popular culture|popular culture]] usually refers to animals that are untouched by human existence, most scientists agree that much wildlife is affected by humans.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Some wildlife threaten human safety, health, property and [[Quality of life|quality of life]], but many wild animals have value to humans, whether economic, educational, or sentimental. Humans have historically tended to separate [[Civilization|civilization]] from wildlife in a number of ways, including the legal, social and moral senses. Some animals, however, have adapted to [[Suburb|suburban]] environments. This includes urban wildlife such as feral cats, dogs, mice, and rats. Some religions declare certain animals to be sacred, and in modern times, concern for the [[Natural environment|natural environment]] has provoked [[Environmentalism|activists]] to protest against the exploitation of wildlife for human benefit or entertainment. The annual international trade may be worth billions of dollars and affects hundreds of millions of individual specimens.",
			},
		},
		related = { "Nikita Khrushchev" },
	},
