		description = "Country in Central America",
		tags = { "North America", "Central America" },
		summary = "**Belize** is a country on the north-eastern coast of [[Central America]]. It is bordered by [[Mexico]] to the north, the [[Caribbean Sea]] to the east, and [[Guatemala]] to the west and south. It also shares a [[Maritime boundary|maritime boundary]] with [[Honduras]] to the southeast. Part of the [[Caribbean]] region, Belize is a member of the [[Caribbean Community]] (CARICOM) and the Commonwealth Caribbean, the historical British West Indies.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The [[Maya civilization]] spread into the area of Belize between 1500 BC and 300 AD and flourished until about 1200. European contact began in 1502–1504 when [[Christopher Columbus]] sailed along the Gulf of Honduras. European exploration was begun by English settlers in 1638. [[Spanish Empire|Spain]] and [[Kingdom of Great Britain|Britain]] both laid claim to the land until the British victory over the Spanish in the Battle of St. George's Caye (1798). It became a British colony in 1840, and a [[Crown colony]] in 1862. Belize achieved its independence from the [[United Kingdom]] on 21 September 1981. Belize's abundance of terrestrial and marine plants and animals and its diversity of ecosystems, including extensive [[Coral reef|coral reefs]], give it a key place in the globally significant Mesoamerican Biological Corridor. It is considered a part of both [[Central America]] and the [[Caribbean]].",
