		summary = "**Bolivia**, officially the **Plurinational State of Bolivia**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] located in central [[South America]]. Its geography primarily consists of an [[Andes|Andean]] region to the west and tropical lowlands to the east and north. The country has a diverse environment, including the vast [[Amazon rainforest|Amazonian]] plain, the [[Gran Chaco]], temperate valleys, the high-altitude [[Altiplano|Altiplanoplateau]], snow-capped peaks, and mountains, encompassing a wide range of climates and biomes across its regions and cities. It includes part of the Pantanal, the largest tropical wetland in the world, along its eastern border.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Bolivia is bordered by [[Brazil]] to the north and east, [[Paraguay]] to the southeast, [[Argentina]] to the south, [[Chile]] to the southwest, and [[Peru]] to the west. The [[Seat of government|seat of government]] is [[La Paz]], which contains the executive, legislative, and electoral branches of government, while the constitutional capital is Sucre, the seat of the judiciary. While most population and urban centers lie in the Andean region, the largest city and principal industrial center is [[Santa Cruz de la Sierra]], located in the eastern tropical lowlands. The [[Sovereign state|sovereign state]] of Bolivia is a constitutionally [[Unitary state|unitary state]] divided into nine departments. One-third of the country is within the [[Andes|Andean]] mountain range.",
