			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Presidential system|presidential republic]] under a hereditary dictatorship" },
			{ "Established", "27 June 1977" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Dominica",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in the Caribbean",
		tags = { "North America", "Caribbean" },
		aliases = { "Commonwealth of Dominica" },
		summary = "**Dominica** officially the **Commonwealth of Dominica**, is an [[Island country|island country]] in the [[Caribbean]]. It is part of the Windward Islands chain in the [[Lesser Antilles]] archipelago in the [[Caribbean Sea]]. The capital, Roseau, is located on the western side of the island. Dominica's closest neighbours are two constituent territories of the [[European Union]], both overseas departments of France: [[Guadeloupe]] to the northwest and [[Martinique]] to the south-southeast. Dominica comprises a land area of 750 km², and the highest point is Morne Diablotins, at 1448 m in elevation. The population was 71,293 at the 2011 census.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The island was settled by the Arawak arriving from South America in the fifth century. The Kalinago displaced the Arawak by the 15th century. [[Christopher Columbus]] is said to have passed the island on Sunday, 3rd November 1493. It was later colonised by Europeans, predominantly by the French from 1690 to 1763. [[Kingdom of Great Britain|Great Britain]] took possession in 1763 after the Seven Years' War and continued the legacy of forced labor to gain wealth, and gradually established English as its official language. The island gained independence as a republic in 1978. Dominica has been nicknamed the \"Nature Island of the Caribbean\" for its natural environment. It is the youngest island in the Lesser Antilles, and is still being formed by Geothermal-Volcanic activity, as evidenced by the world's second-largest [[Hot spring|hot spring]], called Boiling Lake.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Roseau" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[English language|English]]" },
			{ "Languages", "Dominican Creole French, Kokoy" },
			{ "People are called", "Dominican" },
			{ "Government", "[[Unitary parliamentary republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "1 March 1967" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Dominican Republic",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country in the Caribbean",
		tags = { "North America", "Caribbean" },
		summary = "The **Dominican Republic** is an [[Island country|island country]] on the eastern part of the Caribbean island of [[Hispaniola]] in the [[Greater Antilles]] of the [[Caribbean Sea]] in the [[Atlantic Ocean|North Atlantic Ocean]]. It shares a [[Maritime boundary|maritime border]] with [[Puerto Rico]] to the east and a land border with [[Haiti]] to the west, occupying the eastern five-eighths of Hispaniola which, along with Saint Martin, is one of only two islands in the [[Caribbean]] shared by two [[Sovereign state|sovereign states]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"In the Antilles, the country is the second-largest by area after [[Cuba]] at 48,671 km² and the second most populous after Haiti with approximately 11.4 million people in 2024, of whom 3.6 million reside in the metropolitan area of [[Santo Domingo]], the capital city. [[Indigenous peoples of the Caribbean|Indigenous peoples]] had inhabited Hispaniola prior to [[European colonization of the Americas|European contact]], including the [[Taíno]], who divided it into five chiefdoms. [[Christopher Columbus]] claimed the island for [[Crown of Castile|Castile]], landing there on his first voyage in 1492. The colony of Santo Domingo became the site of the first permanent European settlement in the [[Americas]]. In 1697, Spain recognized French dominion over the western third of the island, which became the independent First Empire of Haiti in 1804. A group of Dominicans deposed the Spanish governor and declared independence from Spain in November 1821, but were annexed by Haiti in February 1822.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Santo Domingo]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "Spanish" },
			{ "People are called", "Dominican Quisqueyan (colloquial)" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Presidential system|presidential republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "1821–1822" },
			{ "Area", "48,671 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Ecuador",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in South America",
		tags = { "Countries", "South America" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Ecuador" },
		summary = "**Ecuador**, officially the **Republic of Ecuador**, is a country in northwestern [[South America]], bordered by [[Colombia]] on the north, [[Peru]] on the east and south, and the [[Pacific Ocean]] on the west. It also includes the Galápagos Province which contains the [[Galápagos Islands]] in the Pacific, about 1000 km west of the mainland. The country's [[Capital city|capital]] is [[Quito]], and the largest city is [[Guayaquil]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The land that comprises modern-day Ecuador was once home to several groups of indigenous peoples that were gradually incorporated into the [[Inca Empire]] during the 15th century. The territory was [[Spanish colonization of the Americas|colonized by the Spanish Empire]] during the 16th century, achieving independence in 1820 as part of [[Gran Colombia]], from which it emerged as a [[Sovereign state|sovereign state]] in 1830. Spanish is the official language spoken by a majority of the population, although 13 native languages are also recognized, including [[Quechuan languages|Quechua]] and Shuar. Ecuador is a plurinational [[Representative democracy|representative democratic]] [[Presidential system|presidential]] republic and a [[Developing country|developing country]] whose economy is highly dependent on exports of commodities, primarily petroleum and agricultural products. The country is a founding member of the [[United Nations]], [[Organization of American States]], [[Mercosur]], PROSUR, and the [[Non-Aligned Movement]].",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Official languages", "Spanish" },
