	{
		title = "Ethiopia",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in East Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "East Africa" },
		aliases = { "Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia", "FDRE" },
		summary = "**Ethiopia**, officially the **Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia** (**FDRE**), is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] located in the [[Horn of Africa]] region of [[East Africa]]. It shares borders with [[Eritrea]] to the north, [[Djibouti]] to the northeast, [[Somalia]] to the southeast, [[Kenya]] to the south, [[South Sudan]] to the west, and [[Sudan]] to the northwest. Ethiopia covers a land area of 1,104,300 km². As of 2026, it has around 138 million inhabitants, making it the 10th-most populous country in the world and 2nd most populous country in Africa.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The national capital and largest city, [[Addis Ababa]], lies several kilometres west of the [[East African Rift]] that splits the country into the African and Somali tectonic plates. [[Early modern human|Anatomically modern humans]] emerged in what is now Ethiopia. In 980 BC, the Kingdom of D'mt extended its realm over Eritrea and the northern region of Ethiopia, while the [[Kingdom of Aksum]] maintained a unified civilisation in the region for 900 years. Christianity arrived to the kingdom in 330 AD, while Islam gained influence during the first Hijra in 615. After the collapse of Aksum in 960, the Zagwe dynasty ruled the north-central parts of Ethiopia.",
			},
