	{
		title = "Federated States of Micronesia",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country in Oceania",
		tags = { "Oceania", "Micronesia" },
		aliases = { "FSM" },
		summary = "The **Federated States of Micronesia** (**FSM**), or simply **Micronesia**, is an [[Island country|island country]] in [[Micronesia]], a region of [[Oceania]]. The [[Federation|federation]] encompasses the majority of the Caroline Islands (excluding [[Palau]]) and consists of four states—from west to east: Yap, Chuuk, Pohnpei, and Kosrae—that span the western [[Pacific Ocean|Pacific]] just north of the [[Equator|equator]] for a [[Longitude|longitudinal]] distance of almost 2700 km. Together, the states comprise around 607 islands and a combined land area of approximately 702 km².",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The entire island federation lies across the northern Pacific accordingly: northeast of [[Indonesia]] and [[Papua New Guinea]], south of [[Guam]] and the Marianas, west of [[Nauru]] and the [[Marshall Islands]], east of [[Palau]] and the [[Philippines]], about 2900 km north of eastern [[Australia]], 3,400 km southeast of Japan, and some 4000 km southwest of Honolulu of the [[Hawaiian Islands]]. The country's total land area is relatively small, but its waters occupy nearly 3 million km² of the [[Pacific Ocean]], giving the country the 14th-largest [[Exclusive economic zone|exclusive economic zone]] in the world. The nation's capital is Palikir, on Pohnpei Island, and its largest city is Weno, an island municipality in the Chuuk Lagoon. Each of its four states is centered on one or more main [[Volcanic island|volcanic islands]], and all but Kosrae include numerous outlying [[Atoll|atolls]].",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{
				"Conservation status",
