	{
		title = "Lebanon",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in West Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "West Asia" },
		aliases = { "Lebanese Republic" },
		summary = "**Lebanon**, officially the **Lebanese Republic**, is a country in the [[Levant]] region of [[West Asia]]. Situated at the crossroads of the [[Mediterranean basin|Mediterranean Basin]] and the [[Arabian Peninsula]], it is bordered by [[Syria]] to the north and east, [[Israel]] to the south, and the [[Mediterranean Sea]] to the west; [[Cyprus]] lies a short distance from the coastline. Lebanon has a population of more than five million and an area of 10452 km². [[Beirut]] is the country's capital and largest city.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Human habitation in Lebanon dates to 5000 BC. From 3200 to 539 BC, it was part of [[Phoenicia]], a maritime civilization that spanned the [[Mediterranean basin|Mediterranean Basin]]. In 64 BC, the region became part of the [[Roman Empire]] and the subsequent [[Byzantine Empire]]. After the seventh century, it came under the rule of different Arab Islamic caliphates, including the Rashidun, [[Umayyad Caliphate|Umayyad]] and [[Abbasid Caliphate|Abbasid]] caliphates. The 11th century saw the establishment of Christian Crusader states, which fell to the [[Ayyubid dynasty|Ayyubids]] and the [[Mamluk Sultanate|Mamluks]]. Lebanon came under [[Ottoman Empire|Ottoman]] rule in the early 16th century. Under Ottoman sultan Abdulmejid I, the first Lebanese proto-state, the Mount Lebanon Mutasarrifate, was established as a home for Maronite Christians, as part of the Tanzimat reforms.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Beirut]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Beirut]]" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Arabic]]" },
			{ "Languages", "Lebanese Arabic" },
			{ "People are called", "Lebanese" },
			{ "Government", "[[Unitary parliamentary republic]] under confessionalism" },
			{ "Established", "1516" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Lesotho",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southern Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "Southern Africa" },
		aliases = { "Kingdom of Lesotho" },
		summary = "**Lesotho**, officially the **Kingdom of Lesotho**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[Southern Africa]]. Surrounded by [[South Africa]], it is the largest of the three sovereign enclaves. Lesotho is located in the Maloti Mountains, with the highest peak in southern Africa. It has an area of over 30000 km², with a population of about 2.3 million. Its [[Capital city|capital]] and largest city is Maseru.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Lesotho was formed in 1824 by King Moshoeshoe I. Continuous encroachments by Dutch settlers made the King enter into an agreement with the United Kingdom to become a [[Protectorate|protectorate]] in 1868 and, in 1884, a [[Crown colony|crown colony]]. It achieved independence in 1966, and was subsequently ruled by the Basotho National Party (BNP) for two decades. Its constitutional government was restored in 1993 after seven years of military rule. King Moshoeshoe II was exiled in 1990 but returned in 1992 and was reinstated in 1995. One year later, Moshoeshoe II died and his son Letsie III took the throne, which he still holds. The Sotho ethnic group (also known as Basotho), from which the country derives its name, comprises 99.7% of the country's current population, making it one of the most ethnically homogeneous in the world. Their native language, Sesotho, is an official language along with [[English language|English]], [[Xhosa language|IsiXhosa]], and SiPhuthi.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Maseru" },
			{ "Largest city", "Maseru" },
			{ "Official languages", "Sesotho, [[South African English|English]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Mosotho (singular), Basotho (plural)" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Constitutional monarchy|parliamentary constitutional monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "18 March 1884" },
			{ "Area", "30,355 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Liberia",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in West Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "West Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Liberia" },
		summary = "**Liberia**, officially the **Republic of Liberia**, is a country on the [[West Africa|West African]] coast. It is bordered by [[Sierra Leone]] to its northwest, [[Guinea]] to its north, [[Ivory Coast]] to its east, and the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to its south and southwest. It has a population of around 5.5million and covers an area of 43000 sq mi. The official language is [[English language|English]], though over 20 indigenous languages are spoken, reflecting the country's ethnic and cultural diversity. The capital and largest city is [[Monrovia]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Liberia began in the early 19th century as a project of the American Colonization Society (ACS), which fomented the emigration of Black Americans from the [[United States]] to [[Africa]]. Between 1822 and the outbreak of the American Civil War in 1861, more than 15,000 freed and free-born [[African Americans]], along with 3,198 Afro-Caribbeans, relocated to Liberia. Gradually developing an Americo-Liberian identity, the settlers carried their culture and traditions with them while colonizing the indigenous population. Led by the Americo-Liberians, Liberia declared independence on July 26, 1847, which the U.S. did not recognize until February 5, 1862. Liberia was the first African republic to gain independence and is Africa's oldest continuously independent country. [[Ethiopian Empire|Ethiopia]] was never colonized but endured an Italian occupation from 1936 to 1941.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Official languages", "[[English language|English]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Liberian" },
			{ "Capital", "[[Monrovia]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "Monrovia" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Presidential system|presidential republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "January 7, 1822" },
			{ "Currency", "[[United States dollar]] (USD) Liberian dollar (LRD)" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Libya",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in North Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "North Africa" },
		aliases = { "State of Libya" },
		summary = "**Libya**, officially the **State of Libya**, is a country in the [[Maghreb]] region of [[North Africa]]. It borders the [[Mediterranean Sea]] to the north, [[Egypt]] to the east, [[Sudan]] to the southeast, [[Chad]] to the south, [[Niger]] to the southwest, [[Algeria]] to the west, and [[Tunisia]] to the northwest. With an area of almost 700,000 sq mi, Libya is the fourth-largest country in Africa and the [[Arab world]], and the 16th-largest in the world. The country claims 32,000 square kilometres of southeastern Algeria, south of the Libyan town of Ghat. The capital and largest city is [[Tripoli, Libya|Tripoli]], located in the northwest and containing over a million of Libya's seven million people.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Libya has been inhabited by Berbers since the late [[Bronze Age]] as descendants from Iberomaurusian and Capsian cultures. In classical antiquity, the [[Phoenicia|Phoenicians]] established city-states and trading posts in western Libya, while several [[Cyrenaica|Greek cities]] were established in the East. Parts of Libya were variously ruled by [[Ancient Carthage|Carthaginians]], [[Numidia|Numidians]], [[Achaemenid Empire|Persians]], and [[Ptolemaic Kingdom|Greeks]] before the entire region became a part of the [[Roman Empire]]. Libya was an early centre of Christianity. After the [[Fall of the Western Roman Empire|fall of the Western Roman Empire]], the area of Libya was mostly occupied by the Vandals until the 7th century when invasions brought Islam to the region. From then on, centuries of Arab migration to the Maghreb shifted the demographic scope of Libya in favour of [[Arabs]]. In the 16th century, the [[Spanish Empire]] and the Knights Hospitaller occupied Tripoli until [[Ottoman Empire|Ottoman]] rule began in 1551.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Tripoli, Libya|Tripoli]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Modern Standard Arabic|Arabic]]" },
			{ "Languages", "Libyan Arabic" },
			{ "People are called", "Libyan" },
			{ "Government", "[[Unitary state|Unitary]] republic under a provisional government (GNU)" },
			{ "Established", "1551" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Liechtenstein",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Microstate in Central Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Western Europe" },
		aliases = { "Principality of Liechtenstein" },
		summary = "**Liechtenstein**, officially the **Principality of Liechtenstein**, is a [[Landlocked country|doubly landlocked country]] in the Central European [[Alps]]. A microstate, it is located between [[Austria]] to the east and north-east and [[Switzerland]] to the north-west, west and south.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Formed in 1719, Liechtenstein became fully independent upon the dissolution of the [[German Confederation]] in 1866. Liechtenstein is a [[Monarchy|monarchy]] headed by the prince of Liechtenstein. Hans-Adam II, Prince of Liechtenstein has reigned over Liechtenstein since 1989. Liechtenstein is Europe's fourth-smallest country, with an area of just over 160 km² and a population of 41,389. It is the world's smallest country to border two countries. The official language of Liechtenstein is [[German language|German]]. Liechtenstein is divided into 11 municipalities. Its capital is Vaduz, and its largest municipality is Schaan. It is a member of the [[United Nations]], the European Free Trade Association, and the [[Council of Europe]]. It is not a member state of the [[European Union]], but it participates in both the [[Schengen Area]] and the European Economic Area.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Vaduz" },
			{ "Official languages", "German" },
			{ "People are called", "Liechtensteiner" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary parliamentary [[Constitutional monarchy|Semi-constitutional monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "23 January 1719" },
			{ "Area", "160.50 km²" },
			{ "Currency", "Swiss franc" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Lithuania",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Northern Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Northern Europe" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Lithuania" },
		summary = "**Lithuania**, officially the **Republic of Lithuania**, is a country in the Baltic region of [[Europe]]. It is one of three [[Baltic states]] and lies on the eastern shore of the [[Baltic Sea]], bordered by [[Latvia]] to the north, [[Belarus]] to the east and south, [[Poland]] to the south, and the Russian semi-exclave of [[Kaliningrad Oblast]] to the southwest, with a [[Maritime boundary|maritime border]] with [[Sweden]] to the west. Lithuania covers an area of 65300 km², and has a population of 2.9 million. Its capital and largest city is [[Vilnius]]; other major cities include Kaunas, Klaipėda, Šiauliai and Panevėžys.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Lithuanians are the titular nation, belong to the ethnolinguistic group of [[Balts]], and speak [[Lithuanian language|Lithuanian]]. For millennia, the southeastern shores of the Baltic Sea were inhabited by various [[Balts|Baltic tribes]]. In the 1230s, Lithuanian lands were united for the first time by Mindaugas, who formed the Kingdom of Lithuania on 6 July 1253. Subsequent expansion and consolidation resulted in the [[Grand Duchy of Lithuania]], which by the 14th century was the largest country in Europe. In 1386, the grand duchy entered into a [[De facto and de jure|de facto]] [[Personal union|personal union]] with the [[Crown of the Kingdom of Poland]]. The two realms were united into the [[Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth|Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth]] in 1569, forming one of the largest and most prosperous states in Europe.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Vilnius]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Lithuanian language|Lithuanian]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Lithuanian" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Semi-presidential system|semi-presidential republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "9 March 1009" },
			{ "Area", "65,300 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Luxembourg",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Western Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Western Europe" },
		aliases = { "Grand Duchy of Luxembourg" },
		summary = "**Luxembourg**, officially the **Grand Duchy of Luxembourg**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in Western Europe. It is bordered by Belgium to the west and north, Germany to the east, and France to the south and west. Its capital and most populous city, Luxembourg City, is one of the four institutional seats of the European Union and hosts several EU institutions, notably the Court of Justice of the European Union, the highest judicial authority in the EU.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"As part of the [[Low Countries]], Luxembourg has close historic, political, and cultural ties to Belgium and the Netherlands. Luxembourg's culture, people, and languages are greatly influenced by France and Germany: Luxembourgish, a Germanic language, is the only recognized [[National language|national language]] of the Luxembourgish people and of the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg; French is the sole language for legislation; and both languages along with German are used for administrative matters. With an area of 2586 km², Luxembourg is Europe's seventh-smallest country. In 2026, it had a population of 693,916, which makes it one of the least-populated countries in Europe, albeit with the highest population growth rate; foreign nationals account for almost half the population.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Symbol", "Coat of arms of Luxembourg" },
