	{
		title = "Madagascar",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "African island country in the Indian Ocean",
		tags = { "Africa", "East Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Madagascar" },
		summary = "**Madagascar**, officially the **Republic of Madagascar**, is an [[Island country|island country]] in the [[Indian Ocean]] that includes the island of Madagascar and numerous smaller peripheral islands. Lying off the southeastern coast of [[Africa]], it is the world's fourth-largest island, the second-largest island country, and the 46th-largest country overall. Its [[Capital city|capital]] and largest city is [[Antananarivo]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Following the prehistoric breakup of the [[Supercontinent|supercontinent]] [[Gondwana]], Madagascar split from Africa during the Early [[Jurassic]] period, around 180 million years ago, and from the [[Indian subcontinent]] approximately 90 million years ago. This isolation allowed native plants and animals to evolve in relative seclusion. As a result, Madagascar is a biodiversity hotspot and one of the world's 17 [[Megadiverse countries|megadiverse countries]], with over 90% of its wildlife being [[Endemism|endemic]]. The island has a subtropical to tropical maritime climate. Madagascar was first permanently settled during or before the mid-first millennium CE (roughly 500 to 700) by [[Austronesian peoples]], presumably arriving on outrigger canoes from present-day [[Indonesia]]. These were joined around the ninth century by [[Bantu peoples|Bantu]] groups crossing the [[Mozambique Channel]] from [[East Africa]].",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Antananarivo]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Antananarivo]]" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Malagasy language|Malagasy]], [[French language|French]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Malagasy" },
			{
				"Government",
				"Unitary [[Semi-presidential system|semi-presidential republic]] under a [[Military junta|military junta]]",
			},
			{ "Established", "c. 1540" },
			{ "Area", "592,796 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Malawi",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southeastern Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "East Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Malawi" },
		summary = "**Malawi**, officially the **Republic of Malawi**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[Southeast Africa]]. It is bordered by [[Zambia]] to the west, [[Tanzania]] to the north and northeast, and [[Mozambique]] to the east, south, and southwest. Malawi spans over 118484 km² and has a population of 22,224,282 (as of July 2025). [[Lilongwe]] is its capital and largest city.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The part of Africa now known as Malawi was settled around the 10th century by the Akafula, also known as the Abathwa. Later, the Bantu groups came and drove out the Akafula and formed various kingdoms such as the Maravi and Nkhamanga kingdoms, that flourished from the 16th century. The British Empire began to consolidate control of the area following the 1890 British Ultimatum against the Portuguese, who had claimed the area between [[Angola]] and [[Mozambique]] in the 1885 Pink Map. In 1891, the area was designated by the British as the British Central African Protectorate, renamed Nyasaland in 1907. In 1964, Nyasaland became independent under Prime Minister Hastings Banda and was renamed Malawi. Two years later, Banda became president by converting the country into a [[One-party state|one-party]] presidential republic. Banda was declared president for life in 1971.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Lilongwe]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Lilongwe]]" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[English language|English]]" },
			{ "National languages", "(none at national level)" },
			{ "Languages", "See list" },
			{ "People are called", "Malawian" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Presidential system|presidential republic]]" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Malaysia",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southeast Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "Southeast Asia" },
		summary = "**Malaysia** is a country in [[Southeast Asia]]. A [[Federation|federal]] [[Constitutional monarchy|constitutional monarchy]], it consists of 13 states and three federal territories, separated by the [[South China Sea]] into two regions: [[Peninsular Malaysia]] on [[Mainland Southeast Asia]] and East Malaysia on the island of [[Borneo]]. Peninsular Malaysia shares land and [[Maritime boundary|maritime borders]] with [[Thailand]], as well as maritime borders with [[Singapore]], [[Vietnam]], and [[Indonesia]]; East Malaysia shares land borders with [[Brunei]] and Indonesia, and maritime borders with the [[Philippines]] and Vietnam.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"[[Kuala Lumpur]] is the country's national capital, largest city, and the seat of the legislative branch of the federal government, while Putrajaya is the federal administrative capital, representing the seat of both the executive branch and the judicial branch of the federal government. With a population of over 34 million, it is the world's 43rd-most populous country. The country has its origins in the Malay kingdoms, which, from the 18th century on, became subject to the [[British Empire]], along with the British Straits Settlements protectorate. During [[World War II]], British Malaya, along with other nearby British and American colonies, was occupied by the [[Empire of Japan]]. Following three years of occupation, Malaya was briefly unified as the Malayan Union in 1946 until 1948 when it was restructured as the Federation of Malaya. The country achieved independence on 31 August 1957.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Kuala Lumpur]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Languages", "Malay" },
			{ "People are called", "Malaysian" },
			{ "Government", "Federal parliamentary constitutional [[Elective monarchy|elective monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "31 August 1957" },
			{ "Area", "330,803 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Maldives",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country in South Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "South Asia" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Maldives", "Maldive Islands" },
		summary = "The **Maldives**, officially the **Republic of Maldives**, and historically known as the **Maldive Islands**, is an [[Archipelagic state|archipelagic country]] in [[South Asia]], located in the [[Indian Ocean]], near the southeastern boundary of the [[Arabian Sea]]. The Maldives is located southwest of [[India]] and [[Sri Lanka]], about 750 km from the Asian continent's mainland. The Maldives' chain of 26 atolls stretches across the equator from Ihavandhippolhu Atoll in the north to Addu Atoll in the south.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The Maldives is the smallest country in Asia. Its land area is only 298 km², but this is spread over roughly 90000 km² of the sea, making it one of the world's most spatially dispersed sovereign states. With a population of 515,132 in the 2022 census, it is the second least populous country in Asia and the ninth-smallest country by area, but also one of the most densely populated countries. The Maldives has an average ground-level elevation of around 1.5 m above sea level, and a highest natural point of only 2.4 m, making it the world's lowest-lying country. Some sources state the highest point, Mount Villingili, as 5.1 m. Malé is the capital and the most populated city, traditionally called the \"King's Island\", where the ancient royal dynasties ruled from its central location. The Maldives has been inhabited for over 2,500 years.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Malé" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Languages", "Dhivehi" },
			{ "People are called", "Maldivian" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Presidential system|presidential republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "26 July 1965" },
			{ "Area", "298 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Mali",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in West Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "West Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Mali" },
		summary = "**Mali**, officially the **Republic of Mali**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[West Africa]]. It is the eighth-largest country in Africa and the 23rd largest country in the world, with an area of 1240192 km². It is bordered to the north by [[Algeria]], to the east by [[Niger]], to the northwest by [[Mauritania]], to the south by [[Burkina Faso]] and [[Ivory Coast]], and to the west by [[Guinea]] and [[Senegal]]. The population is about 25.20 million, 47.19% of which are estimated to be under age 15 in 2024. Its capital and largest city is [[Bamako]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"French was the official language until 2022, when it was replaced by 13 [[Languages of Africa|African languages]], with Bambara being the first language of the majority of the population. Mali's northern borders reach deep into the middle of the [[Sahara|Sahara Desert]]. Southern Mali, where the majority of inhabitants live, is in the Sudanian savanna and has the [[Niger River|Niger]] and [[Senegal River|Senegal]] rivers running through it. The economy centres on agriculture and mining with its most prominent natural resources including gold (which represents 80% of its exports) and cotton. Mali is one of the poorest and [[Least developed countries|least developed countries]] in the world. Mali was part of three successive powerful and wealthy West African empires that controlled [[Trans-Saharan trade|trans-Saharan trade]]: the [[Ghana Empire]], the [[Mali Empire]], and the [[Songhai Empire]].",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "People are called", "Malian" },
			{ "Capital", "[[Bamako]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "Bamako" },
