	{
		title = "Malta",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Mediterranean island country",
		tags = { "Europe", "Southern Europe" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Malta" },
		summary = "**Malta**, officially the **Republic of Malta**, is an [[Island country|island country]] located in the central [[Mediterranean Sea]]. It consists of an [[Archipelago|archipelago]] which is 80 km south of [[Italy]], 284 km east of [[Tunisia]], and 333 km north of [[Libya]]. The two official languages are Maltese and English; Maltese is recognised as the national language. The country's capital is Valletta, which is the smallest capital city in the [[European Union]] by both area and population.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Malta is the world's tenth-smallest country by area, the ninth-most densely populated, and the 166th most populated. Various sources consider the country to consist of a single urban region, for which it is often described as a [[City-state|city-state]]. The island of Malta has been inhabited since at least 6500 BC, during the [[Mesolithic]] period. Its location in the centre of the Mediterranean has historically given it great geostrategic importance, with multiple powers having ruled the islands and shaped its culture and society. These include the [[Phoenicia|Phoenicians]], [[Ancient Carthage|Carthaginians]], [[Ancient Greece|Greeks]], and [[Roman Empire|Romans]] in antiquity; the [[Arabs]], [[Normans]], and [[Crown of Aragon|Aragonese]] during the [[Middle Ages]]; and the Knights Hospitaller, [[French people|French]], and British in the [[Modern era|modern era]]. Malta came under [[Crown colony|British rule]] in the early 19th century and served as the headquarters for the British Mediterranean Fleet.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Valletta" },
			{ "Largest city", "Valletta" },
			{ "Official languages", "Maltese, [[English language|English]], Maltese Sign Language" },
			{ "National languages", "Maltese" },
			{ "Languages", "Italian (66% conversational)" },
			{ "People are called", "Maltese" },
			{ "Government", "[[Unitary parliamentary republic]]" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Marshall Islands",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🏝️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country in the Pacific Ocean",
		tags = { "Oceania", "Micronesia" },
		aliases = { "Republic of the Marshall Islands" },
		summary = "The **Marshall Islands**, officially the **Republic of the Marshall Islands**, is an [[Archipelagic state|archipelagic country]] in [[Oceania]]. The sovereign state lies west of the [[International Date Line]] and north of the [[Equator|equator]] in the [[Micronesia]] region of the Northwestern [[Pacific Ocean]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The territory consists of 29 coral [[Atoll|atolls]], five main islands, and 1,220 other very small ones, divided across two [[Archipelago|island chains]]: Ratak in the east and Ralik in the west. 98.47% of its territory is lagoon waters, the largest proportion of water to land of any sovereign state. The country shares [[Maritime boundary|maritime boundaries]] with Wake Island to the north, [[Kiribati]] to the southeast, [[Nauru]] to the south, and the [[Federated States of Micronesia]] to the west. The [[Capital city|capital]] and largest city is Majuro, home to approximately half of the country's population. The Marshall Islands are one of only four atoll-based nations, along with [[Kiribati]], The Maldives, and [[Tuvalu]].",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Majuro" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "Marshallese, [[English language|English]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Marshallese" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary parliamentary republic with an executive president" },
			{ "Established", "May 1, 1979" },
			{ "Area", "181.43 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Mauritania",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in West Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "West Africa" },
		aliases = { "Islamic Republic of Mauritania" },
		summary = "**Mauritania**, officially and also known as the **Islamic Republic of Mauritania**, is a country in the [[Maghreb]] region of [[West Africa]]. It is bordered by the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the west, [[Western Sahara]] to the north and northwest, [[Algeria]] to the northeast, [[Mali]] to the east and southeast, and [[Senegal]] to the southwest. By land area Mauritania is the 11th-largest country in Africa and the 28th-largest in the world; 90% of its territory is in the [[Sahara]] desert. Most of its population of 4.3 million live in the temperate south of the country; roughly a third of the population is concentrated in the capital and largest city, [[Nouakchott]], on the Atlantic coast.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The country's name derives from Mauretania, the [[Latin]] name for a region, to the north, in the ancient Mediterranean [[Maghreb]]. Mauretania extended from central present-day northern Algeria to the Atlantic, in Morocco. [[Berbers]] occupied what is now Mauritania by the beginning of the 3rd century CE. Groups of Arab tribes migrated to this area in the late 7th century, bringing with them Islam, [[Arab culture]], and the [[Arabic|Arabic language]]. In the early 20th century, Mauritania was colonized by France as part of [[French West Africa]]. It achieved independence in 1960. The country has since experienced recurrent coups and periods of military dictatorship. The 2008 Mauritanian coup d'état was led by General Mohamed Ould Abdel Aziz, who won subsequent presidential elections in 2009 and 2014.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Nouakchott]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Modern Standard Arabic|Arabic]]" },
			{ "Languages", "[[Arabic]] Pulaar Soninke Wolof" },
			{ "People are called", "Mauritanian" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary semi-presidential Islamic republic" },
			{ "Established", "28 November 1958" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Mauritius",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country in the Indian Ocean",
		tags = { "Africa", "East Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Mauritius" },
		summary = "**Mauritius**, officially the **Republic of Mauritius**, is an [[Island country|island country]] in the [[Indian Ocean]], located about 1100 nmi off the southeastern coast of [[Africa]], east of [[Madagascar]]. It includes the main island (also called Mauritius), as well as Rodrigues, Agaléga, and St. Brandon (Cargados Carajos shoals). The islands of Mauritius and Rodrigues, along with nearby [[Réunion]], are part of the Mascarene Islands. The main island of Mauritius, where the population is concentrated, hosts the capital and largest city, Port Louis. The country spans 2040 km² and has an [[Exclusive economic zone|exclusive economic zone]] covering approximately 580000 sqnmi.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'The 1502 Portuguese Cantino planisphere has led some historians to speculate that Arab sailors were the first to discover the uninhabited island around 975, naming it Dina Arobi. Called Ilha do Cirne or Ilha do Cerne on early Portuguese maps, the island was visited by Portuguese sailors in 1507. A [[Netherlands|Dutch]] fleet landed at what is now the Grand Port District and took possession of the island in 1598, renaming it after Maurice, Prince of Orange. Short-lived [[Kingdom of the Netherlands|Dutch]] attempts at permanent settlement took place over a century aimed at exploiting the local ebony forests, establishing [[Sugar|sugar]] and arrack production. When French colonisation began in 1715, the island was renamed "Isle de France". In 1810, the United Kingdom seized the island and under the Treaty of Paris, France ceded Mauritius and its dependencies to the United Kingdom.',
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Port Louis" },
			{
				"Official languages",
				"None (de jure) [[English language|English]], [[French language|French]] (de facto)",
			},
			{ "People are called", "Mauritian" },
			{ "Largest city", "Port Louis" },
			{ "Government", "[[Parliamentary republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "12 March 1968" },
			{ "Area", "2040 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Moldova",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Eastern Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Eastern Europe" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Moldova" },
		summary = "**Moldova**, officially the **Republic of Moldova**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[Eastern Europe]], with an area of 33,843 km² and a population of 2.38 million. Moldova is bordered by [[Romania]] to the west and [[Ukraine]] to the north, east, and south. The unrecognised breakaway state of [[Transnistria]] lies across the Dniester river on the country's eastern border with Ukraine. Moldova is a [[Parliamentary system|parliamentary]] democratic republic with its capital in Chișinău, the country's largest city and main cultural and commercial centre.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Most of Moldovan territory was a part of the Principality of Moldavia from the 14th century until 1812, when it was ceded to the [[Russian Empire]] by the [[Ottoman Empire]] (to which Moldavia was a vassal state) and became known as Bessarabia. In 1856, southern Bessarabia was returned to Moldavia, which three years later united with [[Wallachia]] to form Romania. Still, Russian rule was restored over the entire region in 1878. During the 1917 [[Russian Revolution]], Bessarabia briefly became an autonomous state within the [[Russian Republic]]. In February 1918, it declared independence and then integrated into Romania later that year following a vote of its assembly. The decision was disputed by [[Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic|Soviet Russia]], which in 1924 established, within the [[Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic|Ukrainian SSR]], a Moldavian autonomous republic on partially Moldovan-inhabited territories to the east of Bessarabia.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Chișinău" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Languages", "[[Romanian language|Romanian]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Moldovan" },
			{ "Government", "[[Unitary parliamentary republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "1346" },
			{ "Area", "33,843 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Monaco",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Microstate in Western Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Western Europe" },
		aliases = { "Principality of Monaco" },
		summary = "**Monaco**, officially the **Principality of Monaco**, is a [[Sovereign state|sovereign]] [[City-state|city-state]] and microstate in [[Western Europe]]. Situated on the French Riviera, it is a [[Enclave and exclave|semi-enclave]] bordered by [[France]] to the north, east, and west, with the [[Mediterranean Sea]] to the south; the [[Regions of Italy|Italian region]] of Liguria is about 15 km east. With a population of 38,423 living in an area of 2.08 km², Monaco is the second smallest sovereign state in the world, after [[Vatican City]], as well as the most densely populated. It also has the world's shortest national coastline of any non-landlocked nation, at 3.83 km. Fewer than 10,000 of its residents are Monégasque nationals.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Although [[French language|French]] is the [[Official language|official language]] of Monaco, [[Italian language|Italian]] and Monégasque are also widely spoken and understood. Monaco is governed under a form of [[Constitutional monarchy|semi-constitutional monarchy]], with Prince Albert II as [[Head of state|head of state]], who holds substantial political powers. The prime minister, who is the [[Head of government|head of government]], can be either a Monégasque or French citizen; the monarch consults with the Government of France before an appointment. Key members of the judiciary are detached French magistrates. The House of Grimaldi has ruled Monaco, with brief interruptions, since 1297. The state's sovereignty was officially recognised by the Franco-Monégasque Treaty of 1861, with Monaco becoming a full [[United Nations]] voting member in 1993. Despite Monaco's independence and separate foreign policy, its defence is the responsibility of France, notwithstanding two small military units.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Monaco ([[City-state|city-state]])" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[French language|French]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Monégasque" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary parliamentary [[Constitutional monarchy|semi-constitutional monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "8 January 1297" },
			{ "Area", "2.084 km²" },
			{ "Currency", "[[Euro]] ([[Euro sign|€]])" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Mongolia",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in East Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "East Asia" },
		summary = "**Mongolia** is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[East Asia]]. It is bordered by [[Russia]] to the north and [[China]] to the south and covers an area of 1564116 km², making it the 18th-largest country in the world and the second largest landlocked nation after [[Kazakhstan]], as well as the largest landlocked country that does not border an [[Endorheic basin|inland sea]]. With a population of 3.5 million, Mongolia is the world's most sparsely populated sovereign state, excluding [[Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic|Western Sahara]]. The country constitutes a significant portion of the [[Mongolian Plateau]], and its natural environment is characterized by grassy [[Steppe|steppe]], mountains to the north and west, and the [[Gobi Desert]] to the south.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"[[Ulaanbaatar]], the capital and largest city, is home to roughly half of the country's population. The territory of modern-day Mongolia has been ruled by various [[Nomadic empire|nomadic empires]], including the [[Xiongnu]], the Xianbei, the Rouran, the First Turkic Khaganate, the Second Turkic Khaganate, the [[Uyghur Khaganate]] and others. In 1206, [[Genghis Khan]] founded the [[Mongol Empire]], which became the largest contiguous land empire in history. His grandson [[Kublai Khan]] conquered [[China proper]] and established the [[Yuan dynasty]]. After the collapse of the Yuan, the [[Mongols]] retreated to Mongolia and resumed their earlier pattern of factional conflict, except during the era of Dayan Khan and Tumen Zasagt Khan. In the 16th century, Tibetan Buddhism spread to Mongolia. The [[Qing dynasty]] absorbed the country in the 17th century.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Official languages", "[[Mongolian language|Mongolian]] (Buriat, Khalkha, Oirat)" },
			{ "Languages", "Cyrillic, [[Mongolian script|Mongolian]]" },
			{ "People are called", "[[Mongols|Mongolian]], [[Mongols|Mongol]]" },
			{ "Capital", "[[Ulaanbaatar]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Semi-presidential system|semi-presidential republic]]" },
			{ "Area", "1,564,116 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Montenegro",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southeast Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Southern Europe" },
		summary = "**Montenegro** is a country in [[Southeastern Europe|Southeast Europe]], on the Balkan Peninsula. Its 25 municipalities have a total population of 633,158 people in an area of 13,883 km2 (5,360 sq mi). It is bordered by [[Serbia]] to the northeast, [[Bosnia and Herzegovina]] to the northwest, [[Kosovo]] to the east, [[Albania]] to the southeast, and [[Croatia]] to the west, and has a coastline along the [[Adriatic Sea]] to the southwest. The capital and largest city is Podgorica, while Cetinje is the Old Royal Capital and cultural centre.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Before the arrival of the [[Slavs|Slav peoples]] in the Balkans in the 6th and 7th centuries CE, the area now known as Montenegro was inhabited principally by people known as Illyrians. During the Early Medieval period, three principalities were located on the territory of modern-day Montenegro: Duklja, roughly corresponding to the southern half; Travunia, the west; and Rascia proper, the north. The Principality of Zeta emerged in the 14th and 15th centuries. From the late 14th century to the late 18th century, large parts of southern Montenegro were ruled by the Venetian Republic and incorporated into Venetian Albania. The name Montenegro was first used to refer to the country in the late 15th century. After falling under [[Ottoman Empire]] rule, Montenegro gained semi-autonomy in 1696 under the rule of the House of Petrović-Njegoš, first as a theocracy and later as a secular principality.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Podgorica" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "Montenegrin" },
			{
				"National languages",
				"[[Albanian language|Albanian]], [[Bosnian language|Bosnian]], [[Croatian language|Croatian]], [[Serbian language|Serbian]]",
			},
			{ "People are called", "Montenegrin" },
			{ "Government", "[[Unitary parliamentary republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "10th century" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Morocco",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in North Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "North Africa" },
		aliases = { "Kingdom of Morocco" },
		summary = "**Morocco**, officially the **Kingdom of Morocco**, is a country in the [[Maghreb]] region of [[North Africa]]. It has coastlines on the [[Mediterranean Sea]] to the north and the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the west, and has land borders with [[Algeria]] to the east; the [[Spain|Spanish]] [[Enclave and exclave|exclaves]] of [[Ceuta]], [[Melilla]] and Peñón de Vélez de la Gomera along the north, which it claims together with several small Spanish-controlled islands; and the disputed territory of [[Western Sahara]] to the south, partly occupied by Morocco since 1975. Morocco also claims to share a border with [[Mauritania]] through the disputed territory of Western Sahara. It has a population of approximately 37 million.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Its capital is [[Rabat]], while its largest city is [[Casablanca]]. The region constituting Morocco has been inhabited since the [[Paleolithic]] era, more than 300,000 years ago. The Moroccan state traces its origins to the establishment of the Idrisid dynasty by Idris I in 788, although its historical territories did not coincide with those of present-day Morocco; the country is regarded as one of the world's oldest continuously existing states. Morocco was subsequently ruled by a series of other independent dynasties, reaching its zenith as a [[Regional power|regional power]] in the 11th and 12th centuries, under the [[Almoravid dynasty|Almoravid]] and [[Almohad Caliphate|Almohad]] dynasties, both Berber kingdoms, when it controlled most of the [[Iberian Peninsula]] and the Maghreb.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Rabat]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Casablanca]]" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Modern Standard Arabic|Arabic]], Tamazight" },
			{ "People are called", "Moroccan" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary parliamentary [[Constitutional monarchy|semi-constitutional monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "788" },
			{ "Area", "446,550 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Mozambique",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southeastern Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "East Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Mozambique" },
		summary = "**Mozambique**, officially the **Republic of Mozambique**, is a country in [[Southeast Africa]] bordered by the Indian Ocean to the east, [[Tanzania]] to the north, [[Malawi]] and [[Zambia]] to the northwest, [[Zimbabwe]] to the west, and [[Eswatini]] and [[South Africa]] to the south and southwest. The [[Sovereign state|sovereign state]] is separated from the [[Comoros]], [[Mayotte]], and [[Madagascar]] through the [[Mozambique Channel]] to the east. The capital and largest city is [[Maputo]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Between the 7th and 11th centuries, a series of Swahili port towns developed in the area, which contributed to the development of a distinct Swahili culture and dialect. In the late medieval period, these towns were frequented by traders from Somalia, Ethiopia, [[Egypt]], Arabia, Persia, and [[India]]. The voyage of [[Vasco da Gama]] in 1498 marked the arrival of the [[Portuguese Empire|Portuguese]], who began a gradual process of colonisation and settlement in 1505. After over four centuries of Portuguese rule, Mozambique gained independence in 1975, becoming the People's Republic of Mozambique shortly thereafter. After only two years of independence, the country descended into an intense and protracted civil war lasting from 1977 to 1992.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Maputo]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Portuguese language|Portuguese]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Mozambican" },
			{ "Established", "1505–1975" },
			{ "Area", "801,590 km²" },
			{ "Currency", "Metical" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Myanmar",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southeast Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "Southeast Asia" },
		aliases = { "Republic of the Union of Myanmar", "Burma" },
		summary = "**Myanmar**, officially the **Republic of the Union of Myanmar** and also referred to as **Burma** (the official English name until 1989), is a country in northwest [[Southeast Asia]]. It is the largest country by area in [[Mainland Southeast Asia]] and has a population of about 55 million. It is bordered by [[India]] and [[Bangladesh]] to the northwest, [[China]] to the northeast, [[Laos]] and [[Thailand]] to the east and southeast, and the [[Andaman Sea]] and the [[Bay of Bengal]] to the south and southwest. The country's capital city is Naypyidaw, while its largest city is [[Yangon]] (formerly Rangoon).",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Early civilisations in the area included the Tibeto-Burman-speaking [[Pyu city-states]] in Upper Myanmar and the Mon kingdoms in Lower Myanmar. In the 9th century, the Bamar people entered the upper [[Irrawaddy River|Irrawaddy]] valley, and following the establishment of the [[Pagan Kingdom]] in the 1050s, the [[Burmese language]] and culture and Theravada Buddhism slowly became dominant in the country. The [[Pagan Kingdom]] fell to Mongol invasions, and several warring states emerged. In the 16th century, reunified by the Taungoo dynasty, the country became the largest empire in the [[History of Southeast Asia|history of Southeast Asia]] for a short period. The early 19th-century [[Konbaung dynasty]] ruled over an area that included modern Myanmar and briefly controlled Assam, the Lushai Hills, and Manipur as well.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Naypyidaw" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Yangon]]" },
			{ "Languages", "[[Burmese language|Burmese]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Burmese, Myanmar, Myanma" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary assembly-independent republic" },
			{ "Established", "23 December 849" },
			{ "Area", "676,579 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Namibia",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southern Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "Southern Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Namibia" },
		summary = "**Namibia**, officially the **Republic of Namibia**, is a country in [[Southern Africa]]. It borders the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the west, [[Zambia]] (via the Caprivi Strip) and [[Angola]] to the north, [[Botswana]] to the east, and [[South Africa]] to the south; in the northeast, approximating a quadripoint, [[Zimbabwe]] lies less than 200 m away along the [[Zambezi]] river near Kazungula, Zambia. Namibia's capital and largest city is [[Windhoek]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Namibia is the driest country in [[Sub-Saharan Africa|sub-Saharan Africa]], and has been inhabited since prehistoric times by the Khoi, [[San peoples|San]], Damara and Nama people. Around the 14th century, immigrating [[Bantu peoples]] arrived as part of the [[Bantu expansion]]. From 1600, the Owambo formed kingdoms, such as Ondonga and Oukwanyama. In 1884, the [[German Empire]] established rule over most of the territory, forming a colony known as German South West Africa. German rule ended during the First World War with a 1915 defeat by South African forces. In 1920, the [[League of Nations]] [[League of Nations mandate|mandated]] administration of the colony to South Africa. The National Party, elected to power in 1948 in South Africa, applied apartheid to what was then known as South West Africa.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Windhoek]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "English" },
			{ "People are called", "Namibian" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Semi-presidential system|semi-presidential republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "9 February 1990" },
			{ "Area", "825,615 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Nauru",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country in Oceania",
		tags = { "Oceania", "Micronesia" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Naoero" },
		summary = "**Nauru**, officially the **Republic of Naoero**, is an [[Island country|island country]] and microstate in the South Pacific Ocean. It lies within the [[Micronesia]] subregion of [[Oceania]], with its nearest neighbour being Banaba (part of [[Kiribati]]) about 300 km to the east. Yaren is its [[De facto and de jure|de facto]] capital.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"With an area of only 21 km², Nauru is the third-smallest country in the world, as well as the smallest member state of the [[Commonwealth of Nations]] by both area and population. Its population of about 12,000 is the world's third-smallest (not including colonies or overseas territories). Nauru is a member of the [[United Nations]], the Commonwealth of Nations, and the Organisation of African, Caribbean and Pacific States. First settled by Micronesians circa 1000 [[Common Era|BCE]], Nauru was annexed and claimed as a colony by the [[German Empire]] in the late 19th century. It was occupied by Australia during World War I and subsequently became a [[League of Nations mandate]] administered by Australia with New Zealand and United Kingdom as co-trustees. Nauru was occupied by Japan for three years during World War II and became a United Nations trust territory after the war's end.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Yaren ([[De facto and de jure|de facto]])" },
			{ "Official languages", "Nauruan, [[English language|English]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Nauruan, dei-Naoero (official)" },
			{ "Established", "31 January 1968" },
			{ "Area", "21 km²" },
			{ "Population", "11,680" },
			{ "Currency", "Australian dollar" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Nepal",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in South Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "South Asia" },
		aliases = { "Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal" },
		summary = "**Nepal**, officially the **Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[South Asia]]. It is mainly situated in the [[Himalayas]], but also includes parts of the [[Indo-Gangetic Plain]]. It borders the [[Tibet Autonomous Region]] of China to the north, and India to the south, east, and west, while it is narrowly separated from [[Bangladesh]] by the Siliguri Corridor, and from [[Bhutan]] by the [[States and union territories of India|Indian state]] of [[Sikkim]]. Nepal has a diverse geography, including fertile plains, subalpine forested hills, and eight of the world's ten highest mountains, including [[Mount Everest]], the highest point above mean sea level on Earth.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"[[Kathmandu]] is the nation's capital and its largest city. Nepal is a multi-ethnic, multi-lingual, multi-religious, and multi-cultural sovereign state, with [[Nepali language|Nepali]] as the official language. Parts of northern Nepal were intertwined with the culture of [[Tibet]]. The centrally located Kathmandu Valley is intertwined with the culture of Indo-Aryans, and was the seat of the prosperous Newar confederacy known as Nepal Mandala. The Himalayan branch of the ancient [[Silk Road]] was dominated by the valley's traders. The cosmopolitan region developed distinct traditional art and architecture. By the 18th century, the Gorkha Kingdom achieved the unification of Nepal. The Shah dynasty established the Kingdom of Nepal and later formed an alliance with the [[British Empire]], under its Rana dynasty of premiers.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Kathmandu]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Nepali language|Nepali]]" },
			{ "National languages", "All mother-tongues (see Languages of Nepal)" },
			{ "People are called", "Nepali, Nepalese" },
			{ "Government", "Federal [[Parliamentary republic|parliamentary republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "25 September 1768" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "New Zealand",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🎆",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country in the Pacific Ocean",
		tags = { "Oceania", "Australia and New Zealand" },
		summary = "**New Zealand** is an [[Island country|island country]] in the southwestern [[Pacific Ocean]]. It comprises two main landmasses—the [[North Island]] and the [[South Island]]—and over 700 smaller islands. It is the sixth-largest island country by area and lies east of [[Australia]] across the [[Tasman Sea]] and south of the islands of [[New Caledonia]], [[Fiji]], and [[Tonga]]. The country's varied topography and sharp mountain peaks, including the [[Southern Alps]], owe much to tectonic uplift and volcanic eruptions. New Zealand's capital city is Wellington, and its most populous city is [[Auckland]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The islands of New Zealand were the last large habitable land to be settled by humans. Between about 1280 and 1350, [[Polynesians]] began to settle in the islands and subsequently developed a distinctive Māori culture. In 1642, the Dutch explorer [[Abel Tasman]] became the first European to sight and record New Zealand. In 1769, the British explorer [[James Cook|Captain James Cook]] became the first European to set foot on and map New Zealand. In 1840, representatives of the United Kingdom and [[Māori people|Māori]] chiefs signed the Treaty of Waitangi, which paved the way for Britain's declaration of sovereignty later that year and the establishment of the Colony of New Zealand in 1841. Subsequently, a series of conflicts between the colonial government and Māori tribes resulted in the alienation and confiscation of large amounts of Māori land.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Wellington" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Auckland]]" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Westminster system|parliamentary constitutional monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "6 February 1840" },
			{ "Area", "263,310 km²" },
			{ "Currency", "New Zealand dollar" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Nicaragua",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Central America",
		tags = { "North America", "Central America" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Nicaragua" },
		summary = "**Nicaragua**, officially the **Republic of Nicaragua**, is a [[Sovereign state|country]] in [[Central America]], comprising 130,370 km². With a population of 7,097,329 as of 2026, it is the third-most populous country in Central America after [[Guatemala]] and [[Honduras]], and the largest by area in all of Central America.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'Nicaragua is bordered by Honduras to the north, the [[Caribbean Sea]] of the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the east, [[Costa Rica]] to the south, and the [[Pacific Ocean]] to the west. The country also shares maritime borders with [[El Salvador]] to the west and [[Colombia]] to the east. Nicaragua\'s largest city and national capital is [[Managua]], which is also the fourth-largest city in Central America, with a population of 1,055,247 as of December 2020. Nicaragua is known as "the breadbasket of Central America" due to having the most fertile soil and arable land in all of Central America. The official language is [[Spanish language|Spanish]], though different groups on the Caribbean coast (Mosquitia) speak their own languages and [[English language|English]].',
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Managua]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "Spanish" },
			{ "People are called", "Nicaraguan, Pinolero/Pinolera (colloquial)" },
			{ "Established", "15 September 1821" },
			{ "Area", "130,375 km²" },
			{ "Currency", "Córdoba" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Niger",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in West Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "West Africa" },
		aliases = { "Republic of the Niger" },
		summary = "**Niger**, officially the **Republic of the Niger**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[West Africa]]. It is a [[Unitary state|unitary state]] bordered by [[Libya]] to the northeast, [[Chad]] to the east, [[Nigeria]] to the south, [[Benin]] and [[Burkina Faso]] to the southwest, [[Mali]] to the west and [[Algeria]] to the northwest. It covers a land area of almost 1.27 million km², making it the sixth-largest country in Africa and the second-largest landlocked nation in Africa behind Chad. Over 80% of its land area lies in the [[Sahara]]. The capital [[Niamey]] is located in the southwest corner along the namesake [[Niger River]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Following the spread of Islam to the region, Niger was on the fringes of some states, including the [[Kanem–Bornu Empire]] and the [[Mali Empire]] before more significant parts of its territory became included in states such as the Sultanate of Agadez and the [[Songhai Empire]]. It was colonized by France during the Scramble for Africa as part of [[French West Africa]], becoming a distinct colony in 1922. Since obtaining independence in 1960, Niger has experienced five coups d'état and four periods of military rule. Niger's seventh and most recent constitution was enacted in 2010, establishing a multiparty, unitary semi-presidential system. Following the most recent coup in 2023, the country has been ruled by National Council for the Safeguard of the Homeland, a [[Military junta|military junta]], led by President Abdourahamane Tiani.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Official languages", "[[Hausa language|Hausa]]" },
			{ "Languages", "[[English language|English]] [[French language|French]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Nigerien" },
			{ "Capital", "[[Niamey]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "Niamey" },
			{
				"Government",
				"Unitary [[Semi-presidential system|semi-presidential republic]] under a [[Military junta|military junta]]",
			},
			{ "Area", "1,267,000 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Nigeria",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in West Africa",
		tags = { "Africa", "West Africa" },
		aliases = { "Federal Republic of Nigeria" },
		summary = "**Nigeria**, officially the **Federal Republic of Nigeria**, is a country in [[West Africa]] between the [[Sahel]] to the north and the [[Gulf of Guinea]] in the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the south. It covers an area of 923769 km². With a population of more than 242 million, it is the most populous country in [[Africa]], and the world's sixth-most populous country. Nigeria borders [[Niger]] in the north, [[Chad]] in the northeast, [[Cameroon]] in the east, and [[Benin]] in the west. Nigeria is a [[Federation|federal republic]] comprising 36 [[States of Nigeria|states]] and the Federal Capital Territory, where its capital, [[Abuja]], is located.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The largest city in Nigeria by population is [[Lagos]], one of the largest metropolitan areas in the world and the second largest in Africa. Nigeria is a [[Multinational state|multinational state]] inhabited by more than 250 ethnic groups speaking 500 distinct languages, all identifying with a wide variety of cultures. The three largest ethnic groups are the [[Hausa people|Hausa]], [[Yoruba people|Yoruba]], and Igbo together constituting over 60% of the total population. The [[Official language|official language]] is English. Nigeria's constitution ensures [[Freedom of religion|freedom of religion]]. The country is divided roughly in half between Muslims and Christians; indigenous religions, such as those native to the Igbo and Yoruba ethnicities, are in the minority. Nigeria has been home to several indigenous material cultures, pre-colonial states and kingdoms since the second millennium BC. The [[Nok culture]], c. 1500 BC, marks one of the earliest known civilisations in the region.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Abuja]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Lagos]]" },
			{ "Official languages", "English" },
			{ "Languages", "[[Hausa language|Hausa]], [[Yoruba language|Yoruba]], [[Igbo language|Igbo]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Nigerian" },
			{ "Government", "Federal [[Presidential system|presidential republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "1 January 1900" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Niue",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island country",
		tags = { "Countries", "Oceania" },
		summary = '**Niue** is a self-governing [[Island country|island country]] in [[Associated state|free association]] with [[New Zealand]]. It is situated in the South Pacific Ocean, is part of [[Polynesia]], and is predominantly inhabited by [[Polynesians]]. As one of the world\'s largest coral islands, Niue is nicknamed "The Rock", which comes from the traditional name "Rock of Polynesia".',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Niue's position is inside a triangle drawn between [[Tonga]], [[Samoa]], and the [[Cook Islands]]. It is 2400 km northeast of New Zealand, and 604 km northeast of Tonga. Niue's land area is about 261.46 km² and its population was 1,689 at the Census in 2022. The terrain of the island has two noticeable levels. The higher level is made up of a [[Limestone|limestone]] cliff running along the coast, with a plateau in the centre of the island reaching approximately 60 m above sea level. The lower level is a coastal terrace approximately 500 m wide and about 25–27 metres (80–90 feet) high, which slopes down and meets the sea in small cliffs. A [[Coral reef|coral reef]] surrounds the island; the only major break in the reef is in the central western coast, close to the capital, Alofi. Niue is subdivided into 14 villages (municipalities).",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Alofi" },
			{ "Official languages", "Niuean, [[New Zealand English|English]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Niuean" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary non-partisan parliamentary [[Constitutional monarchy|constitutional monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "19 October 1974" },
			{ "Area", "261.46 km²" },
			{ "Population", "1,681" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "North Korea",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in East Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "East Asia" },
		aliases = { "Democratic People's Republic of Korea", "DPRK" },
		summary = "**North Korea**, officially the **Democratic People's Republic of Korea** (**DPRK**), is a country in [[East Asia]]. It constitutes the northern half of the [[South Korea|Korean Peninsula]] and borders [[China]] and [[Russia]] to the north at the Yalu (Amnok) and Tumen rivers, and [[South Korea]] (officially the Republic of Korea) to the south at the Korean Demilitarized Zone (DMZ). The country's western border is formed by the [[Yellow Sea]], while its eastern border is defined by the [[Sea of Japan]]. [[Pyongyang]] is the capital and largest city.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The Korean Peninsula was first inhabited as early as the [[Lower Paleolithic]] period. Its [[Old Chosŏn|first kingdom]] was noted in Chinese records in the early 7th century BCE. Following the unification of the [[Three Kingdoms of Korea]] into Silla and Balhae in the late 7th century, Korea was ruled by the Goryeo dynasty (918–1392) and the Joseon dynasty (1392–1897). The succeeding [[Korean Empire]] (1897–1910) was annexed in 1910 into [[Empire of Japan|Japan]]. In 1945, after the [[Surrender of Japan|Japanese surrender]] at the end of World War II, Korea was divided into two zones along the 38th parallel, with the north occupied by the Soviet Union and the south occupied by the United States. In 1948, two separate governments were formed in Korea: the [[Eastern Bloc|Soviet-aligned]] Democratic People's Republic of Korea in the north, and the [[Western Bloc|Western-aligned]] Republic of Korea in the south. The North Korean invasion of South Korea in 1950 started the Korean War.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Pyongyang]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Korean language|Korean]] (Munhwaŏ)" },
			{ "Languages", "Chosŏn'gŭl (Hangul)" },
			{ "People are called", "North Korean, [[Koreans|Korean]]" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary [[Communist state|communist state]]" },
			{ "Established", "2 September 1945" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "North Macedonia",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Southeast Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Southern Europe" },
		aliases = { "Republic of North Macedonia" },
		summary = "**North Macedonia**, officially the **Republic of North Macedonia**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] in [[Southeastern Europe|Southeast Europe]]. It shares land borders with [[Greece]] to the south, [[Albania]] to the west, [[Bulgaria]] to the east, [[Kosovo]] to the northwest and [[Serbia]] to the north. It constitutes approximately the northern third of the larger geographical region of Macedonia. Skopje, the capital and largest city, is home to a quarter of the country's population of over 1.83 million. The majority of the residents are ethnic Macedonians, a [[South Slavs|South Slavic people]]. Albanians form a significant minority at around 25%, followed by Turks, Roma, Serbs, Bosniaks, Aromanians and a few other minorities.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"In [[Classical antiquity|classical antiquity]] most of present-day North Macedonia corresponded to the ancient regions of Paeonia and Pelagonia. In the late-6th century BC, most of the area was subjugated by the Persian Empire, and then incorporated into the [[Macedonia (ancient kingdom)|kingdom of Macedonia]] by the mid-4th century BC. [[Roman Empire|Rome]] conquered the region by the mid-2nd century BC and made it part of its larger province of Macedonia. The area remained part of the [[Byzantine Empire]], but was often raided and settled by [[Early Slavs|Slavic tribes]] beginning in the 6th century CE. Following centuries of contention between the Byzantine and [[First Bulgarian Empire|Bulgarian]] empires, it became part of the Serbian Empire in the mid-14th century, and then it was part of the [[Ottoman Empire]] from the late-14th century until the Balkan Wars (1912-1913), when it came under [[Kingdom of Serbia|Serbian]] rule. During the [[World War I|First World War]], the territory was ruled by Bulgaria.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Skopje" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "Macedonian, [[Albanian language|Albanian]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Macedonian" },
			{ "Government", "[[Unitary parliamentary republic]]" },
			{ "Established", "2 August 1944" },
			{ "Area", "25,436 km²" },
