		tags = { "Countries", "South America" },
		aliases = { "Republic of Suriname" },
		summary = "**Suriname**, officially the **Republic of Suriname**, is a country on the northern coast of [[South America]], also considered as part of the [[Caribbean]] and the [[West Indies]]. Situated [[Tropics|slightly north of the equator]], over 90% of its territory is covered by [[Rainforest|rainforest]], the second-highest proportion of forest cover in the world. Suriname is bordered by the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the north, [[French Guiana]] to the east, [[Brazil]] to the south, and [[Guyana]] to the west. The capital and largest city is Paramaribo, which is home to roughly half the population.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Suriname was inhabited as early as the fourth millennium BC by various [[Indigenous peoples of the Americas|Indigenous peoples]], including the Lokono, Kalina, and Wayana. Europeans arrived and contested the area in the 16th century, with the [[Dutch Republic|Dutch]] controlling much of the country's current territory by the late 17th century. After 1863, indentured servants were recruited mostly from [[British Raj|British India]] and the [[Dutch East Indies]]. In 1954, Suriname became a constituent country of the [[Kingdom of the Netherlands]]. On 25 November 1975, it became [[Independence|independent]] following negotiations with the Dutch government. Suriname continues to maintain close diplomatic, economic, and cultural ties with the Netherlands. Surinamese culture and society strongly reflect the legacy of Dutch colonial rule.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "Paramaribo" },
			{ "Largest city", "Paramaribo" },
			{ "Official languages", "Dutch" },
			{ "People are called", "Surinamese" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary assembly-independent presidential republic" },
			{ "Established", "15 December 1954" },
			{ "Area", "165,940 km²" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Sweden",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in northern Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Northern Europe" },
		aliases = { "Kingdom of Sweden" },
		summary = "**Sweden**, formally the **Kingdom of Sweden**, is a [[Nordic countries|Nordic country]] located on the [[Scandinavian Peninsula]] in [[Northern Europe]]. It borders [[Norway]] to the west and north, and [[Finland]] to the east, and shares a maritime border with [[Denmark]] to the south. At 450295 km² and with a population of 10.6 million, Sweden is the largest and most populous Nordic country, and is the fifth-largest country in Europe. Its capital and largest city is [[Stockholm]]. The population density is 25.5 PD/km2, and 88% of Swedes reside in urban areas, mostly in the southern and central portions of the country. Sweden's urban areas together cover 1.5% of its land area.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Sweden has a diverse climate owing to the length of the country, which ranges from 55°N to 69°N. Sweden has been inhabited since prehistoric times around 12,000 BC. The inhabitants emerged as the Geats and Swedes, who formed part of the sea-faring peoples known as the [[Vikings|Norsemen]]. A unified Swedish state was established during the late 10th century. In 1397, Sweden joined Norway and Denmark to form the Scandinavian [[Kalmar Union]], which Sweden left in 1523. When Sweden became involved in the Thirty Years' War on the Protestant side, an expansion of its territories began, forming the [[Swedish Empire]], which remained one of the [[Great power|great powers]] of Europe until the early 18th century. During this era Sweden controlled much of the Baltic Sea. Most of the conquered territories outside the Scandinavian Peninsula were lost during the 18th and 19th centuries.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Stockholm]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "Official languages", "[[Swedish language|Swedish]]" },
			{ "Languages", "Sámi, [[Finnish language|Finnish]], Meänkieli, [[Romani language|Romani]], [[Yiddish]]" },
			{ "People are called", "Swedish, Swede" },
			{ "Government", "Unitary parliamentary [[Constitutional monarchy|constitutional monarchy]]" },
			{ "Established", "By the late 10th century" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Switzerland",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in Central Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Western Europe" },
		aliases = { "Swiss Confederation" },
		summary = "**Switzerland**, officially the **Swiss Confederation**, is a [[Landlocked country|landlocked country]] located at the intersection of [[Central Europe|Central]], [[Western Europe|Western]], and [[Southern Europe]]. It is bordered by [[Germany]] to the north, [[France]] to the west, [[Austria]] and [[Liechtenstein]] to the east, and [[Italy]] to the south. Switzerland is geographically divided among the Swiss Alps, the Swiss Plateau, and the Jura Mountains; the Alps cover most of the country's territory, whereas the majority of its 9 million people are concentrated on the plateau, which hosts many of the largest cities and economic centres, including [[Zurich]], [[Geneva]], [[Basel]], Bern, Lausanne, Winterthur, and Lucerne.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'Switzerland is a [[Federal republic|federal republic]] composed of 26 cantons, with Bern serving as the federal city and the seat of the national government. The country encompasses four principal linguistic and cultural regions—German, French, Italian, and Romansh—reflecting a long-standing tradition of multilingualism and cultural pluralism. Swiss national identity nonetheless remains fairly cohesive, rooted in a shared historical background, common values such as [[Federalism|federalism]] and [[Direct democracy|direct democracy]], and [[Alps|Alpine]] symbolism. Swiss [[Nation|nationhood]] transcends language, ethnicity, and religion, leading to Switzerland being described as a ("nation of volition") rather than a conventional [[Nation state|nation state]]. The country originates from the [[Old Swiss Confederacy]] established in the [[Late Middle Ages]] as a defensive and commercial alliance; the Federal Charter of 1291 is considered the country\'s founding document.',
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "None ([[De facto and de jure|de jure]]); Bern ([[De facto and de jure|de facto]])" },
			{ "Largest city", "[[Zurich]]" },
			{
				"Official languages",
				"[[German language|German]] (62%), [[French language|French]] (23%), [[Italian language|Italian]] (8%), Romansh (0.5%)",
			},
			{ "Languages", "72.6% Swiss, 27.4% foreign nationals" },
			{ "People are called", "or" },
			{ "Government", "Federal assembly-independent directorial republic" },
			{ "Established", "1 August 1291" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Syria",
		category = "Country",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Country in West Asia",
		tags = { "Asia", "West Asia" },
		aliases = { "Syrian Arab Republic" },
		summary = "**Syria**, officially the **Syrian Arab Republic**, is a country in [[West Asia]] located in the [[Eastern Mediterranean]] and the [[Levant]]. It borders the [[Mediterranean Sea]] to the west, [[Turkey]] to the north and northwest, [[Iraq]] to the east and southeast, [[Jordan]] to the south, and [[Israel]] and [[Lebanon]] to the southwest. It is a [[Republic|republic]] under a provisional government and comprises 14 governorates. [[Damascus]] is Syria's capital and largest city. With a population of 26 million across an area of 185180 km², it is the 56th-most populous and 87th-largest country.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'The name "Syria" historically referred to the [[Syria (region)|region of Syria]], or known as Greater Syria and Syria-Palestine. The modern state encompasses the sites of several ancient kingdoms and empires, including the [[Ebla|Eblan]] civilization. Damascus was the capital of the [[Umayyad Caliphate|Umayyad Empire]] and later became an important political and administrative center, alongside [[Aleppo]], under the [[Ayyubid dynasty|Ayyubid]] and [[Mamluk Sultanate|Mamluk]] Sultanates and the [[Ottoman Empire]]. The modern Syrian state was established in the mid-20th century after centuries of Ottoman rule, as a French Mandate. The state represented the largest Arab state to emerge from the formerly [[Ottoman Empire|Ottoman]]-ruled Syrian provinces. It gained de jure independence as a [[Parliamentary republic|parliamentary republic]] in 1945 when the First Syrian Republic became a founding member of the [[United Nations]], an act which legally ended the French Mandate.',
			},
		},
		infobox = {
