		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Tallest single drop waterfall in the world, Venezuela",
		tags = { "Other hydrologic features", "Waterfalls" },
		summary = "**Angel Falls ** is a [[Waterfall|waterfall]] in [[Venezuela]]. It is the world's tallest uninterrupted waterfall, with a height of 979 m, and a plunge of 807 m. The waterfall drops over the edge of the Auyán-tepui mountain in the Canaima National Park, a [[World Heritage Site|UNESCO World Heritage Site]] in the Gran Sabana region of Bolívar State. The height figure, 979 m, mostly consists of the main plunge but also includes about 400 m of sloped cascade and [[Rapids|rapids]] below the drop and then a 30 m plunge downstream of these talus rapids.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
