		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🗺️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Collection of maps",
		tags = { "Basics", "Cartography" },
		summary = "An **atlas** is a collection of [[Map|maps]]; it is typically a bundle of maps of Earth or of a [[Continent|continent]] or region of [[Earth]]. Advances in [[Astronomy|astronomy]] have also resulted in atlases of the [[Celestial sphere|celestial sphere]] or of other planets.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Atlases have traditionally been bound into [[Book|book]] form, but today, many atlases are in [[Multimedia|multimedia]] formats. In addition to presenting [[Geography|geographical]] features and [[Border|political boundaries]], many atlases often feature geopolitical, social, religious, and economic statistics. They also have information about the map and places in it.",
			},
		},
		related = { "Remote sensing", "Surveying" },
	},
	{
		title = "Atlas Mountains",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "⛰️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "North African mountain range",
		tags = { "Land relief", "Africa" },
		summary = "The **Atlas Mountains** are a [[Mountain range|mountain range]] in the [[Maghreb]] in [[North Africa]]. They separate the [[Sahara]] from the [[Mediterranean Sea]] and the [[Atlantic Ocean]]; the mountain range stretches around 2500 km through [[Morocco]], [[Algeria]] and [[Tunisia]]. The mountains are associated with the [[Titans|Titan]] Atlas. The range's highest peak is Toubkal, in central Morocco, with an elevation of 4167 m. The Atlas Mountains are primarily inhabited by [[Berbers|Berber]] populations.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The terms for 'mountain' are Adrar and adras in some [[Berber languages]], and these terms are believed to be cognates of the toponym Atlas. The Atlas Mountains are home to a number of [[Animal|animals]] and [[Plant|plants]] which are mostly found within Africa but some of which can be found in Europe. Many of these species are [[Endangered species|endangered]] and a few are already [[Extinction|extinct]]. The weather is generally cool but summers are sunny, and the average temperature there is 25 °C.",
