		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Mountain range in northern Niger",
		tags = { "Land relief", "Africa" },
		aliases = { "Aïr Massif" },
		summary = "The **Aïr Mountains** or **Aïr Massif** (Tamajăq: Ayǝr; [[Hausa language|Hausa]]: Eastern Azbin, Western Abzin) is a triangular massif, located in northern [[Niger]], within the [[Sahara]]. Part of the West Saharan montane xeric woodlands [[Ecoregion|ecoregion]], they rise to more than 1800 m and extend over 84000 km². Lying in the midst of desert north of the 17th parallel, the Aïr plateau, with an average altitude between 500 and 900 m, forms an island of [[Sahel]] climate which supports a wide variety of life, many pastoral and farming communities, and dramatic geological and archaeological sites. There are notable archaeological excavations in the region that illustrate the prehistoric past of this region.",
