		tags = { "Basics", "Continents" },
		summary = "**Eurasia**, is the largest continental area on [[Earth]], comprising all of [[Europe]] and [[Asia]]. According to some models of the world, [[Physical geography|physio-graphically]], Eurasia is a single [[Supercontinent|supercontinent]]. The concept of Europe and Asia as distinct continents dates back to [[Classical antiquity|antiquity]], and is largely cultural, but their borders have historically been subject to change. For example, the ancient [[Greeks]] originally included [[Africa]] in Asia but classified Europe as separate land. Eurasia is connected to Africa at the [[Suez Canal]], and the two are sometimes combined to describe the largest contiguous landmass on Earth, [[Afro-Eurasia]].",
