		aliases = { "GAB" },
		summary = "The **Great Artesian Basin** (**GAB**) of [[Australia]] is the largest and deepest artesian basin in the world, extending over 1700000 km². Measured water temperatures range from 30 to 100 °C. The basin provides the only source of [[Fresh water|fresh water]] through much of inland Australia.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The basin underlies 22% of the Australian continent, including most of [[Queensland]], the south-east corner of the Northern Territory, north-eastern [[South Australia]], and northern [[New South Wales]]. It is 3000 m deep in places and is estimated to contain 64900 km³ of [[Groundwater|groundwater]]. The Great Artesian Basin Coordinating Committee (GABCC) coordinates activity between federal, state/territory, and local levels of government and community organisations.",
