	{
		title = "Greater Iran",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🏔️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Sociocultural region in West and Central Asia",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Greater Persia", "Iranosphere", "Persosphere" },
		summary = "**Greater Iran** or **Greater Persia**, also called the **Iranosphere**, the **Persosphere** or **Iranzamin**, is a term used to refer to a broader cultural sphere that has been influenced by [[Iranian peoples]] and [[Iranian languages]], and primarily includes the [[Iranian plateau]], the [[South Caucasus]], [[Central Asia]], the [[Indian subcontinent]], and as far east as the [[Tarim Basin]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'The regions which make up Greater Iran are defined by having long been under the rule of various [[History of Iran|Iranian empires]] and dynasties, during which the local populace gradually absorbed Iranian influence and assimilated it into their cultural and linguistic traditions; or those where a considerable Iranian population settled and retained their culture, such as in the areas surrounding the Iranian plateau. It is referred to as the "Iranian Cultural Continent" by [[Encyclopædia Iranica]]. Throughout the 16th to 19th centuries, Iran lost many of its historical territories that had been reconquered under the Iranian dynasties of the [[Safavid dynasty|Safavids]] and Qajars. The Ottoman–Persian Wars resulted in the loss of present-day [[Iraq]] to the [[Ottoman Empire]], as outlined in the Treaty of Amasya in 1555 and the Treaty of Zuhab in 1639.',
			},
		},
		related = { "White people in the United Kingdom" },
	},
	{
		title = "Greenland",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🏔️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Autonomous territory of Denmark",
		tags = { "Islands", "North America" },
		summary = "**Greenland** is an [[Autonomous administrative division|autonomous territory]] of the [[Danish Realm|Kingdom of Denmark]] and is the largest of the kingdom's three constituent parts by land area, the others being [[Denmark]] proper and the [[Faroe Islands]]. Citizens of Greenland are citizens of Denmark. They are thus citizens of the European Union (EU), although Greenland is [[Special territories of members of the European Economic Area|not part of the EU]]. It is the world's largest island and lies between the [[Arctic Ocean|Arctic]] and [[Atlantic Ocean|Atlantic]] oceans, east of the Canadian [[Arctic Archipelago]]. It shares a small 1.2 km border with Canada on Hans Island. The capital and largest city is Nuuk.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Kaffeklubben Island off the northern coast is the world's northernmost undisputed point of land – Cape Morris Jesup on the main island was thought to be so until the 1960s. Though a part of the continent of North America, Greenland was politically and culturally associated with the European kingdom of [[Norway]] from 986 until the early 15th century. From the 18th century, following the union of [[Denmark–Norway|Denmark and Norway]] and the establishment of the Nuuk settlement, Greenland gradually became associated with Denmark. Greenland has been inhabited at intervals over at least the last 4,500 years by [[Circumpolar peoples|circumpolar peoples]] whose forebears migrated there from what is now Canada.",
