		description = "Arm of the Baltic Sea",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "The **Gulf of Finland** is the easternmost arm of the [[Baltic Sea]]. It extends between [[Finland]] to the north and [[Estonia]] to the south, to [[Saint Petersburg]]—the second largest city of [[Russia]]—to the east, where the river [[Neva]] drains into it. Other major cities around the gulf include [[Helsinki]] and [[Tallinn]]. The eastern parts of the gulf belong to Russia, and some of Russia's most important oil harbors are located there, including Primorsk. As the seaway to [[Saint Petersburg]], the gulf is of considerable strategic importance to Russia. Some of the [[Baltic Sea|environmental problems affecting the Baltic Sea]] are at their most pronounced in the shallow gulf.",
		sections = {
			{ "Overview", "Proposals for an undersea Helsinki–Tallinn Tunnel through the gulf have been made." },
