		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'In [[Ancient Greece]] (ca. 8th BC – AD 6th c.), hegemony denotes the politico-military dominance of the hegemon [[City-state|city-state]] over other city-states. In the 19th century, hegemony denoted the "social or cultural predominance or ascendancy; predominance by one group within a society or milieu" and "a group or regime which exerts undue influence within a society." In [[International relations|international relations]] theories, hegemony is distinguished from empire as ruling only external but not internal affairs of other states.',
