		tags = { "Peninsulas", "Europe" },
		summary = "The **Iberian Peninsula**, also known as **Iberia**, is a [[Peninsula|peninsula]] in southwestern [[Europe]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Mostly separated from the rest of continental Europe by the [[Pyrenees]], the Iberian Peninsula includes Peninsular Spain and Continental Portugal, which together make up almost all of the region, as well as [[Andorra]], [[Gibraltar]], and a small part of [[Metropolitan France]]. With an area of approximately 583,254 km², and a population of roughly 53 million, it is the second-largest European peninsula by area, after the [[Scandinavian Peninsula]].",
