		title = "Jharkhand",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🏔️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "State in eastern India",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Jharkhand** is a landlocked [[States and union territories of India|state]] in eastern India. The state shares borders with the states of [[West Bengal]] to the east, [[Chhattisgarh]] to the west, [[Uttar Pradesh]] to the northwest, [[Bihar]] to the north and [[Odisha]] to the south. It is the 15th largest state by area, and the 14th largest by population. [[Hindi]] is the official language of the state. The city of [[Ranchi]] is its capital, and Dumka its sub-capital. The state is known for its waterfalls, hills and holy places; Baidyanath Dham, Parasnath, Dewri and Rajrappa are major religious sites. As per the 2011 census, Jharkhand is primarily rural, with about 24% of its population living in cities.",
