	{
		title = "Kingdom of Great Britain",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "👑",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Sovereign state in Western Europe (1707–1801)",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Great Britain**, officially the **Kingdom of Great Britain**, was a [[Sovereign state|sovereign state]] in [[Western Europe]] from 1707 to the end of 1800. The state was created by the 1706 Treaty of Union and ratified by the Acts of Union 1707, which united the [[Kingdom of England]] (including [[Wales]]) and the [[Kingdom of Scotland]] to form a single kingdom encompassing the whole island of [[United Kingdom|Great Britain]] and its outlying islands, with the exception of the [[Isle of Man]] and the [[Channel Islands]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'The [[Unitary state|unitary state]] was governed by a single parliament at the [[Palace of Westminster]], but the distinct legal systems—English law and Scots law—remained in use, as did distinct educational systems and religious institutions, namely the Church of England and the Church of Scotland remaining as the national churches of England and Scotland respectively. The formerly separate kingdoms had been in [[Personal union|personal union]] since the Union of the Crowns in 1603 when James VI of Scotland became [[Monarchy of the United Kingdom|King of England]] and King of Ireland. Since the reign of James, who had been the first to refer to himself as "king of Great Britain", a political union between the two mainland British kingdoms had been repeatedly attempted and aborted by both the [[Parliament of England]] and the Parliament of Scotland.',
			},
		},
		related = { "Statistics Indonesia" },
