		description = "River in southern India",
		tags = { "Rivers", "Asia" },
		summary = "The **Krishnā River** in the [[Deccan Plateau]] is the third-longest in India, after the Ganga and Godavari. It is also the fourth-largest in terms of water inflows and river basin area in India, after the Ganga, Indus and Godavari. The river, also called the Krishnaveni, is 1400 km long and flows for 282 kilometres in Maharashtra. It is a major source of [[Irrigation|irrigation]] in the Indian states of [[Maharashtra]], [[Karnataka]], [[Telangana]] and [[Andhra Pradesh]].",
