		tags = { "Lakes", "Africa" },
		summary = "**Lake Kariba** is the world's largest artificial lake and reservoir by volume. It lies 1300 km upstream from the mouth of the Zambezi river on the [[Indian Ocean]], bordering [[Zambia]] and [[Zimbabwe]]. Lake Kariba was filled between 1958 and 1963 following the completion of the Kariba Dam at its northeastern end, flooding the Kariba Gorge on the Zambezi River.",
