		description = "Lake in Zambia and Congo DR",
		tags = { "Lakes", "Africa" },
		summary = "**Lake Mweru** (also spelled Mwelu, Mwero) is a [[Fresh water|freshwater]] [[Lake|lake]] on the longest arm of [[Africa]]'s second-longest river, the [[Congo River|Congo]]. Located on the border between [[Zambia]] and [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]], it makes up 110 km of the total length of the Congo, lying between its Luapula River (upstream) and Luvua River (downstream) segments.",
