		tags = { "Lakes", "North America" },
		summary = "**Lake Superior** is a lake in central North America. The northernmost, westernmost, and highest of the [[Great Lakes]], Lake Superior straddles the [[Canada–United States border]] with the Canadian province of [[Ontario]] to the north and east and the U.S. states of [[Minnesota]] to the west and [[Michigan]] and [[Wisconsin]] to the south. It is the largest freshwater lake in the world by surface area and the third-largest freshwater lake by volume. It drains into [[Lake Huron]] via St. Marys River, then through the lower Great Lakes to the [[St. Lawrence River]] and ultimately the Atlantic Ocean.",
