		emoji = "🏞️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Lake in East-central Africa",
		tags = { "Lakes", "Africa" },
		summary = "**Lake Victoria** is one of the [[African Great Lakes]]. With a surface area of approximately 59947 km², Lake Victoria is Africa's largest lake by area, the world's largest [[Tropics|tropical]] lake, and the world's second-largest [[Fresh water|fresh water]] lake by surface area after [[Lake Superior]] in North America. In terms of volume, Lake Victoria is the world's ninth-largest continental lake, containing about 2424 km³ of water. Lake Victoria occupies a shallow [[Depression (geology)|depression]] in Africa. The lake has an average depth of 40 m and a maximum depth of 80 - 81 m. Its [[Drainage basin|catchment area]] covers 169858 km². The lake has a shoreline of 7142 km when digitized at the 1:25,000 level, with islands constituting 3.7% of this length.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The lake's area is divided among three countries: [[Tanzania]] occupies 49% (33,700 km²), [[Uganda]] 45% (31,000 km²), and [[Kenya]] 6% (4,100 km²). The lake is home to many species of fish which live nowhere else, especially [[Cichlid|cichlids]]. [[Invasive species|Invasive]] fish, such as the Nile perch, have driven many [[Endemism|endemic]] species to [[Extinction|extinction]].",
