		tags = { "Rivers", "South America" },
		summary = "The **Madeira River** is a major waterway in South America. It is estimated to be 1,450 km in length, while the Madeira-Mamoré is estimated near 3,250 km or 3,380 km in length depending on the measuring party and their methods. The Madeira is the biggest tributary of the [[Amazon River|Amazon]], accounting for about 15% of the water in the basin. A map from Emanuel Bowen in 1747, held by the David Rumsey Map Collection, refers to the Madeira by the pre-colonial, indigenous name Cuyari.",
