	{
		title = "Magnetosphere",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🏔️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Region around an astronomical object",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "In [[Astronomy|astronomy]] and [[Planetary science|planetary science]], a **magnetosphere** is a region of space surrounding an [[Astronomical object|astronomical object]], such as a planet or other object, in which [[Charged particle|charged particles]] are affected by that object's [[Magnetic field|magnetic field]]. It is created by a [[Astronomical object|celestial body]] with an active interior dynamo.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"In the space environment close to a planetary body with a dipole magnetic field such as Earth, the field lines resemble a simple magnetic dipole. Farther out, field lines can be significantly distorted by the flow of electrically conducting [[Plasma (physics)|plasma]], as emitted from the Sun (i.e., the [[Solar wind|solar wind]]) or a nearby star. Planets having active magnetospheres, like the Earth, are capable of mitigating or blocking the effects of solar radiation or cosmic radiation. Interactions of particles and atmospheres with magnetospheres are studied under the specialized scientific subjects of [[Plasma (physics)|plasma physics]], space physics, and aeronomy.",
			},
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Maharashtra",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🏔️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "State in western India",
		tags = { "Asia", "India" },
		summary = "**Maharashtra** is a [[States and union territories of India|state]] in the [[Western India|western]] peninsular region of [[India]] occupying a substantial portion of the [[Deccan Plateau]]. It is bordered by the [[Arabian Sea]] to the west, the Indian states of [[Karnataka]] and [[Goa]] to the south, [[Telangana]] to the southeast and [[Chhattisgarh]] to the east, [[Gujarat]] and [[Madhya Pradesh]] to the north, and the Indian [[Union territory|union territory]] of Dadra and Nagar Haveli and Daman and Diu to the northwest. Maharashtra is the second-most populous state in India, the third-most populous country subdivision in [[South Asia]], and the fourth-most populous in the world.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The region that encompasses the modern state has a history going back many millennia. Notable dynasties that ruled the region include the Asmakas, the Mauryas, the [[Satavahana dynasty|Satavahanas]], the Western Satraps, the Abhiras, the Vakatakas, the Chalukyas, the Rashtrakutas, the Western Chalukyas, the Seuna Yadavas, the Khaljis, the Tughlaqs, the Bahamanis and the [[Mughal Empire|Mughals]]. In the early 19th century, the region was divided between the Dominions of the Peshwa in the [[Maratha Empire|Maratha Confederacy]] and the Nizamate of Hyderabad. Early in the 19th century, the British [[East India Company]] defeated the Marathas and brought most of present-day Maharashtra under its control, both directly and indirectly through many princely states. After 1858, the British crown assumed control of the area from the company.",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
