			{ "Area", "22348.87 km²" },
			{ "Population", "3,000,000" },
			{ "Type", "Historical land" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Mount Elbrus",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "⛰️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Highest mountain of Russia and Europe",
		tags = { "Mountain peaks", "Europe" },
		summary = "**Mount Elbrus** is the highest mountain in [[Russia]] and [[Europe]]. It is a dormant [[Stratovolcano|stratovolcano]] rising 5642 m above sea level, and is the highest volcano in [[Eurasia]], as well as the tenth-most prominent peak in the world. It is situated in the [[Southern Russia|southern Russian]] republic of Kabardino-Balkaria in the western extension of [[North Caucasus|Ciscaucasia]], and is the highest peak of the [[Caucasus Mountains]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Elbrus has two summits, both of which are dormant volcanic domes. The taller, western summit is 5642 m; the eastern summit is 5621 m. The earliest recorded ascent of the eastern summit was on 10 July 1829 by a Circassian man named Khillar Khashirov, and the western summit in 1874 by a British expedition led by F. Crauford Grove and including Frederick Gardiner, Horace Walker and the Swiss guide Peter Knubel",
