		title = "Mount Pelée",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🌋",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Active volcano on the Caribbean island of Martinique",
		tags = { "Mountain peaks", "North America" },
		aliases = { "Mont Pelée" },
		summary = "**Mount Pelée** or **Mont Pelée** is an active stratovolcano at the northern end of [[Martinique]], an island and [[France|French]] overseas department in the Lesser Antilles Volcanic Arc of the [[Caribbean]]. Its volcanic cone is composed of stratified layers of hardened [[Volcanic ash|ash]] and solidified [[Lava|lava]]. Its most recent eruption was in 1932.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The main eruption, on 8 May 1902, left only three known survivors. Ludger Sylbaris survived because he was in a poorly ventilated, dungeon-like jail cell. Léon Compère-Léandre, living on the edge of the city, escaped with severe burns. The third was a young girl named Havivra Da Ifrile, who fled to a nearby sea cave in a boat, enduring burns from falling ash. In 2023, it was listed as [[UNESCO]] [[World Heritage Site|World heritage site]].",
			},
