		title = "Niger River",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "🏞️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Major river in West Africa",
		tags = { "Rivers", "Africa" },
		summary = "The **Niger River** is the main river of [[West Africa]], extending about 4180 km. Its [[Drainage basin|drainage basin]] is 2,117,700 km² in area. Its source is in the Guinea Highlands in south-eastern [[Guinea]] (Faranah Region) near the Sierra Leone border. It runs in a crescent shape through southwest [[Mali]] and through southwest [[Niger]], on the border with [[Benin]], and then through [[Nigeria]], discharging through a massive [[River delta|delta]], known as the Niger Delta, into the [[Gulf of Guinea]] in the [[Atlantic Ocean]]. The Niger is the 14th-longest river in the world, and the third-longest river in [[African diaspora|Africa]], exceeded by the [[Nile]], and the [[Congo River]]. Its main [[Tributary|tributary]] is the Benue River.",
