		summary = "**Northern Canada**, colloquially **the North** or **the Territories**, is the vast northernmost region of [[Canada]], variously defined by geography and politics. Politically, the term refers to the three [[Provinces and territories of Canada|territories of Canada]]: [[Yukon]], [[Northwest Territories]] and [[Nunavut]]. This area covers about 48 per cent of Canada's total land area, but has less than 0.5 per cent of Canada's population.",
