		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Pannonia** was a [[Roman province|province]] of the [[Roman Empire]] bounded on the north and east by the [[Danube]], on the west by Noricum and upper [[Roman Italy|Italy]], and on the south by Dalmatia and upper Moesia. It included the modern regions of western [[Hungary]], western [[Slovakia]], eastern [[Austria]], northern [[Croatia]], north-western [[Serbia]], northern [[Slovenia]], and northern [[Bosnia and Herzegovina]]. The northern and eastern boundary line of Pannonia was formed by the River [[Danube]].",
