	{
		title = "Queensland",
		category = "Geography",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🏔️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "State of Australia",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Queensland** is a state in northeastern [[Australia]], the second-largest and third-most-populous state in Australia. It is bordered by the Northern Territory, [[South Australia]] and [[New South Wales]] to the west, south-west and south, respectively. To the east, Queensland is bounded by the [[Coral Sea]] and the [[Pacific Ocean]]; to the state's north is the Torres Strait, separating the Australian mainland from [[Papua New Guinea]], and the [[Gulf of Carpentaria]] to the north-west. With an area of 1723030 km², Queensland is the world's sixth-largest subdivision of any country on earth; it is larger than all but 16 countries.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Due to its size, Queensland's geographical features and climates are diverse, and include [[Tropical rainforest|tropical rainforests]], [[River|rivers]], [[Coral reef|coral reefs]], [[Mountain range|mountain ranges]] and white sandy beaches in its [[Tropical climate|tropical]] and [[Humid subtropical climate|sub-tropical]] coastal regions, as well as [[Desert|deserts]] and [[Savanna|savanna]] in the [[Semi-arid climate|semi-arid]] and [[Desert climate|desert]] climatic regions of its [[Outback|interior]]. Queensland has a population of over 5.5 million, concentrated in South East Queensland, where nearly three in four reside. The capital and largest city in the state is [[Brisbane]], Australia's third-largest city and comprising fully half of the state's population. Ten of Australia's thirty largest cities are located in Queensland, the largest outside Brisbane being the Gold Coast, the Sunshine Coast, Townsville, Cairns, Ipswich, and Toowoomba. 24.2% of the state's population were born overseas. The state has the highest inter-state net migration in Australia.",
