		summary = "The **Sea of Marmara**, also known as the **Sea of Marmora**, the **Marmara Sea**, or **Propontis**, is a small inland sea entirely within the borders of [[Turkey]]. It links the [[Black Sea]] and the [[Aegean Sea]] via the [[Bosporus]] and [[Dardanelles]] straits, separating Turkey's European and [[Anatolia|Asian]] sides. It has an area of 11,350 km², and its dimensions are roughly 280 × 80 km, considered as the smallest sea in the world. Its greatest depth is 1,370 m.",
