		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🏝️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Island and region of Japan",
		tags = { "Islands", "Asia" },
		summary = "**Shikoku** is the smallest of the four main islands of [[Japan]]. It is 225 km long and between 50 and 150 km wide. It has a population of 3.5 million, the least of Japan's four main islands. It is south of [[Honshu]] and northeast of [[Kyushu]]. Shikoku's ancient names include Iyo-no-futana-shima, Iyo-shima, and Futana-shima, and its current name refers to the four former provinces that make up the island: Awa, Tosa, Sanuki, and Iyo.",
