		tags = { "Bodies of water", "Straits" },
		aliases = { "Dover Strait", "Dover Narrows" },
		summary = "The **Strait of Dover** or **Dover Strait**, historically known as the **Dover Narrows**, is the [[Strait|strait]] at the narrowest part of the [[English Channel]], marking the boundary between the Channel and the [[North Sea]], and separating [[United Kingdom|Great Britain]] from [[Continental Europe|continental Europe]]. The shortest distance across the strait, at 20.6 miles (33.2 km), is from the South Foreland, northeast of Dover in the English county of [[Kent]], to Cap Gris-Nez, a cape near to Calais in the French département of Pas-de-Calais. Between these points lies the most popular route for [[English Channel|cross-channel swimmers]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The entire strait is within the territorial waters of France and the United Kingdom, but a right of transit passage under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea allows vessels of other nations to move freely through the strait.",
