		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🏔️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "State of Brazil",
		tags = { "Americas", "Brazil" },
		summary = "**São Paulo** is one of the [[Federative units of Brazil|26 states]] of the Federative Republic of Brazil and is named after Saint Paul of Tarsus. It is located in the Southeast Region and is bordered by the states of [[Minas Gerais]] to the north and northeast, Paraná to the south, Rio de Janeiro to the east, and Mato Grosso do Sul to the west, in addition to the [[Atlantic Ocean]] to the southeast. It is divided into 645 municipalities. The total area is 248,219.481 km², which is equivalent to 2.9% of Brazil's surface. Its capital is the [[São Paulo|municipality of São Paulo]], which is Brazil's most populous city.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"With more than 44 million inhabitants in 2022, São Paulo is the [[Federative units of Brazil|most populous Brazilian state]] (around 22% of the Brazilian population), the world's 28th-most-populous [[Administrative division|sub-national entity]] and the most populous sub-national entity in the [[Americas]], and the fourth-most-populous political entity of [[South America]], surpassed only by the rest of the Brazilian federation, [[Colombia]], and [[Argentina]]. In addition, Arabs, Armenians, Chinese, Germans, Greeks, Japanese, Spanish and American Southerners also are present in the ethnic composition of the local population. Today's area corresponds to the state territory inhabited by Indigenous peoples from approximately 12,000 BC. In the early 16th century, the coast of the region was visited by [[Portuguese Empire|Portuguese]] and [[Spanish Empire|Spanish]] explorers and navigators.",
