		tags = { "Bodies of water", "Oceans and seas" },
		summary = "The **Tasman Sea** is a marginal sea of the South Pacific Ocean, situated between [[Australia]] and [[New Zealand]]. It measures about 2000 km across and about 2800 km from north to south. The sea was named after the Dutch explorer Abel Janszoon Tasman, who in 1642 was the first known European to cross it. British explorer Lieutenant [[James Cook]] later extensively navigated the Tasman Sea in the 1770s during his three voyages of exploration.",
