				"Overview",
				'The Tian Shan is sacred in Tengrism. Its second-highest peak is known as Khan Tengri, which can be translated as "Lord of the Spirits". At the 2013 [[World Heritage Committee|Conference on World Heritage]], the eastern portion of Tian Shan in western China\'s Xinjiang Region was listed as a [[World Heritage Site]]. The western portion in Kyrgyzstan, Kazakhstan, and Uzbekistan was then listed in 2016.',
