		summary = '**Victoria Falls** (Lozi: Mosi-oa-Tunya, "Thundering Smoke/Smoke that Rises"; Tonga: Shungu Namutitima, "Boiling Water") is a [[Waterfall|waterfall]] on the [[Zambezi]] River, located on the border between [[Zambia]] and [[Zimbabwe]]. It is one of the world\'s largest waterfalls, with a width of 1,708 m (5,604 ft). The region around it has a high degree of biodiversity in both plants and animals.',
