		summary = "**Vojvodina**, officially the **Autonomous Province of Vojvodina**, is an [[Autonomous administrative division|autonomous province]] in northern [[Serbia]]. It encompasses the historical and geographical regions of Bačka, Banat, Syrmia, and northernmost part of Mačva, lying to the north of the national capital [[Belgrade]] and the Sava and [[Danube]] rivers. Vojvodina has 1.7 million inhabitants, about a quarter of the country's population, and its administrative centre, Novi Sad, is the second largest city in Serbia.",
