		summary = "Geologically, a **volcanic island** is an [[Island|island]] of [[Volcano|volcanic]] origin. The term **high island** can be used to distinguish such islands from low islands, which are formed from sedimentation or the uplifting of [[Coral reef|coral reefs]] (which have often formed on sunken volcanoes).",
