		tags = { "Asia", "Central Asia and Iran" },
		aliases = { "White Sheep Turkomans" },
		summary = "The **Aq Qoyunlu** or the **White Sheep Turkomans** was a [[Turkoman (ethnonym)|Turkoman]], culturally [[Persianate society|Persianate]], Sunni Muslim tribal [[Confederation|confederation]]. Founded in the Diyarbakir region by Qara Yuluk Uthman Beg, they ruled parts of present-day eastern [[Turkey]] from 1378 to 1508, and in their last decades also ruled [[Armenia]], [[Azerbaijan]], much of [[Iran]], [[Iraq]], and [[Oman]] where the ruler of Hormuz recognised Aq Qoyunlu suzerainty. The Aq Qoyunlu empire reached its zenith under Uzun Hasan.",
