		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Gestation** is the period of development during the carrying of an [[Embryo|embryo]], and later fetus, inside viviparous [[Animal|animals]] (the embryo develops within the parent). It is typical for [[Mammal|mammals]], but also occurs for some non-mammals. Mammals during pregnancy can have one or more gestations at the same time, for example in a multiple birth.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The time interval of a gestation is called the gestation period. In obstetrics, gestational age refers to the time since the onset of the last menses, which on average is fertilization age plus two weeks.",
			},
		},
