	{
		title = "History of Central Asia",
		category = "History",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "📜",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "none",
		tags = { "History by continent and region" },
		summary = "The **history of Central Asia** concerns the history of the various peoples that have inhabited Central Asia. The lifestyle of such people has been determined primarily by the area's climate and geography. The [[Aridity|aridity]] of the region makes agriculture difficult and distance from the sea cut it off from much trade. Thus, few major cities developed in the region. [[Nomad|Nomadic]] horse peoples of the [[Steppe|steppe]] dominated the area for millennia.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Relations between the steppe nomads and the settled people in and around [[Central Asia]] were marked by conflict. The nomadic lifestyle was well-suited to warfare, and the steppe horse riders became some of the most militarily potent people in the world, due to the devastating techniques and ability of their horse archers. Periodically, tribal leaders or changing conditions would cause several tribes to organize themselves into a single military force, which would then often launch campaigns of conquest, especially into more 'civilized' areas. A few of these types of tribal coalitions included the [[Huns]]' invasion of [[Europe]], various [[Turkic peoples|Turkic]] migrations into [[Transoxiana]] and most notably the [[Mongols|Mongol]] conquest of much of [[Eurasia]].",
			},
