		tags = { "History by country", "Africa" },
		summary = "[[Egypt]], one of the world's oldest civilizations, was unified around 3150 BC by [[Narmer|King Narmer]]. It later came under Persian, Greek, Roman, and Arab rule before being joined to the [[Ottoman Empire]] in 1517. Controlled by Britain in the late 19th century, it became a republic in 1953. After several political transitions, Abdel Fattah el-Sisi currently leads the country.",
