		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "none",
		tags = { "History by country", "Asia" },
		summary = "The **history of Turkey**, understood as the history of the area now forming the territory of the Republic of Turkey, includes the history of both [[Anatolia]] (the Asian part of Turkey) and Eastern Thrace (the European part of Turkey). These two previously politically distinct regions came under control of the [[Roman Empire]] in the second century BC, eventually becoming the core of the Roman [[Byzantine Empire]]. For times predating the Ottoman period, a distinction should also be made between the history of the Turkic peoples, and the history of the territories now forming the Republic of Turkey.",
