	{
		title = "History of medicine",
		category = "History",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "💊",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "none",
		tags = { "History by subject matter", "History of science and technology" },
		summary = "The **history of medicine** is both a study of medicine throughout history as well as a multidisciplinary field of study that seeks to explore and understand medical practices, both past and present, throughout human societies.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The history of medicine is the study and documentation of the evolution of medical treatments, practices, and knowledge over time. Medical historians often draw from other [[Humanities|humanities]] fields of study including economics, health sciences, sociology, and [[Political science|politics]] to better understand the institutions, practices, people, professions, and social systems that have shaped medicine. Early medical traditions include those of Babylon, Egypt, China and India. Invention of the microscope was a consequence of improved understanding, during the Renaissance. Military doctors advanced the methods of trauma treatment and surgery. [[Public health]] measures were developed especially in the 19th century as the rapid growth of cities required systematic sanitary measures. Advanced research centers opened in the early 20th century, often connected with major hospitals.",
			},
		},
		related = { "History of spaceflight" },
