		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Empire of Korea", "Imperial Korea", "Taehan Cheguk" },
		summary = "The **Korean Empire**, officially the **Empire of Korea** or **Imperial Korea** in English and commonly called **Taehan Cheguk** in Korean, was a [[South Korea|Korean]] monarchical state proclaimed in October 1897 by King Gojong of the [[Joseon|Joseon dynasty]]. The empire lasted until the Japanese annexation of Korea in August 1910.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"During this period, Emperor Gojong oversaw the Gwangmu Reform, a partial modernization and westernization of Korea's military, economy, land system, education system, and various industries. In 1905, the Korean Empire became a [[Protectorate|protectorate]] of the [[Empire of Japan]]. After the Japanese annexation in 1910, the Korean Empire ceased to exist.",
