	{
		title = "Odrysian kingdom",
		category = "History",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "👑",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Union of Thracian tribes and kingdoms (5th century BC to 3rd century BC)",
		tags = { "Ancient", "Europe" },
		summary = "The **Odrysian kingdom** was an [[Classical antiquity|ancient]] Thracian state that thrived between the early 5th century [[Common Era|BC]] and the early 3rd / late 1st century BC. Located in present-day [[Bulgaria]], southeastern [[Romania]] (Northern Dobruja), northern Greece and European Turkey, it was a tribal amalgam dominated by the Odrysians that was the first large political entity to develop in the eastern [[Balkans]]. Before the foundation of Seuthopolis in the late 4th century it had no fixed capital.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The Odrysian kingdom was founded by king Teres I, exploiting the collapse of the Persian presence in Europe due to failed invasion of Greece in 480–79. Teres and his son Sitalces pursued a policy of expansion, making the kingdom one of the most powerful of its time. Throughout much of its early history it remained an ally of [[Classical Athens|Athens]] and even joined the Peloponnesian War on its side. Afterwards the kingdom disintegrated: southern and central Thrace were divided among three Odrysian kings, while the northeast came under the dominion of the kingdom of the Getae.",
