		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Mongol-led dynasty of China (1271–1368)",
		tags = { "Asia", "East Asia" },
		aliases = { "Great Yuan" },
		summary = "The **Yuan dynasty**, officially the **Great Yuan**, was a [[Mongols|Mongol]]-led imperial dynasty of China and a [[Successor state|successor state]] to the [[Mongol Empire]] after its division. It was established by Kublai (Emperor Shizu or Setsen Khan), the fifth khagan-emperor of the Mongol Empire from the [[Borjigin]] clan, and lasted from 1271 to 1368 AD. In [[History of China|Chinese history]], the Yuan dynasty followed the [[Song dynasty]] and preceded the [[Ming dynasty]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Although [[Genghis Khan]]'s enthronement as khagan in 1206 was described in [[Chinese language|Chinese]] as the [[Han Chinese|Han]]-style title of [[Emperor of China|emperor]] and the [[Mongol Empire]] had ruled territories including modern-day northern China for decades, it was not until 1271 that Kublai Khan officially proclaimed the dynasty in the traditional Han style, and the conquest was not complete until 1279 when the Southern Song dynasty was defeated in the Battle of Yamen. His realm was, by this point, isolated from the other Mongol-led khanates and controlled most of modern-day [[China]] and its surrounding areas, including modern-day [[Mongolia]]. It was the first dynasty founded by a non-Han ethnicity that ruled all of [[China proper]].",
			},
		},
		infobox = {
			{ "Era", "[[Post-classical history]]" },
			{
				"Conservation status",
				"Khagan-ruled division of the [[Mongol Empire]] Conquest dynasty of [[History of China|Imperial China]]",
			},
			{ "Government", "[[Monarchy]]" },
			{ "Capital", "Dadu (now [[Beijing]]), Shangdu (summer capital)" },
			{ "Languages", "ʼPhags-pa script" },
			{ "Currency", "Jiaochao banknotes, Chinese cash" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Yugoslavia",
		category = "History",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "📜",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "1918–1992 country in Southeast Europe",
		tags = { "Europe", "Eastern Europe" },
		summary = "**Yugoslavia** was a country in [[Central Europe]] and the [[Balkans]] that existed from 1918 to 1992. It came into existence following [[World War I]], under the name of the Kingdom of Serbs, Croats and Slovenes, from the merger of the [[Kingdom of Serbia]] with the provisional State of Slovenes, Croats and Serbs, and constituted the first union of South Slavic peoples as a [[Sovereign state|sovereign state]], following centuries of foreign rule over the region under the [[Ottoman Empire]] and the [[Habsburg monarchy]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Under the rule of the House of Karađorđević, the kingdom gained international recognition on 13 July 1922 at the Conference of Ambassadors in [[Paris]] and was renamed the [[Kingdom of Yugoslavia]] on 3 October 1929. Peter I was the country's first sovereign. Prince Paul headed the state as a prince regent until Alexander's son Peter II was declared of-age, which happened following the Yugoslav coup d'état in March 1941. Alexander I was the longest reigning of the three Yugoslav monarchs. The kingdom was invaded and occupied by the [[Axis powers]] in April 1941, marking the start of World War II in Yugoslavia. The Communist-led Partisan resistance went on to proclaim the Democratic Federal Yugoslavia and acquire the backing of the Allies at the Tehran Conference in late November 1943.",
			},
		},
		related = { "Russian Revolution of 1905" },
		infobox = {
			{ "Capital", "[[Belgrade]]" },
			{ "Largest city", "capital" },
			{ "People are called", "Yugoslav" },
			{ "Official languages", "Serbo-Croato-Slovene (before 1944) [[Serbo-Croatian]] (de facto; from 1944)" },
			{ "Currency", "Yugoslav dinar" },
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Zapotec civilization",
		category = "History",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🏞️",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Indigenous civilization that flourished in the Valley of Oaxaca in Mesoamerica",
		tags = { "Ancient", "Americas" },
		summary = "The **Zapotec civilization** (Be'ena'a \"The People that came from the clouds\"; c. 700 BC – AD 1521) is an [[Indigenous peoples|indigenous]] [[Pre-Columbian era|pre-Columbian]] civilization that flourished in the Valley of Oaxaca in [[Mesoamerica]]. Archaeological evidence shows that their culture originated at least 2,500 years ago. The Zapotec archaeological site at the ancient city of Monte Albán has monumental buildings, ball courts, tombs and grave goods, including finely worked gold jewelry. Monte Albán was one of the first major cities in Mesoamerica. It was the center of a Zapotec state that dominated much of the territory which today is known as the Mexican state of Oaxaca. The Zapotec peoples are their modern descendants.",
		related = { "Clovis culture" },
		infobox = {
			{ "Era", "Pre-classic – Late post-classic" },
			{ "Conservation status", "Zapotec–Mixtec Alliance" },
