		aliases = { "Rake" },
		summary = "A **rake** is a broom for outside use; a versatile horticultural implement consisting of a toothed bar fixed transversely to a handle, or tines fixed to a handle, and used to collect leaves, [[Hay|hay]], grass, and in [[Gardening|gardening]], for loosening the soil, light weeding and to make furrows, mounds and levelling, removing dead grass from lawns, and generally for purposes performed in agriculture by the [[Harrow (tool)|harrow]]. Depending on purpose, their materials and form will vary greatly.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Large mechanized versions of rakes are used in [[Agriculture|farming]], called hay rakes, are built in many different forms (e.g. star-wheel rakes, rotary rakes). Non mechanized farming may be done with various forms of a hand rake. Rakes can be a mechanical component of a Threshing machine.",
