		summary = "In [[Mathematics|mathematics]], the **associative property** is a property of some [[Binary operation|binary operations]] that rearranging the parentheses in an expression will not change the result. In [[Propositional logic|propositional logic]], **associativity** is a [[Validity (logic)|valid]] rule of replacement for expressions in logical proofs.",
		sections = {
