		tags = { "Statistics and probability" },
		summary = "**Bayesian inference** ( or ) is a method of [[Statistical inference|statistical inference]] in which [[Bayes' theorem]] is used to calculate a probability of a hypothesis, given prior [[Evidence|evidence]], and update it as more [[Information|information]] becomes available. Fundamentally, Bayesian inference uses a prior distribution to estimate posterior probabilities. Bayesian inference is an important technique in [[Statistics|statistics]], and especially in mathematical statistics. Bayesian updating is particularly important in the dynamic analysis of a sequence of data. Bayesian inference has found application in a wide range of activities, including [[Science|science]], [[Engineering|engineering]], [[Philosophy|philosophy]], [[Medicine|medicine]], [[Sport|sport]], [[Psychology|psychology]], and [[Law|law]].",
