		tags = { "Statistics and probability" },
		aliases = { "CLT" },
		summary = "In [[Probability theory|probability theory]], the **central limit theorem** (**CLT**) states that, under appropriate conditions, the [[Probability distribution|distribution]] of a normalized version of the sample mean converges to a [[Normal distribution|standard normal distribution]]. This holds even if the original variables themselves are not [[Normal distribution|normally distributed]]. There are several versions of the CLT, each applying in the context of different conditions.",
		sections = {
