		summary = 'Since no real number satisfies the above equation, i was called an [[Imaginary number|imaginary number]] by [[René Descartes]]. Despite the historical nomenclature, "imaginary" numbers are not fictitious: they are no less real mathematically than real numbers, and they are essential to the scientific description of the physical world.',
