		tags = { "Discrete mathematics" },
		summary = '**Discrete mathematics** is the study of mathematical structures that can be considered "discrete" (in a way analogous to discrete variables, having a one-to-one correspondence (bijection) with natural numbers), rather than "continuous" (analogously to [[Continuous function|continuous functions]]). Objects studied in discrete mathematics include [[Integer|integers]], [[Graph (discrete mathematics)|graphs]], and statements in [[Mathematical logic|logic]]. By contrast, discrete mathematics excludes topics in "continuous mathematics" such as [[Real number|real numbers]], [[Calculus|calculus]] or [[Euclidean geometry]].',
