		summary = "The **fundamental theorem of algebra**, also called **d'Alembert's theorem** or the **d'Alembert–Gauss theorem**, states that every non-constant single-variable [[Polynomial|polynomial]] with [[Complex number|complex]] [[Coefficient|coefficients]] has at least one complex root. This includes polynomials with real coefficients, since every real number is a complex number with its imaginary part equal to zero.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
