		tags = { "Geometry" },
		aliases = { "Homology" },
		summary = "In [[Mathematics|mathematics]], the term **homology**, originally introduced in [[Algebraic topology|algebraic topology]], has three primary, closely related usages. First, there is the homology of a chain complex, a sequence of [[Abelian group|abelian groups]], called homology groups, which are regarded as fundamental invariants of the chain complex. Secondly, when one can associate a chain complex to a different mathematical object, one can also associate its homology to that object. Distinct procedures of associating chain complexes to a given object are grouped into homology theories. Finally, homology is important in the study of [[Topological space|topological spaces]].",
		sections = {
