		tags = { "Statistics and probability" },
		summary = 'The **median** of a set of numbers is the value separating the higher half from the lower half of a data sample, a [[Statistical population|population]], or a [[Probability distribution|probability distribution]]. For a data set, it may be thought of as the "middle" value. The basic feature of the median in describing data compared to the mean (often simply described as the "average") is that it is not skewed by a small proportion of extreme values, and therefore provides a better representation of the center. Median income, for example, may be a better way to describe the center of the income distribution because increases in the largest incomes alone have no effect on the median.',
