		summary = 'In [[Numerical analysis|analysis]], **numerical integration** comprises a broad family of [[Algorithm|algorithms]] for calculating the numerical value of a definite [[Integral|integral]]. The term **numerical quadrature** (often abbreviated to **quadrature**) is more or less a synonym for "numerical integration", especially as applied to one-dimensional integrals. Some authors refer to numerical integration over more than one dimension as **cubature**; others take "quadrature" to include higher-dimensional integration.',
