		tags = { "Calculus and analysis" },
		summary = "In [[Mathematics|mathematics]], particularly in [[Complex analysis|complex analysis]], a **Riemann surface** is a connected one-dimensional complex manifold. These surfaces were first studied by and are named after [[Bernhard Riemann]]. Riemann surfaces can be thought of as deformed versions of the [[Complex plane|complex plane]]: locally near every point they look like patches of the complex plane, but the global [[Topology|topology]] can be quite different. For example, they can look like a [[Sphere|sphere]] or a [[Torus|torus]] or several sheets glued together.",
