		tags = { "Music genres and forms", "Western classical music" },
		summary = "**20th-century classical music** is Western art music that was written between 1901 and 2000, inclusive. Musical style diverged during the 20th century as it never had previously, so this century was without a dominant style. [[Modernism (music)|Modernism]], impressionism, and post-romanticism can all be traced to the decades before the turn of the 20th century, but can be included because they evolved beyond the musical boundaries of the 19th-century styles that were part of the earlier [[Common practice period|common practice period]]. Neoclassicism and expressionism came mostly after 1900.",
