	{
		title = "Big band",
		category = "Music",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🎸",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Music ensemble associated with jazz music",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		aliases = { "Jazz orchestra" },
		summary = 'A **big band** (historically referred to as **jazz orchestra**) is a type of [[Musical ensemble|musical ensemble]] of jazz music that usually consists of 10 or more musicians with four sections: [[Saxophone|saxophones]], trumpets, [[Trombone|trombones]], and a rhythm section. Big bands originated during the early 1910s and dominated [[Jazz|jazz]] in the early 1940s when [[Swing music|swing]] was most popular. The term "big band" is also used to describe a genre of music, although this was not the only style of music played by big bands.',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Big bands started as accompaniment for dancing the Lindy Hop. In contrast to the typical jazz emphasis on improvisation, big bands relied on written compositions and arrangements. They gave a greater role to bandleaders, arrangers, and sections of instruments rather than soloists.",
