		title = "Clarinet",
		category = "Music",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🎵",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Single-reed woodwind instrument",
		tags = { "Music", "Musical instruments" },
		summary = "The **clarinet** is a single-reed musical instrument in the woodwind family, with a nearly cylindrical bore and a flared bell.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Clarinets comprise a family of instruments of differing sizes and pitches. The clarinet family is the largest woodwind family, ranging from the BB♭ contrabass to the A♭ piccolo. German instrument maker Johann Christoph Denner is generally credited with inventing the clarinet sometime around 1700 by adding a register key to the chalumeau, an earlier single-reed instrument. Over time, additional keywork and airtight pads were added to improve the tone and playability. Today the clarinet is a standard fixture of the [[Orchestra|orchestra]] and [[Concert band|concert band]] and is used in [[Classical music|classical music]], military bands, klezmer, [[Jazz|jazz]], and other styles.",
