		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Family of musical instruments",
		tags = { "Music", "Musical instruments" },
		aliases = { "Horn" },
		summary = "A **horn** is any of a family of [[Musical instrument|musical instruments]] made of a tube, usually made of metal and often curved in various ways, with one narrow end into which the musician blows, and a wide end from which sound emerges. In horns, unlike some other [[Brass instrument|brass instruments]] such as the trumpet, the bore gradually increases in width through most of its length—that is to say, it is conical rather than [[Cylinder|cylindrical]]. In jazz and popular-music contexts, the word may be used loosely to refer to any [[Wind instrument|wind instrument]], and a section of [[Brass instrument|brass]] or [[Woodwind instrument|woodwind instruments]], or a mixture of the two, is called a horn section in these contexts.",
		related = { "Double bass", "Cello" },
	},
	{
		title = "Hymn",
		category = "Music",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🎶",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Religious song for the purpose of adoration or prayer",
		tags = { "Music", "Music genres and forms" },
		summary = 'A **hymn** is a type of [[Song|song]], and partially synonymous with devotional song, specifically written for the purpose of adoration or prayer, and typically addressed to a deity or deities, or to a prominent figure or personification. The word hymn derives from [[Greek language|Greek]] (hymnos), which means "a song of praise". A writer of hymns is known as a hymnist or hymnodist. The singing or composition of hymns is called **hymnody**. Collections of hymns are known as hymnals or hymn books. Hymns may or may not include instrumental accompaniment. Polyhymnia is the Greek goddess of hymns.',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Although most familiar to speakers of English in the context of Christianity, hymns are also a fixture of other world religions, especially on the Indian subcontinent (stotras). Hymns also survive from antiquity, especially from Egyptian and Greek cultures. Some of the oldest surviving examples of notated music are hymns with Greek texts.",
