		description = "1803/1805 composition by Ludwig van Beethoven",
		tags = { "Specific musical works", "Classical" },
		summary = "One of Beethoven's most celebrated works, the Eroica symphony is a large-scale composition that marked the beginning of the composer's innovative \"middle period\".",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Composed mainly in 1803–1804, the work broke boundaries in symphonic form, length, harmony, emotional and cultural content. It is widely considered a landmark in the transition between the [[Classical period (music)|Classical]] and the [[Romantic music|Romantic]] era. It is also often considered to be the first Romantic symphony. Beethoven first conducted a private performance on 9 June 1804, and later the first public performance on 7 April 1805.",
			},
