	{
		title = "Symphony No. 5 (Beethoven)",
		category = "Music",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🎼",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Musical composition by Ludwig van Beethoven",
		tags = { "Specific musical works", "Classical" },
		summary = 'The **Symphony No. 5** in C minor, Op. 67 (occasionally known as the **Fate Symphony**, ), is a [[Symphony|symphony]] composed by [[Ludwig van Beethoven]] between 1804 and 1808. It is one of the best-known of all symphonies and one of the most frequently played. First performed in Vienna in 1808, the work achieved its strong critical reputation not long afterward; E. T. A. Hoffmann described it as "one of the most important works of the time".',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'The 5th Symphony has 4 movements. It begins with a distinctive 4-note "short-short-short-long" motif, often characterized as "fate knocking at the door", the (fate motif). Sometimes this motif is remembered as "da-da-da-dum" or "da da da DUM".',
