		aliases = { "Charles Parker Jr.", "Yardbird" },
		summary = '**Charles Parker Jr.** (August 29, 1920 – March 12, 1955), nicknamed "**Bird**" or "**Yardbird**", was an American [[Jazz|jazz]] [[Saxophone|saxophonist]], bandleader, and composer. Parker was a highly influential soloist and leading figure in the development of [[Bebop|bebop]], a form of jazz characterized by fast tempos, [[Virtuoso|virtuosic]] technique, and advanced harmonies. He was a virtuoso and introduced revolutionary rhythmic and harmonic ideas into jazz, including rapid passing chords, new variants of altered chords, and chord substitutions. Parker primarily played the alto saxophone.',
