		tags = { "Performers", "Conductors" },
		summary = "**Herbert von Karajan** was an Austrian conductor. He was principal conductor of the Berlin Philharmonic for 34 years. Generally regarded as one of the greatest conductors of the 20th century, he was a controversial but dominant figure in European classical music from the mid-1950s until his death. Part of the reason for this was the large number of recordings he made and their prominence during his lifetime. By one estimate, he sold 200 million records.",
