		description = "Cushion for the head",
		tags = { "Household items", "Furniture and interior design" },
		summary = "A **pillow** is a soft fabric cushion used to support the head or body. Pillows are a form of bedding that supports the head and neck. Some pillows are purely decorative.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"In contemporary [[Western culture|western culture]], pillows are encased in a plain or patterned fabric envelope (known as a pillowcase). Inside is a soft stuffing from synthetic or natural materials. The word pillow comes from Middle English pilwe, from Old English pyle (akin to Old High German pfuliwi) and from Latin pulvinus. The first known use of the word pillow was before the 12th century.",
			},
