		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'Maslow was a [[Psychology|psychology]] professor at [[Cornell University]], Brooklyn College, Brandeis University, The New School for Social Research, and [[Columbia University]]. He stressed the importance of focusing on the positive qualities in people, as opposed to treating them as a "bag of symptoms". A [[Review of General Psychology]] survey, published in 2002, ranked Maslow as the tenth most cited psychologist of the 20th century.',
