		summary = "**Adrien-Marie Legendre** was a French [[Mathematician|mathematician]] who made numerous contributions to [[Mathematics|mathematics]]. Well-known and important concepts such as the Legendre polynomials and Legendre transformation are named after him. He is also known for his contributions to the method of least squares, and was the first to officially publish on it, though [[Carl Friedrich Gauss]] had discovered it before him.",
