		summary = "**Abu Ali al-Mansur**, better known by his [[Regnal name|regnal name]] **al-Hakim bi-Amr Allah**, was the sixth Fatimid caliph and 16th Ismaili imam (996–1021). Al-Hakim is an important figure in a number of Shia Ismaili sects, such as the world's 15 million Nizaris and 1–2 million Musta'lis, in addition to 2 million Druze.",
