	{
		title = "Alexander Pushkin",
		category = "Person",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Russian writer (1799–1837)",
		tags = { "Eastern Europe", "Russia" },
		aliases = { "Alexander Sergeyevich Pushkin" },
		summary = "**Alexander Sergeyevich Pushkin** was a Russian poet, playwright, and novelist of the Romantic era. He is considered by many to be the greatest Russian poet, as well as the founder of modern [[Russian literature]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'Pushkin was born into the [[Russian nobility]] in Moscow. His father, Sergey Lvovich Pushkin, belonged to an old noble family. Pushkin published his first poem at the age of 15, and was widely recognized by the literary establishment by the time of his graduation from the Tsarskoye Selo Lyceum. Upon graduation from the Lyceum, Pushkin recited his controversial poem "Ode to Liberty", one of several that led to his exile by Emperor Alexander I. While under strict surveillance by the Emperor\'s political police and unable to publish, Pushkin wrote his most famous play, Boris Godunov. His grand opus novel in verse [[Eugene Onegin]] was serialized between 1825 and 1832.',
			},
		},
