		summary = "**Antoine Maria Joseph Paul Artaud**, better known as **Antonin Artaud**, was a French artist who worked across a variety of media. He is best known for his writings, as well as his work in the theatre and cinema. Widely recognized as a major figure of the European [[Avant-garde|avant-garde]], he had a particularly strong influence on twentieth-century theatre through his conceptualization of the Theatre of Cruelty.",
