		summary = "**Aryabhata** or **Aryabhata I** (476–550 [[Common Era|CE]]) was the first of the major [[Mathematician|mathematician]]-[[Astronomer|astronomers]] and early physicist from the classical age of [[Indian mathematics]] and Indian astronomy. His works include the Āryabhaṭīya (which mentions that in 3600 Kali Yuga, 499 CE, he was 23 years old) and the Arya-siddhanta.",
