		description = "Italian Renaissance sculptor (c. 1386–1466)",
		tags = { "Other visual arts", "Sculptors" },
		aliases = { "Donato di Niccolò di Betto Bardi" },
		summary = "**Donato di Niccolò di Betto Bardi** (c. 1386 – 13 December 1466), known [[Mononym|mononymously]] as **Donatello**, was an Italian sculptor of the Renaissance period. Born in [[Republic of Florence|Florence]], he studied classical sculpture and used his knowledge to develop an Early Renaissance style of sculpture. He spent time in other cities, where he worked on commissions and taught others; his periods in Rome, Padua, and Siena introduced to other parts of Italy the techniques he had developed in the course of a long and productive career.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
