		category = "Person",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "French Impressionist artist (1834–1917)",
		tags = { "Western painters and illustrators", "Modern era" },
		summary = "**Edgar Degas** was a French [[Impressionism|Impressionist]] artist famous for his pastel drawings and oil paintings.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Degas also produced [[Wax|wax]] [[Sculpture|sculptures]], [[Printmaking|prints]], and drawings. Degas is especially identified with the subject of dance; more than half of his works depict dancers. Although Degas is regarded as one of the founders of [[Impressionism]], he rejected the term, preferring to be called a realist, and did not paint outdoors as many Impressionists did. In addition to ballet dancers and bathing women, Degas painted racehorses and racing jockeys, as well as portraits. His [[Portrait|portraits]] are notable for their psychological complexity and their portrayal of human isolation. At the beginning of his career, Degas wanted to be a history painter, a calling for which he was well prepared by his rigorous academic training and close study of classical Western art.",
