		tags = { "Eastern Europe", "Poland and Lithuania" },
		summary = "**Gediminas** (c. 1275 – December 1341) was Grand Duke of Lithuania from 1315 or 1316 until his death in 1341. Gediminas is traditionally considered to have been the founder of [[Vilnius]], the capital city of [[Lithuania]] (see: Iron Wolf legend). During his reign, he brought under his rule lands stretching from the [[Baltic Sea]] to the [[Black Sea]]. The Gediminids dynasty he founded and which is named after him came to rule over Poland, [[Kingdom of Hungary|Hungary]] and [[Kingdom of Bohemia|Bohemia]].",
