	{
		title = "Guru Dutt",
		category = "Person",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Indian filmmaker and actor (1925–1964)",
		tags = { "Asia", "India" },
		summary = "**Guru Dutt** was an Indian film [[Actor|actor]], director, producer, [[Choreography|choreographer]], and [[Writer|writer]]. He is regarded as one of the greatest filmmakers of Indian cinema. He was heavily influenced by [[Alfred Hitchcock]] in his initial films and later was compared with [[Orson Welles]] due to his works getting a legitimate amount of prominence amongst the cinephiles.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Dutt was lauded for his artistry, notably his usage of close-up shots, lighting, and depictions of melancholia. He directed a total of eight Hindi films, several of which have gained a cult following internationally. This includes Pyaasa (1957), which made its way onto Time magazine's 100 Greatest Movies list, as well as Kaagaz Ke Phool (1959), all of which are frequently listed among the greatest films in Hindi cinema. He was included among [[CNN]]'s \"Top 25 Asian Actors\" in 2012.",
