		description = "German physicist and mathematician (1824–1887)",
		tags = { "Physics", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Gustav Robert Kirchhoff" },
		summary = "**Gustav Robert Kirchhoff** was a German [[Physicist|physicist]] and [[Mathematician|mathematician]] who contributed to the fundamental understanding of [[Electrical network|electrical circuits]], [[Spectroscopy|spectroscopy]], and the emission of [[Black-body radiation|black-body radiation]] by heated objects. He coined the term black body in 1860.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Several different sets of concepts are named \"Kirchhoff's laws\" after him, which include [[Kirchhoff's circuit laws]], Kirchhoff's law of thermal radiation, Kirchhoff's diffraction formula, and Kirchhoff's law of thermochemistry. The Bunsen–Kirchhoff Award for spectroscopy is named after Kirchhoff and his colleague, Robert Bunsen.",
