		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "French civil engineer (1832–1923)",
		tags = { "Inventors and engineers", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Alexandre Gustave Eiffel" },
		summary = "**Alexandre Gustave Eiffel** was a French civil engineer. A graduate of École Centrale des Arts et Métiers, he made his name with various bridges for the French railway network, most famously the Garabit Viaduct. He is best known for the [[Eiffel Tower]], designed by his company and built for the 1889 Universal Exposition in Paris, and his contribution to building the [[Statue of Liberty]] (Liberty Enlightening the World) in New York. After his retirement from engineering, Eiffel focused on research into [[Meteorology|meteorology]] and [[Aerodynamics|aerodynamics]], making significant contributions in both fields.",
