		description = "Ancient Chinese writer, essayist and poet (768–824)",
		tags = { "Asia", "Eastern Asia" },
		aliases = { "Tuizhi", "Han Wengong" },
		summary = '**Han Yu**, [[Courtesy name|courtesy name]] **Tuizhi**, and commonly known by his [[Posthumous name|posthumous name]] **Han Wengong**, was an essayist, Confucian scholar, poet, and government official during the [[Tang dynasty]] who significantly influenced the development of [[Neo-Confucianism]]. Described as "comparable in stature to [[Dante Alighieri|Dante]], [[William Shakespeare|Shakespeare]] or Goethe" for his influence on the Chinese literary tradition, Han Yu stood for strong central authority in [[Politics|politics]] and orthodoxy in cultural matters.',
		sections = {
