		description = "German businessman and archaeologist (1822–1890)",
		tags = { "Historians and archaeologists", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Johann Ludwig Heinrich Julius Schliemann" },
		summary = "**Johann Ludwig Heinrich Julius Schliemann** was a German businessman and an influential [[Archaeology|archeologist]]. He was an advocate of the historicity of places mentioned in the works of [[Homer]] and an archaeological excavator of [[Troy|Hisarlık]], now presumed to be the site of [[Troy]], along with the [[Mycenaean Greece|Mycenaean]] sites Mycenae and Tiryns.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"His work lent weight to the idea that Homer's [[Iliad]] reflects historical events. Schliemann's excavation of nine layers of archaeological remains has been criticized as destructive of significant historical artefacts, including the layer that is believed to be the Homeric Troy.",
