		description = "French painter (1844–1910)",
		tags = { "Western painters and illustrators", "Modern era" },
		aliases = { "Henri Julien Félix Rousseau" },
		summary = "**Henri Julien Félix Rousseau** was a French [[Post-Impressionism|post-Impressionist]] painter in the Naïve or Primitive manner. He was also known as **Le Douanier** (the customs officer), a humorous description of his occupation as a toll and tax collector. He started painting seriously in his early forties; by age 49, he retired from his job to work on his art full-time.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Ridiculed during his lifetime by critics, he came to be recognised as a self-taught genius whose works are of high artistic quality. Rousseau's work exerted an extensive influence on several generations of [[Avant-garde|avant-garde]] artists.",
