		tags = { "Western Europe", "Germany and Austria" },
		aliases = { "Hermann Karl Hesse" },
		summary = "**Hermann Karl Hesse** was a German-Swiss poet and novelist, and winner of the 1946 Nobel Prize in Literature. His interest in [[Eastern philosophy|Eastern religious, spiritual, and philosophical traditions]], combined with his involvement with Jungian analysis, helped shape his literary work. His best-known novels include Demian, Steppenwolf, Siddhartha, Narcissus and Goldmund, and The Glass Bead Game, each of which explores an individual's search for authenticity, self-knowledge, and [[Spirituality|spirituality]].",
