		description = "Russian author (1870–1953)",
		tags = { "Eastern Europe", "Russia" },
		aliases = { "Ivan Alekseyevich Bunin" },
		summary = '**Ivan Alekseyevich Bunin** was a Russian writer. He became the first Russian writer awarded the [[Nobel Prize in Literature]], in 1933. He was noted for the strict artistry with which he carried on the classical [[Russian literature|Russian traditions in the writing]] of [[Prose|prose]] and [[Poetry|poetry]]. The texture of his poems and stories, sometimes referred to as "Bunin brocade", is considered to be one of the richest in the language.',
