		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"His work has been interpreted as [[Surrealism|Surrealist]] with a personal style, sometimes also veering into [[Fauvism]] and [[Expressionism]]. He was notable for his interest in the unconscious or the subconscious mind, reflected in his re-creation of the childlike. His sometimes difficult-to-classify works are also said to contain manifestations of [[Catalonia|Catalan]] pride. In 1975 a museum dedicated to his work, the Fundació Joan Miró, was established in his native city of [[Barcelona]] with another one being opened in 1981 in his adoptive city of Palma, Mallorca.",
