		tags = { "Western Europe", "France" },
		aliases = { "Jules Gabriel Verne" },
		summary = "**Jules Gabriel Verne** was a French novelist, [[Poet|poet]], and [[Playwright|playwright]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"His collaboration with the publisher Pierre-Jules Hetzel led to the creation of the Voyages extraordinaires, a series of bestselling adventure novels including Journey to the Center of the Earth (1864), Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas (1870), and Around the World in Eighty Days (1872). His novels are generally set in the second half of the 19th century, taking into account contemporary scientific knowledge and the technological advances of the time. In addition to his novels, he wrote numerous plays, short stories, autobiographical accounts, poetry, songs, and scientific, artistic and literary studies. His work has been adapted for film and television since the beginning of cinema, as well as for comic books, theater, opera, music and video games.",
