		category = "Person",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "German mathematician (1815–1897)",
		tags = { "Mathematicians", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Karl Theodor Wilhelm Weierstrass" },
		summary = '**Karl Theodor Wilhelm Weierstrass** was a German [[Mathematician|mathematician]] often cited as the "father of modern [[Mathematical analysis|analysis]]". Despite leaving university without a degree, he studied mathematics and trained as a school teacher, eventually teaching [[Mathematics|mathematics]], [[Physics|physics]], [[Botany|botany]] and [[Gymnastics|gymnastics]]. He later received an honorary doctorate and became professor of mathematics in Berlin.',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Among many other contributions, Weierstrass formalized the definition of the [[Continuous function|continuity of a function]] and [[Complex analysis|complex analysis]], proved the intermediate value theorem and the Bolzano–Weierstrass theorem, and used the latter to study the properties of continuous functions on closed bounded intervals.",
