		tags = { "Inventors and engineers", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Louis-Jacques-Mandé Daguerre" },
		summary = "**Louis-Jacques-Mandé Daguerre** was a French scientist, artist and photographer. He is recognized for his invention of the eponymous daguerreotype process of [[Photography|photography]]. He became known as one of the fathers of photography. Though he is most famous for his contributions to photography, he was also an accomplished [[Painting|painter]], scenic designer, and a developer of the diorama theatre.",
