		summary = "**Luigi Galvani** was an Italian physician, [[Physicist|physicist]], [[Biologist|biologist]] and [[Philosophy|philosopher]] who studied animal electricity. In 1780, using a frog, he discovered that the muscles of dead frogs' legs twitched when struck by an electrical spark. This was an early study of bioelectricity, following experiments by John Walsh and Hugh Williamson.",
