		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "American and French visual artist (1890–1976)",
		tags = { "Other visual arts", "Photographers" },
		summary = '**Man Ray** was an American-born, French-naturalized visual artist who spent most of his career in [[Paris]]. He was a significant contributor to the [[Dada]] and [[Surrealism|Surrealist]] movements, although his ties to each were informal. He produced major works in a variety of media but considered himself a painter above all. He was a photography innovator as well as a fashion and portrait photographer, and is noted for his work with photograms, which he called "rayographs" in reference to himself.',
