		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "French sociologist and anthropologist (1872–1950)",
		tags = { "Social scientists" },
		aliases = { "Marcel Israël Mauss" },
		summary = '**Marcel Israël Mauss** was a French [[Sociology|sociologist]] and [[Anthropologist|anthropologist]] known as the "father of French [[Ethnology|ethnology]]". The nephew of [[Émile Durkheim]], Mauss, in his academic work, crossed the boundaries between sociology and [[Anthropology|anthropology]]. Mauss had a significant influence upon [[Claude Lévi-Strauss]], the founder of structural anthropology. His most famous work is The Gift (1925).',
