		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "German banker (1744–1812)",
		tags = { "Businesspeople" },
		summary = '**Mayer Amschel Rothschild** (23 February 1743 or 1744 – 19 September 1812; also spelled Anschel) was a German Jewish banker and the founder of the [[Rothschild family|Rothschild banking dynasty]], which dominated international finance in Europe between the 1820s and the 1870s. Referred to as a "founding father of international finance", Rothschild was ranked seventh on the [[Forbes]] magazine list of "The Twenty Most Influential Businessmen of All Time" in 2005.',
