		description = "French inventor (1765–1833)",
		tags = { "Inventors and engineers", "Early modern" },
		aliases = { "Joseph Nicéphore Niépce" },
		summary = "**Joseph Nicéphore Niépce** was a French inventor and one of the pioneers of photography. Niépce developed heliography, a technique he used to create the world's oldest surviving products of a photographic process. In the mid-1820s, he used a primitive camera to produce the oldest surviving photograph of a real-world scene. Among Niépce's other inventions was the Pyréolophore, one of the world's first [[Internal combustion engine|internal combustion engines]], which he conceived, created, and developed with his older brother Claude Niépce.",
