		description = "French physicist and chemist (1859–1906)",
		tags = { "Physics", "Modern" },
		summary = "**Pierre Curie** (15 May 1859 – 19 April 1906) was a French [[Physicist|physicist]] and [[Chemist|chemist]], and a pioneer in [[Crystallography|crystallography]] and [[Magnetism|magnetism]]. He shared one half of the 1903 [[Nobel Prize in Physics]] with his wife, [[Marie Curie]], for their work on [[Radioactivity|radioactivity]]. With their win, the Curies became the first married couple to win a [[Nobel Prize]], launching the [[Nobel Prize|Curie family legacy]] of five Nobel Prizes.",
