	{
		title = "Raj Kapoor",
		category = "Person",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Indian actor and filmmaker (1924–1988)",
		tags = { "Asia", "India" },
		aliases = { "Ranbir Raj Kapoor" },
		summary = "**Ranbir Raj Kapoor**, popularly known as **Raj Kapoor** was an Indian actor and filmmaker who worked in Hindi cinema. He is considered to be one of the greatest and most influential actors and filmmakers in the history of Indian cinema. He has been referred to as The Greatest Showman of [[Cinema of India|Indian Cinema]] as well as The [[Charlie Chaplin]] of Indian Cinema.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Born in [[Peshawar]] as the eldest son of Prithviraj Kapoor of the Kapoor family, Raj Kapoor starred in and produced many films for which he received multiple accolades, including three National Film Awards and 11 Filmfare Awards in India. He was inspired by [[Charlie Chaplin]] and played characters based on The Tramp in films, such as Awāra (1951), Shree 420 (1955) and Mera Naam Joker (1970). His performance in Awāra was ranked as one of the \"Top-Ten Greatest Performances of All Time in World Cinema\" by [[Time (magazine)|Time]] magazine in 2005. His films Awāra (1951) and Boot Polish (1954) competed for the [[Palme d'Or|Palme d'Or prize]] at the [[Cannes Film Festival]] in [[Cannes Film Festival|1951]] and 1955. His films were global commercial successes in parts of Asia, the Middle East, the Caribbean, Africa, and the Soviet bloc. The [[Government of India]] honoured him with the [[Padma Bhushan]] in 1971 for his contributions to [[The arts|the arts]].",
			},
		},
