		tags = { "Mathematicians", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Julius Wilhelm Richard Dedekind" },
		summary = "**Julius Wilhelm Richard Dedekind** was a German [[Mathematician|mathematician]] who made important contributions to [[Number theory|number theory]], [[Abstract algebra|abstract algebra]] (particularly [[Ring theory|ring theory]]), and the axiomatic foundations of arithmetic. His best known contribution is the definition of [[Real number|real numbers]] through the notion of Dedekind cut. He is also considered a pioneer in the development of modern [[Set theory|set theory]] and of the [[Philosophy of mathematics|philosophy of mathematics]] known as logicism.",
