		summary = "**Samuel Finley Breese Morse** (April 27, 1791 – April 2, 1872) was an American inventor and painter. After establishing his reputation as a portrait painter, Morse, in his middle age, contributed to the invention of a [[Electrical telegraph|single-wire telegraph system]] based on European telegraphs. He was a co-developer and the namesake of [[Morse code]] in 1837 and helped to develop the commercial use of telegraphy.",
