		description = "Spanish neuroscientist (1852–1934)",
		tags = { "Biology", "Modern" },
		summary = "**Santiago Ramón y Cajal** was a Spanish neuroscientist, pathologist, and histologist specialising in neuroanatomy, and the [[Central nervous system|central nervous system]]. He and Camillo Golgi received the [[Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine]] in 1906. Ramón y Cajal was the first Spaniard to win a scientific [[Nobel Prize]]. His original investigations of the microscopic structure of the brain made him a pioneer of [[Neuroscience|modern neuroscience]].",
