		category = "Person",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Soviet-Russian filmmaker and theorist (1898–1948)",
		tags = { "Directors", "Europe" },
		summary = "Considered one of the greatest filmmakers of all time, he was a pioneer in the theory and practice of montage. He is noted in particular for his [[Silent film|silent films]] Strike (1925), Battleship Potemkin (1925) and October (1928), as well as the historical [[Epic film|epics]] Alexander Nevsky (1938) and Ivan the Terrible (1945/1958). In its decennial poll, the magazine [[Sight and Sound]] named his Battleship Potemkin the 54th-greatest film of all time.",
