		description = "Nepalese-Indian mountaineer (1914–1986)",
		tags = { "Explorers", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Namgyal Wangdi", "Sherpa Tenzing" },
		summary = "**Tenzing Norgay**, born **Namgyal Wangdi**, and also referred to as **Sherpa Tenzing**, was a Nepalese-Indian Sherpa mountaineer. On 29 May 1953, he and [[Edmund Hillary]] were the first confirmed to have reached the summit of [[Mount Everest]], as part of the 1953 British Mount Everest expedition. [[Time (magazine)|Time]] named Norgay one of the 100 most influential people of the 20th century.",
