		tags = { "Eastern Europe", "Russia and Ukraine" },
		aliases = { "Vladimir I Sviatoslavich", "Volodymyr I Sviatoslavych" },
		summary = '**Vladimir I Sviatoslavich** or **Volodymyr I Sviatoslavych**, given the epithet "**the Great**", was Prince of Novgorod from 970 and Grand Prince of Kiev from 978 until his death in 1015. The Catholic Church and the Eastern Orthodox Church both canonised him as **Saint Vladimir**.',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Vladimir's father was [[Sviatoslav I]] of the Rurik dynasty. Vladimir assembled a Varangian army and returned to depose Yaropolk in 978. By 980, Vladimir had consolidated his realm to the [[Baltic Sea]] and solidified the frontiers against incursions of [[Bulgarians]], Baltic tribes and Eastern nomads. Originally a follower of [[Slavic paganism]], Vladimir converted to Christianity in 988, and Christianized the Kievan Rus.",
			},
