		title = "Wolfgang Pauli",
		category = "Person",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "👤",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Austrian physicist (1900–1958)",
		tags = { "Physics", "Modern" },
		aliases = { "Wolfgang Ernst Pauli" },
		summary = '**Wolfgang Ernst Pauli** (25 April 1900 – 15 December 1958) was an [[Austria|Austrian]] theoretical [[Physicist|physicist]] and a pioneer of [[Quantum mechanics|quantum mechanics]]. In 1945, after having been nominated by [[Albert Einstein]], Pauli received the [[Nobel Prize in Physics]] "for the discovery of the Exclusion Principle, also called the [[Pauli exclusion principle|Pauli Principle]]". The discovery involved [[Spin (physics)|spin]] theory, which is the basis of a theory of the [[Matter|structure of matter]].',
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'To preserve the [[Conservation of energy|conservation of energy]] in [[Beta decay|beta decay]], Pauli proposed the existence of a small neutral particle, dubbed the "[[Neutrino|neutrino]]" by [[Enrico Fermi]], in 1930. Neutrinos were first detected in 1956.',
