		summary = "**Amaryllis** is the only [[Genus|genus]] in the subtribe Amaryllidinae ([[Tribe (taxonomy)|tribe]] Amaryllideae). It is a small genus of flowering [[Bulb|bulbs]], with two species. The better known of the two, Amaryllis belladonna, is a [[Native species|native]] of the Western Cape region of South Africa, particularly the rocky southwest area between the Olifants River Valley and Knysna.",
