		tags = { "Flowering plants", "Monocots" },
		summary = '**Arrowroot** is a [[Starch|starch]] obtained from the [[Rhizome|rhizomes]] (rootstock) of several tropical plants, traditionally Maranta arundinacea, but also Florida arrowroot from Zamia integrifolia, and tapioca from [[Cassava|cassava]] (Manihot esculenta), which is often labeled arrowroot. In Kenya, "arrowroot" refers to nduma, a plant known elsewhere as [[Taro|taro]]. Polynesian arrowroot or pia (Tacca leontopetaloides), from Palawan-Philippines arrowroot ("uraro/araro"), Guyana arrowroot (Dioscorea alata), Japanese arrowroot (Pueraria lobata), also called kudzu, and purple arrowroot Canna indica, are used in similar ways. In [[Odisha]], [[India]], it is called (paḷua).',
