		description = "Genus of trees",
		tags = { "Eudicots", "Fagales" },
		aliases = { "Betula" },
		summary = "A **birch** is a thin-leaved [[Deciduous|deciduous]] [[Hardwood|hardwood]] [[Tree|tree]] of the [[Genus|genus]] **Betula**, in the family Betulaceae, which also includes [[Alder|alders]], hazels, and hornbeams. It is closely related to the [[Beech|beech]]-[[Oak|oak]] family Fagaceae. The genus Betula contains 30 to 60 known taxa of which 11 are on the [[IUCN Red List|IUCN 2011 Red List]] of Threatened Species. They are typically short-lived pioneer species and are widespread in the [[Northern Hemisphere]], particularly in northern areas of temperate climates and in boreal climates. Birch wood is used for a wide range of purposes.",
		related = { "Hazelnut" },
