		description = "Common name of several species of fungi",
		tags = { "Fungi", "Edible fungi" },
		summary = "**Chanterelle** is the [[Common name|common name]] of several [[Species|species]] of agaricomycetous [[Mushroom|fungi]] in the genera Cantharellus, Craterellus, Gomphus and Polyozellus. These fungi are orange, yellow or white, meaty and funnel-shaped. On the lower surface, most species have rounded, forked folds that run almost all the way down the stipe, which tapers down from the cap. Many species emit a fruity aroma and often have a mildly peppery taste.",
		sections = {
