		tags = { "Monocots", "Poales" },
		aliases = { "Triticum aestivum", "Bread wheat" },
		summary = "**Common wheat** (**Triticum aestivum**), also known as **bread wheat**, is a cultivated [[Wheat|wheat]] species. It originated around 8,000 years ago, from the hybridization of an already existing domesticated variety of wheat and the wild goatgrass in the South Caucasus or southwestern Caspian area. About 95% of wheat produced worldwide is this species; it is the most widely grown of all crops and the [[Cereal|cereal]] with the highest monetary yield.",
