		description = "Flowering, deciduous trees, family Ulmaceae",
		tags = { "Eudicots", "Rosales" },
		aliases = { "Elms", "Ulmus" },
		summary = "**Elms** are [[Deciduous|deciduous]] and semi-deciduous trees comprising the genus **Ulmus** in the family Ulmaceae. They are distributed over most of the Northern Hemisphere, inhabiting the [[Temperate climate|temperate]] and [[Tropical climate|tropical]]-montane regions of North America and Eurasia, ranging southward in Western Asia to Iran, in Africa to Libya, and in Southeast Asia into Indonesia.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Elms are components of many kinds of natural [[Forest|forests]]. Moreover, during the 19th and early 20th centuries, many species and [[Cultivar|cultivars]] were also planted as ornamental street, garden, and park trees in [[Europe]], North America, and parts of the [[Southern Hemisphere]], notably [[Australasia]]. Some individual elms reached great size and age.",
