		tags = { "Flowering plants", "Monocots" },
		summary = "**Gladiolus** is a [[Genus|genus]] of [[Perennial|perennial]] cormous [[Flowering plant|flowering plants]] in the iris [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] (Iridaceae).",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"It is sometimes called the 'sword lily', but is usually called by its generic name (plural gladioli). The genus occurs in Asia, Mediterranean Europe, South Africa, and tropical Africa. The center of diversity is in the Cape Floristic Region. The genera Acidanthera, Anomalesia, Homoglossum, and Oenostachys, formerly considered distinct, are now included in Gladiolus.",
