		tags = { "Non-flowering plants", "Gymnosperms" },
		aliases = { "Junipers", "Juniperus" },
		summary = "**Junipers** are [[Conifer|coniferous]] trees and shrubs in the [[Genus|genus]] **Juniperus** of the cypress family Cupressaceae. Depending on the taxonomy, between 50 and 67 species of junipers are widely [[Species distribution|distributed]] throughout the [[Northern Hemisphere]] as far south as tropical [[Africa]], as far north as the [[Arctic]], and parts of [[Asia]] and [[Central America]]. The highest-known juniper forest occurs at an altitude of 4900 m in southeastern [[Tibet]] and the northern [[Himalayas]], creating one of the highest tree lines on earth.",
