		tags = { "Eudicots", "Fabales" },
		aliases = { "Common bean" },
		summary = "**Phaseolus vulgaris**, the **common bean**, is a herbaceous [[Annual plant|annual plant]]. Its botanical classification, along with other Phaseolus species, is as a member of the [[Legume|legume]] family, [[Fabaceae]]. It forms a green-leaved vine which produces [[Bean|beans]] inside of pods.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"All wild members of the species have a climbing habit, but many [[Cultivar|cultivars]] are classified either as bush beans or climbing beans, depending on their style of growth. In 2022, 28 million [[Tonne|tonnes]] of dry common beans were produced worldwide, led by India with 23% of the total. The common bean is the most consumed bean species in the world and is native to the Americas. It has many [[Cultivar|cultivars]]. In addition to the beans, the [[Green bean|unripe green pods]] are used for food. The leaf is occasionally used as a [[Leaf vegetable|vegetable]] and the straw as [[Fodder|fodder]].",
