		tags = { "Non-flowering plants", "Gymnosperms" },
		aliases = { "Pines", "Pinus" },
		summary = "**Pines** (genus **Pinus**) are a genus of conifers in the family Pinaceae. Pinus is the sole genus in the [[Subfamily|subfamily]] **Pinoideae**. The species are [[Tree|trees]] or shrubs with their leaves in bunches, usually of 2 to 5 needles. The seeds are carried on woody cones, with two seeds to each cone scale.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Pines are widely [[Species distribution|distributed]] in the [[Northern Hemisphere]]; they occupy large areas of [[Taiga|taiga]] (boreal forest), but are found in many habitats, including the [[Mediterranean basin|Mediterranean Basin]], and dry tropical forests in [[Southeast Asia|southeast Asia]] and [[Central America]]. Some are fire-resistant or fire-dependent. Pine trees provide one of the most extensively used types of [[Lumber|timber]].",
