		summary = "**Puya** is a [[Genus|genus]] of the [[Botany|botanical]] family [[Bromeliaceae]]. It is the sole genus of the subfamily **Puyoideae**, and is composed of 226 species. These terrestrial plants are native to the [[Andes]] Mountains of [[South America]] and southern [[Central America]]. Many of the species are monocarpic, with the parent plant dying after one flower and seed production event.",
