		tags = { "Anatomy and morphology", "Plant anatomy" },
		aliases = { "Roots" },
		summary = "In [[Vascular plant|vascular plants]], the **roots** are the organs of a plant that are modified to provide anchorage for the plant and take in water and nutrients into the plant body, which allows plants to grow taller and faster. They are most often below the surface of the [[Soil|soil]], but roots can also be aerial or aerating, that is, growing up above the ground or especially above water.",
