		description = "Root vegetable in the Brassica family",
		tags = { "Eudicots", "Brassicales" },
		aliases = { "Swede", "Brassica napus" },
		summary = "**Rutabaga** or **swede** ([[British English]] and some [[English in the Commonwealth of Nations|Commonwealth English]]) is a [[Root vegetable|root vegetable]], a form of **Brassica napus** (which also includes rapeseed). Other names include **Swedish turnip**, **neep** ([[Scots language|Scots]]), and **turnip** (Scottish and Canadian English, Irish English, Cornish English and Manx English, as well as some dialects of English in Northern England, New England English, and [[Australian English]]). However, elsewhere, the name turnip usually refers to the related white turnip.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The species B. napus originated as a hybrid between the [[Cabbage|cabbage]] (B. oleracea) and the turnip (B. rapa). Rutabaga roots are eaten as human food in various ways, and the leaves can be eaten as a [[Leaf vegetable|leaf vegetable]]. The roots and tops are also used for livestock, fed directly in the winter or [[Forage|foraged]] in the field during the other seasons.",
