		tags = { "Flowering plants", "Monocots" },
		summary = "**Taro** is a [[Root vegetable|root vegetable]]. It is the most widely cultivated species of several plants in the family [[Araceae]] that are used as vegetables for their corms, leaves, stems and petioles. Taro corms are a food staple in African, [[Caribbean]], [[Oceania|Oceanian]], [[East Asia|East Asian]], [[Southeast Asia|Southeast Asian]] and [[South Asia|South Asian]] cultures (similar to [[Yam (vegetable)|yams]]).",
