		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🌿",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Culinary herb",
		tags = { "Eudicots", "Lamiales" },
		summary = "**Thyme** is a culinary herb consisting of the dried aerial parts of some members of the genus Thymus of [[Flowering plant|flowering plants]] in the mint family [[Lamiaceae]]. Thymes are native to [[Mediterranean Sea|Mediterranean]] countries in [[North Africa]], [[Levant]] and [[Southern Europe]]. Thymes have culinary, medicinal, and [[Ornamental plant|ornamental]] uses. The species most commonly cultivated and used for culinary purposes is Thymus vulgaris, native to Southeast Europe.",
