	{
		title = "Viola (plant)",
		category = "Plant",
		fame = 3,
		emoji = "🌱",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Genus of flowering plants",
		tags = { "Eudicots", "Malpighiales" },
		aliases = { "Violets" },
		summary = "**Viola**, commonly known as the **violets**, is a [[Genus|genus]] of [[Flowering plant|flowering plants]] in the family Violaceae. It is the largest genus in the family, containing over 680 species. Most species are found in the temperate Northern Hemisphere; however, some are also found in widely divergent areas such as [[Hawaii]], [[Australasia]], and the [[Andes]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Some Viola species are [[Perennial|perennial plants]], some are [[Annual plant|annual plants]], and a few are small [[Shrub|shrubs]]. Many species, varieties and [[Cultivar|cultivars]] are grown in gardens for their ornamental flowers. In [[Horticulture|horticulture]], the term pansy is normally used for those multi-colored large-flowered cultivars which are raised annually or biennially from seed and used extensively in bedding.",
