		summary = 'Yams are [[Perennial|perennial]] herbaceous [[Vine|vines]] native to Africa, Asia, and the Americas and cultivated for the consumption of their [[Starch|starchy]] tubers in many [[Temperate climate|temperate]] and [[Tropics|tropical]] regions. The tubers themselves, also called "yams", come in a variety of forms owing to numerous [[Cultivar|cultivars]] and related species.',
