		tags = { "Geomorphology", "Aeolian landforms" },
		aliases = { "Eolian" },
		summary = "**Aeolian processes**, also spelled **eolian**, pertain to [[Wind|wind]] activity in the study of [[Geology|geology]] and [[Weather|weather]] and specifically to the wind's ability to shape the surface of the [[Earth]] (or other [[Planet|planets]]). Winds may [[Erosion|erode]], transport, and deposit materials. They are effective agents in regions with sparse [[Vegetation|vegetation]], a lack of soil moisture and a large supply of unconsolidated [[Sediment|sediments]]. Although water is a much more powerful eroding force than wind, aeolian processes are important in arid environments such as [[Desert|deserts]].",
