		tags = { "Chemical compounds", "Salts" },
		summary = "**Calcium chloride** is an [[Inorganic compound|inorganic compound]], a [[Salt (chemistry)|salt]] with the [[Chemical formula|chemical formula]] CaCl2. The compound is a white crystalline solid at room temperature, and it is highly soluble in water. The salt can be created by neutralising [[Hydrochloric acid|hydrochloric acid]] with calcium hydroxide.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Calcium chloride is commonly encountered as a hydrated solid with generic formula CaCl2*nH2O, where n = 0, 1, 2, 4, and 6. These compounds are mainly used for de-icing and dust control. Because the anhydrous salt is hygroscopic and deliquescent, it is used as a desiccant.",
