		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Interdisciplinary scientific study of cognitive processes",
		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Cognitive science** is the interdisciplinary, scientific study of the [[Mind|mind]] and its processes. It examines the nature, the tasks, and the functions of [[Cognition|cognition]] (in a broad sense). Mental faculties of concern to cognitive scientists include [[Perception|perception]], [[Memory|memory]], [[Attention|attention]], reasoning, [[Language|language]], and [[Emotion|emotion]]. To understand these faculties, cognitive scientists borrow from fields such as [[Psychology|psychology]], [[Philosophy of mind|philosophy]], [[Artificial intelligence|artificial intelligence]], [[Neuroscience|neuroscience]], [[Linguistics|linguistics]], and [[Anthropology|anthropology]]. The typical analysis of cognitive science spans many levels of organization, from learning and decision-making to logic and planning; from [[Neuron|neural]] circuitry to modular brain organization.",
