		emoji = "🔬",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Organic compound (H3C–CH3)",
		tags = { "Chemical compounds", "Hydrocarbons" },
		summary = "**Ethane** is a naturally occurring [[Organic compound|organic]] [[Chemical compound|chemical compound]] with the [[Chemical formula|chemical formula]] C2H6. At [[Standard temperature and pressure|standard temperature and pressure]], ethane is a colorless, odorless [[Gas|gas]]. Like many [[Hydrocarbon|hydrocarbons]], ethane is isolated on an industrial scale from [[Natural gas|natural gas]] and as a [[Petrochemical|petrochemical]] by-product of [[Oil refinery|petroleum refining]]. Its chief use is as [[Raw material|feedstock]] for [[Ethylene|ethylene]] production. The ethyl group is formally, although rarely practically, derived from ethane.",
