		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "**Evolutionary biology** is a subfield of [[Biology|biology]] that analyzes the four mechanisms of [[Evolution|evolution]]: [[Evolution|natural selection]], [[Mutation|mutation]], [[Genetic drift|genetic drift]], and gene flow. Natural selection was independently discovered as the engine of evolution by [[Charles Darwin]] and [[Alfred Russel Wallace]], based on patterns in the geographic distribution of species. [[Gregor Mendel]] discovered the laws of [[Heredity|heredity]]. R. A. Fisher unified Darwin and Mendel in the [[Modern synthesis (20th century)|modern synthesis]].",
