		summary = "An **extinction event** (also known as a **mass extinction** or **biotic crisis**) is a widespread and rapid decrease in the [[Biodiversity|biodiversity]] on [[Earth]]. Such an event is identified by a sharp fall in the diversity and abundance of [[Multicellular organism|multicellular organisms]]. It occurs when the rate of [[Extinction|extinction]] increases with respect to the background extinction rate and the rate of [[Speciation|speciation]].",
