		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🪨",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Group of rock-forming minerals",
		tags = { "Geology", "Mineralogy" },
		summary = "**Feldspar** is a group of rock-forming aluminium tectosilicate minerals, also containing other [[Ion|cations]] such as sodium, calcium, potassium, or barium. The most common members of the feldspar group are the plagioclase (sodium-calcium) feldspars and the alkali (potassium-sodium) feldspars. Feldspars make up about 60% of the [[Earth's crust]] and 41% of the Earth's [[Continental crust|continental crust]] by weight.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Feldspars [[Crystal|crystallize]] from [[Magma|magma]] as both intrusive and extrusive igneous rocks and are also present in many types of [[Metamorphic rock|metamorphic rock]]. Rock formed almost entirely of calcic plagioclase feldspar is known as anorthosite. Feldspars are also found in many types of [[Sedimentary rock|sedimentary rocks]].",
