		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Mathematical concept applicable to physics",
		tags = { "Physics", "Basics" },
		summary = "**Flux** describes any effect that appears to pass or travel (whether it actually moves or not) through a surface or substance. Flux is a concept in [[Applied mathematics|applied mathematics]] and [[Vector calculus|vector calculus]] which has many applications in [[Physics|physics]]. For transport phenomena, flux is a [[Euclidean vector|vector]] quantity, describing the magnitude and direction of the flow of a substance or property. In [[Vector calculus|vector calculus]], flux is a [[Scalar (physics)|scalar]] quantity, defined as the surface integral of the perpendicular component of a [[Vector field|vector field]] over a surface.",
