		summary = "A **gemstone** (also called a **fine gem**, **jewel**, **precious stone**, **semiprecious stone**, or simply **gem**) is a piece of [[Mineral|mineral]] [[Crystal|crystal]] which, when cut or polished, is used to make [[Jewellery|jewelry]] or other adornments. Certain [[Rock (geology)|rocks]] (such as lapis lazuli, opal, and obsidian) and occasionally [[Organic chemistry|organic]] materials that are not minerals (such as [[Amber|amber]], jet, and [[Pearl|pearl]]) may also be used for jewelry and are therefore often considered to be gemstones as well. Most gemstones are hard, but some softer minerals such as brazilianite may be used in jewelry because of their color, [[Lustre (mineralogy)|luster]], or other physical properties that have aesthetic value.",
