		summary = "A **hill** is a [[Landform|landform]] that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as [[Mountain|mountains]]. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms.",
