		tags = { "Chemical compounds", "Inorganic compounds" },
		summary = "**Ice** is [[Water|water]] that is [[Freezing|frozen]] into a [[Solid|solid]] state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °[[Celsius|C]], 32 °[[Fahrenheit|F]], or 273.15 [[Kelvin|K]]. It occurs naturally on [[Earth]], on other planets, in [[Oort cloud]] objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a [[Mineral|mineral]]. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of [[Soil|soil]] or bubbles of [[Atmosphere of Earth|air]], it can appear transparent or a more or less [[Opacity|opaque]] bluish-white color.",
