		emoji = "🔬",
		source = "wikipedia",
		tags = { "Chemical compounds", "Carbon–oxygen bond" },
		summary = "In [[Organic chemistry|organic chemistry]], a **ketone** is an [[Organic compound|organic compound]] with the structure R\\sC(\\dO)\\sR', where R and R' can be a variety of [[Carbon|carbon]]-containing [[Substituent|substituents]]. Ketones contain a carbonyl group \\sC(\\dO)\\s (a carbon-oxygen double bond C=O). A ketone derived from an [[Alkane|alkane]] is an **alkanone**. The simplest ketone is [[Acetone|acetone]] (where R and R' are methyl), with the formula (CH3)2CO. Many ketones are of great importance in biology and industry. Examples include many [[Sugar|sugars]] (ketoses), many [[Steroid|steroids]], e.g., testosterone, and the [[Solvent|solvent]] [[Acetone|acetone]].",
