				"Overview",
				"For many systems, where T and V are the [[Kinetic energy|kinetic]] and [[Potential energy|potential]] energy of the system, respectively. The stationary action principle requires that the action functional of the system derived from L must remain at a stationary point (specifically, a maximum, minimum, or saddle point) throughout the time evolution of the system. This constraint allows the calculation of the equations of motion of the system using Lagrange's equations.",
