		summary = "**Melting**, or fusion, is a physical process that results in the [[Phase transition|phase transition]] of a [[Substance (chemistry)|substance]] from a [[Solid|solid]] to a [[Liquid|liquid]]. This occurs when the [[Internal energy|internal energy]] of the solid increases, typically by the application of [[Heat|heat]] or [[Pressure|pressure]], which increases the substance's [[Temperature|temperature]] to the [[Melting point|melting point]]. At the melting point, the ordering of [[Ion|ions]] or [[Molecule|molecules]] in the solid breaks down to a less ordered state, and the solid melts to become a liquid.",
