		summary = '**Micas** are a group of [[Silicate|silicate]] [[Mineral|minerals]] whose outstanding physical characteristic is that individual mica [[Crystal|crystals]] can easily be split into fragile elastic plates. This characteristic is described as perfect basal cleavage. Mica is common in [[Igneous rock|igneous]] and [[Metamorphic rock|metamorphic rock]] and is occasionally found as small flakes in [[Sedimentary rock|sedimentary rock]]. It is particularly prominent in many [[Granite|granites]], pegmatites, and [[Schist|schists]], and "books" (large individual crystals) of mica several feet across have been found in some pegmatites.',
