		tags = { "More articles" },
		summary = "In [[Biology|biology]], **morphology** is the study of the form and structure of [[Organism|organisms]] and their specific structural features.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"This includes aspects of the outward appearance (shape, structure, color, pattern, size), as well as the form and structure of internal parts like bones and organs, i.e., [[Anatomy|anatomy]]. This is in contrast to [[Physiology|physiology]], which deals primarily with function. Morphology is a branch of life science dealing with the study of the overall structure of an [[Organism|organism]] or [[Taxon|taxon]] and its component parts.",
