		description = "Organic compounds that contain sulfur",
		tags = { "Chemical compounds", "Organic compounds" },
		aliases = { "Organosulfur compounds" },
		summary = "**Organosulfur chemistry** is the study of the properties and synthesis of **organosulfur compounds**, which are [[Organic compound|organic compounds]] that contain [[Sulfur|sulfur]]. They are often associated with foul odors, but many of the sweetest compounds known are organosulfur derivatives, e.g., saccharin. Nature abounds with organosulfur compounds—sulfur is vital for life. Fossil fuels, [[Coal|coal]], [[Petroleum|petroleum]], and [[Natural gas|natural gas]], which are derived from ancient organisms, necessarily contain organosulfur compounds, the removal of which is a major focus of oil refineries.",
