		tags = { "Chemical compounds", "Salts" },
		summary = "**Potassium nitrate** is a [[Chemical compound|chemical compound]] with a sharp, salty, bitter taste and the [[Chemical formula|chemical formula]] KNO3. It is a [[Potassium|potassium]] [[Salt (chemistry)|salt]] of [[Nitric acid|nitric acid]]. This salt consists of potassium cations K+ and [[Nitrate|nitrate]] anions NO3−, and is therefore an alkali metal nitrate. It occurs in nature as a mineral, nitre (or niter in the United States). It is a source of [[Nitrogen|nitrogen]], and nitrogen was named after niter. Potassium nitrate is one of several nitrogen-containing compounds collectively referred to as **saltpetre** (or **saltpeter** in [[American English]]).",
