		emoji = "🔬",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Phylum of single-celled organisms",
		tags = { "Organisms", "Other eukaryotes" },
		aliases = { "Radiozoa", "Radiolarians" },
		summary = "The **Radiolaria**, also called **Radiozoa** and informally called **radiolarians**, are unicellular eukaryotes of diameter 0.1–0.2 mm that produce intricate [[Mineral|mineral]] [[Skeleton|skeletons]], typically with a central capsule dividing the [[Cell (biology)|cell]] into the inner and outer portions of endoplasm and ectoplasm. The elaborate mineral skeleton is usually made of [[Silicon dioxide|silica]]. They are found as [[Zooplankton|zooplankton]] throughout the global ocean. As zooplankton, radiolarians are primarily [[Heterotroph|heterotrophic]], but many have photosynthetic [[Endosymbiont|endosymbionts]] and are, therefore, considered mixotrophs. The skeletal remains of some types of radiolarians make up a large part of the cover of the ocean floor as siliceous ooze.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
