		summary = "**Rapids** are sections of a river where the river bed has a relatively steep gradient, causing an increase in water [[Velocity|velocity]] and [[Turbulence|turbulence]]. Flow, gradient, constriction, and obstacles are four factors that are needed for a rapid to be created.",
