		tags = { "Zoology", "Ethology" },
		aliases = { "Scavengers" },
		summary = "**Scavengers** are animals that feed on dead and decaying [[Organic matter|organic matter]]. However, the term is also used to describe animals that feed on rotting plant matter or refuse.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Vultures and burying beetles are examples of scavengers that feed on carrion, pink bud moth and stag beetle larvae are examples of scavengers that feed on rotting plant matter, and raccoons and squirrels are examples of scavengers that feed on refuse. Carrion-eating scavengers are called necrophages. Scavengers play an important role in [[Ecosystem|ecosystems]] by preventing the accumulation of decaying matter and helping to recycle nutrients. [[Detritivore|Detritivores]] and [[Decomposer|decomposers]] complete this process by consuming the remains left by scavengers.",
