		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Ecoregion of plain grasslands without trees",
		tags = { "Biomes", "Grasslands" },
		summary = "In [[Physical geography|physical geography]], a **steppe** is an [[Ecoregion|ecoregion]] characterized by [[Grassland|grassland]] [[Plain|plains]] without closed [[Forest|forests]] except near rivers and lakes.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"the montane grasslands and shrublands biome the tropical and subtropical grasslands, savannas, and shrublands biome the temperate grasslands, savannas, and shrublands biome A steppe is usually covered with [[Poaceae|grass]] and [[Shrub|shrubs]], depending on the [[Season|season]] and [[Latitude|latitude]]. The term steppe climate denotes a [[Semi-arid climate|semi-arid climate]], which is too dry to support a [[Forest|forest]], but not dry enough to be a [[Desert|desert]]. Steppes are characterized by a semi-arid or [[Continental climate|continental]] climate. Temperature extremes can be recorded in the summer of up to 45 °C and in winter of down to -55 °C. Besides this major seasonal difference, fluctuations between day and night are also significant: in both the highlands of [[Mongolia]] and northern [[Nevada]], 30 °C can be reached during the day with sub-freezing readings at night.",
