		tags = { "Chemical compounds", "Organic compounds" },
		aliases = { "Thiol derivative" },
		summary = "In [[Organic chemistry|organic chemistry]], a **thiol** or **thiol derivative** is any organosulfur compound of the form R\\sSH, where R represents an alkyl or other organic [[Substituent|substituent]]. The \\sSH [[Functional group|functional group]] itself is referred to as either a **thiol group** or a **sulfhydryl group**, or a **sulfanyl group**.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Many thiols have strong odors resembling that of [[Garlic|garlic]], [[Cabbage|cabbage]] or rotten eggs. Thiols are used as odorants to assist in the detection of [[Natural gas|natural gas]] (which in pure form is odorless). The smell of natural gas is due to the addition of thiol.",
