		description = "One of two foundational theories of quantum chemistry",
		tags = { "Chemistry", "Chemical bonds" },
		aliases = { "Valence bond (VB) theory" },
		summary = "In [[Chemistry|chemistry]], **valence bond (VB) theory** is one of the two basic theories, along with [[Molecular orbital theory|molecular orbital (MO) theory]], that were developed to use the methods of [[Quantum mechanics|quantum mechanics]] to describe [[Chemical bond|chemical bonding]]. It focuses on how the [[Atomic orbital|atomic orbitals]] of the dissociated atoms combine to give individual chemical bonds when a molecule is formed. In contrast, [[Molecular orbital theory|molecular orbital theory]] has orbitals that cover the whole molecule.",
	},
	{
		title = "Valley",
		category = "Science",
