		emoji = "🔬",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "SI derived unit of power",
		tags = { "Mechanics", "Energy, power, force and pressure" },
		summary = "The **watt** (symbol: **W**) is the unit of [[Power (physics)|power]] or radiant flux in the [[International System of Units]] (SI), equal to 1 [[Joule|joule]] per [[Second|second]] or 1 kg⋅m2⋅s−3. It is used to quantify the rate of [[Work (physics)|energy transfer]]. The watt is named in honor of [[James Watt]] (1736–1819), an 18th-century Scottish [[Invention|inventor]], mechanical engineer, and [[Chemist|chemist]] who in 1776 improved the Newcomen engine with his own steam engine, which became fundamental for the [[Industrial Revolution]].",
