		tags = { "Physics", "Basics" },
		aliases = { "Weak force", "Weak nuclear force" },
		summary = "In [[Nuclear physics|nuclear physics]] and [[Particle physics|particle physics]], the **weak interaction**, **weak force** or **weak nuclear force**, is one of the four known [[Fundamental interaction|fundamental interactions]], with the others being [[Electromagnetism|electromagnetism]], the [[Strong interaction|strong interaction]], and [[Gravity|gravitation]]. It is the mechanism of interaction between subatomic particles that is responsible for the radioactive [[Beta decay|beta decay]] of atoms: The weak interaction participates in [[Nuclear fission|nuclear fission]] and [[Nuclear fusion|nuclear fusion]]. The theory describing its behaviour and effects is sometimes called **quantum flavordynamics** (**QFD**); however, the term QFD is rarely used, because the weak force is better understood by electroweak theory (EWT).",
