		title = "Arcturus",
		category = "Space",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "⭐",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Brightest star in the constellation Boötes",
		tags = { "Astronomical objects", "Notable stars" },
		summary = "**Arcturus** is a [[Red giant|red giant]] star in the [[Northern celestial hemisphere|northern]] [[Constellation|constellation]] of Boötes, and the brightest star in the constellation. It has the [[Bayer designation]] ** Boötis**, which is [[Latinisation of names|Latinized]] to **Alpha Boötis** and abbreviated **Alpha Boo** or ** Boo**. With an apparent visual magnitude of −0.05, it is the fourth-brightest star in the [[Night sky|night sky]] and the brightest in the [[Northern celestial hemisphere|northern celestial hemisphere]]. Arcturus forms one corner of the Spring Triangle [[Asterism (astronomy)|asterism]].",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Located relatively close at 36.7 [[Light-year|light-years]] from the [[Sun]], Arcturus is a [[Red giant|red giant]] of [[Stellar classification|spectral type]] K1.5III—an aging star around 7.1 billion years old that has used up its [[Stellar core|core]] [[Hydrogen|hydrogen]] and [[Stellar evolution|evolved]] off the [[Main sequence|main sequence]]. It is about the same mass [[Solar mass|as the Sun]], but has expanded to 25 times its size (around 35 million kilometers) and is around 170 times as luminous.",
