	{
		title = "Atmosphere",
		category = "Space",
		fame = 1,
		emoji = "💨",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Layer of gases surrounding an astronomical body held by gravity",
		tags = { "Astronomy", "Planetary science" },
		summary = "An **atmosphere** is a layer of [[Gas|gases]] that envelop an [[Astronomical object|astronomical object]], held in place by the [[Gravity|gravity]] of the object. An object acquires most of its atmosphere during its primordial epoch, either by [[Accretion (astrophysics)|accretion]] of matter or by outgassing of [[Volatile (astrogeology)|volatiles]]. The chemical interaction of the atmosphere with the solid surface can change its fundamental composition, as can photochemical interaction with the Sun. A planet retains an atmosphere for longer durations when the [[Gravity|gravity]] is high and the [[Temperature|temperature]] is low. The [[Solar wind|solar wind]] works to strip away a planet's outer atmosphere, although this process is slowed by a [[Magnetosphere|magnetosphere]]. The further a body is from the Sun, the lower the rate of atmospheric stripping.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Aside from [[Mercury (planet)|Mercury]], all [[Solar System]] planets have substantial atmospheres, as does the [[Dwarf planet|dwarf planet]] [[Pluto]] and the moon [[Titan (moon)|Titan]]. The high gravity and low temperature of [[Jupiter]] and the other [[Gas giant|gas giant]] planets allow them to retain massive atmospheres of mostly hydrogen and helium. Lower mass [[Terrestrial planet|terrestrial planets]] orbit closer to the Sun, and so mainly retain higher molar mass atmospheres made of carbon, nitrogen, and oxygen, with trace amounts of inert gas. Atmospheres have been detected around [[Exoplanet|exoplanets]] such as HD 209458 b and Kepler-7b. A stellar atmosphere is the outer region of a star, which includes the layers above the [[Opacity|opaque]] [[Photosphere|photosphere]]; stars of low temperature might have outer atmospheres containing compound [[Molecule|molecules]]. Other objects with atmospheres are [[Brown dwarf|brown dwarfs]] and active [[Comet|comets]].",
			},
		},
	},
	{
		title = "Barred spiral galaxy",
