	{
		title = "Centaurus",
		category = "Space",
		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🪐",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Constellation in the southern celestial hemisphere",
		tags = { "Celestial mechanics and astrometry", "Constellations" },
		summary = "**Centaurus** is a bright constellation in the southern sky. One of the largest constellations, Centaurus was included among the 48 [[Constellation|constellations]] listed by the 2nd-century astronomer [[Ptolemy]], and it remains one of the 88 modern constellations. In [[Greek mythology]], Centaurus represents a [[Centaur|centaur]]; a creature that is half human, half horse (another constellation named after a centaur is one from the [[Zodiac|zodiac]]: Sagittarius). Notable stars include [[Alpha Centauri]], the nearest star system to the [[Solar System]], its neighbour in the sky Beta Centauri, and HR 5171, one of the largest stars yet discovered.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"The constellation also contains [[Omega Centauri]], the brightest [[Globular cluster|globular cluster]] as visible from Earth and the largest identified in the Milky Way, possibly a remnant of a dwarf galaxy.",
			},
