		fame = 2,
		emoji = "🌌",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Small galaxy composed of up to several billion stars",
		tags = { "Astronomy", "Galaxy morphological classification" },
		summary = "A **dwarf galaxy** is a small [[Galaxy|galaxy]] composed of about 1,000 up to several billion [[Star|stars]], as compared to the [[Milky Way]]'s 100–400 billion stars. The [[Large Magellanic Cloud]], which closely orbits the Milky Way and contains over 30 billion stars, is sometimes classified as a dwarf galaxy; others consider it a full-fledged galaxy. Dwarf galaxies' formation and activity are thought to be heavily influenced by interactions with larger galaxies. Astronomers identify numerous types of dwarf galaxies, based on their shape and composition.",
