		tags = { "Astronomical objects", "Other notable objects" },
		summary = "**Omega Centauri** is a [[Globular cluster|globular cluster]] in the [[Constellation|constellation]] of [[Centaurus]] that was first identified as a non-stellar object by [[Edmond Halley]] in 1677. Located at a distance of 17090 light-years, it is the largest known globular cluster in the [[Milky Way]] at a diameter of roughly 150 light-years. It is estimated to contain approximately 10 million stars, with a total mass of 4 million [[Solar mass|solar masses]], making it the most massive known globular cluster in the Milky Way.",
