		tags = { "Astronomical objects", "Notable stars" },
		summary = "**Polaris** is a yellow supergiant [[Star|star]] in the northern circumpolar constellation of [[Ursa Minor]]. It is designated ** Ursae Minoris** ([[Latinisation of names|Latinized]] to Alpha Ursae Minoris) and is commonly called the **North Star**. The position of the star lies less than 1° away from the north celestial pole, making it the current northern pole star. The stable position of the star in the [[Northern celestial hemisphere|Northern Sky]] makes it useful for [[Celestial navigation|navigation]].",
