		tags = { "Astronomical objects", "Notable stars" },
		summary = "**Procyon** is the brightest [[Star|star]] in the [[Constellation|constellation]] of Canis Minor and usually the eighth-brightest star in the [[Night sky|night sky]], with an apparent visual magnitude of 0.34. It has the [[Bayer designation]] ** Canis Minoris**, which is [[Latinisation of names|Latinized]] to **Alpha Canis Minoris**, and abbreviated ** CMi** or **Alpha CMi**, respectively. As determined by the [[European Space Agency]] Hipparcos astrometry satellite, this system lies at a distance of just 11.46 light-years, and is therefore one of Earth's nearest stellar neighbors.",
