		tags = { "Astronomical objects", "Notable stars" },
		summary = "**Rigel** is a blue [[Supergiant|supergiant]] star in the equatorial [[Constellation|constellation]] of [[Orion (constellation)|Orion]]. It has the [[Bayer designation]] ** Orionis**, which is [[Latinisation of names|Latinized]] to **Beta Orionis** and abbreviated **Beta Ori** or ** Ori**. This system is located at a distance of approximately 850 light-years.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"A star of [[Stellar classification|spectral type]] B8Ia, Rigel is calculated to be anywhere from 61,500 to 363,000 times as luminous as the Sun, and 18 to 24 times [[Solar mass|as massive]], depending on the method and assumptions used. Its radius is more than seventy times that of the Sun, and its surface temperature is 12,100 K. Due to its [[Stellar wind|stellar wind]], Rigel's mass-loss is estimated to be ten million times that of the Sun. With an estimated age of seven to nine million years, Rigel has exhausted its core hydrogen fuel, expanded, and cooled to become a supergiant. Rigel varies slightly in brightness, its [[Apparent magnitude|apparent magnitude]] ranging from 0.05 to 0.18. It is classified as an Alpha Cygni variable due to the amplitude and periodicity of its brightness variation, as well as its spectral type. Its [[Variable star|intrinsic variability]] is caused by pulsations in its unstable atmosphere.",
