		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Magnetic field generated inside a star",
		tags = { "Astronomy", "Stellar astronomy" },
		summary = "A **stellar magnetic field** is a [[Magnetic field|magnetic field]] generated by the motion of conductive [[Plasma (physics)|plasma]] inside a [[Star|star]]. This motion is created through [[Convection|convection]], which is a form of energy transport involving the physical movement of material. A localized [[Magnetic field|magnetic field]] exerts a force on the plasma, effectively increasing the pressure without a comparable gain in density. As a result, the magnetized region rises relative to the remainder of the plasma, until it reaches the star's [[Photosphere|photosphere]]. This creates starspots on the surface, and the related phenomenon of coronal loops.",
