		aliases = { "SMBH", "SBH" },
		summary = "A **supermassive black hole** (**SMBH** or sometimes **SBH**) is the largest type of [[Black hole|black hole]], with its [[Mass|mass]] being on the order of hundreds of thousands, or millions to billions, of times the mass of the [[Sun]]. Black holes are a class of [[Astronomical object|astronomical objects]] that have undergone [[Gravitational collapse|gravitational collapse]], leaving behind spheroidal regions of space that nothing, not even [[Light|light]], can escape. Observational evidence indicates that almost every large [[Galaxy|galaxy]] has a supermassive black hole at its center. For example, the [[Milky Way]] galaxy has a [[Galactic Center|supermassive black hole at its center]], corresponding to the radio source [[Sagittarius A*]].",
