		tags = { "Industry", "Food, water and health" },
		summary = '**Soap** is a [[Salt (chemistry)|salt]] of a [[Fatty acid|fatty acid]] (sometimes other carboxylic acids) used for cleaning and lubricating products as well as other applications. In a domestic setting, soaps, specifically "toilet soaps", are [[Surfactant|surfactants]] usually used for washing, bathing, and other types of housekeeping. In industrial settings, soaps are used as thickeners, components of some lubricants, emulsifiers, and [[Catalysis|catalysts]].',
