		fame = 3,
		emoji = "💻",
		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Computer program for working with tabular data",
		tags = { "Computing and information technology", "Computer software" },
		summary = "A **spreadsheet** is a computer application for [[Computation|computation]], organization, analysis and [[Data storage|storage]] of [[Data|data]] in tabular form. Spreadsheets were developed as computerized analogs of paper accounting worksheets. The program operates on data entered in cells of a table. Each cell may contain either numeric or text data, or the results of [[Formula|formulas]] that automatically calculate and display a value based on the contents of other cells. The term spreadsheet may also refer to one such electronic document.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				'In modern spreadsheet applications, several spreadsheets, often known as "**worksheets**" or simply "sheets", are gathered together to form a "**workbook**". A workbook is physically represented by a file containing all the data for the book, the sheets, and the cells with the sheets. Worksheets are normally represented by tabs that flip between pages, each one containing one of the sheets, although Numbers changes this model significantly. Cells in a multi-sheet book add the sheet name to their reference, for instance, "Sheet 1!C10". Some systems extend this syntax to allow cell references to different workbooks. Spreadsheet users can adjust any stored value and observe the effects on calculated values. This makes the spreadsheet useful for "what-if" analysis since many cases can be rapidly investigated without manual recalculation.',
			},
