		tags = { "Industry", "Basics" },
		aliases = { "Standardisation" },
		summary = "**Standardization** ([[American English]]) or **standardisation** ([[British English]]) is the process of implementing and developing technical standards based on the consensus of different parties that may include firms, users, interest groups, standards organizations and governments. Standardization can help maximize compatibility, interoperability, [[Safety|safety]], repeatability, efficiency, and quality. It can also facilitate a normalization of formerly custom processes.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"In [[Social science|social sciences]], including [[Economics|economics]], the idea of standardization is close to the solution for a coordination problem, a situation in which all parties can realize mutual gains, but only by making mutually consistent decisions. Divergent national standards impose costs on consumers and can be a form of non-tariff trade barrier.",
