		tags = { "Computing and information technology", "Computer software" },
		summary = "A **word processor** (**WP**) is a device or computer program that provides for input, editing, formatting, and output of text, often with some additional features.",
		sections = {
			{
				"Overview",
				"Early word processors were stand-alone devices dedicated to the function, but current word processors are primarily word processor programs running on general purpose computers, including smartphones, tablets, laptops, and desktop computers, with dedicated hardware word processors being confined to a small niche market. The functions of a word processor program are typically between those of a simple text editor and a desktop publishing program. Many word processing programs have gained advanced features over time providing similar functionality to desktop publishing programs. Common word processor programs include LibreOffice Writer, Google Docs, and Microsoft Word.",
