		source = "wikipedia",
		description = "Goods or produce transported",
		tags = { "Transportation", "Basics" },
		aliases = { "Freight" },
		summary = "In [[Transport|transportation]], **cargo** refers to [[Goods|goods]] transported by [[Land transport|land]], water, or air, while **freight** refers to its conveyance. In [[Economics|economics]], freight refers to goods transported at a freight rate for [[Commerce|commercial]] gain. The term cargo is also used in the case of goods in the cold-chain, because the perishable inventory is always in transit towards a final end-use, even when it is held in [[Refrigeration|cold storage]] or other similar climate-controlled facilities, including warehouses.",
